ugh to outweigh the bubble it removes, so its CPI win must be measured against the added MEM-to-EX timing cost.\nhyp-20260710-001-r6s0\tShare the combinational divide and remainder datapath\tbroken\t0\t0\t0\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r6s0 (broken, n/a): In Yosys `always_comb`, a module-scoped integer used as a restoring-divider loop iterator is a synthesizable signal, so paths that skip the loop (such as divide-by-zero) must still assign it or the tool infers a latch; keep loop indices local/automatic or fully assigned.\nhyp-20260710-001-r7s0\tRemove redundant MEM/WB forwarding leg\timprovement\t480.9\t21.33\t208.72\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r7s0 (improvement, +21.33%): Removing a redundant MEM/WB forwarding compare and mux improved CoreMark because EX1's write-first register-file reread already exposes WB data, so forwarding should retain only younger values unavailable at the read ports while preserving EX2-over-EX/MEM priority.\nhyp-20260710-001-r8s0\tQualify load-use hazard source comparisons\tbroken\t0\t0\t0\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r8s0 (broken, n/a): Source-use bits for load-use interlocks must remain hazard-only; zeroing unused `rs1`/`rs2` addresses or data in RVFI changes the cosim-visible raw instruction-field trace and breaks selftest.\nhyp-20260710-001-r9s0\tOpcode-qualified load-use interlock\tbroken\t0\t0\t0\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r9s0 (broken, n/a): Opcode-qualified load-use comparisons in the hazard unit still failed the RVFI register check, so removing bubbles requires proving the raw-instruction source map remains aligned with valid, held, and redirected ID/EX entries across the full instruction stream.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
