{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -c 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260710-001-r7s0\\\") | {id,title,motivation,hypothesis,changes,fitness,delta_pct,fmax_mhz,lut4,implementation_notes}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-001-r7s0\",\"title\":\"Remove redundant MEM/WB forwarding leg\",\"motivation\":\"The retimed core already captures forwarded operands in EX1, but its\\nforwarding network still performs a third age comparison and selects a\\nMEM/WB value.  The register file has an explicit write-first WB bypass, and\\nEX1 re-reads the held instruction's registers, so this MEM/WB leg duplicates\\na value that is already available at the register-file read ports.  Removing\\nthe duplicate compare and mux should reduce EX1 capture delay and routing\\nwithout changing the arithmetic or memory pipeline.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The retimed core already captures forwarded operands in EX1, but its\\nforwarding network still performs a third age comparison and selects a\\nMEM/WB value.  The register file has an explicit write-first WB bypass, and\\nEX1 re-reads the held instruction's registers, so this MEM/WB leg duplicates\\na value that is already available at the register-file read ports.  Removing\\nthe duplicate compare and mux should reduce EX1 capture delay and routing\\nwithout changing the arithmetic or memory pipeline.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Eliminate the MEM/WB source from the EX1 forwarding priority, retaining only\\nthe freshest EX2 result, the EX/MEM result or load value, and the\\nwrite-first register-file read as the fallback.  Simplify the forwarding\\ninterfaces and wiring so the WB value is supplied solely by the existing\\nregister-file bypass.  Because WB writes are visible combinationally and\\nEX1 re-reads operands when an instruction is held, dependent ALU, load-use,\\nbus-stall, redirect, RVFI, and x0 behavior should remain unchanged while\\nthe operand-capture path becomes smaller and faster.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":2,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Remove the MEM/WB equality comparison and forwarding selection while preserving EX2-over-EX/MEM age priority and x0 suppression.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Simplify the EX1 operand mux inputs to use EX2, EX/MEM, or the write-first register-file read, with no functional change to load forwarding or stalls.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Update forwarding wiring to drop the redundant MEM/WB forwarding source while retaining the existing WB write-first regfile path and top-level RVFI contract.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Remove the MEM/WB equality comparison and forwarding selection while preserving EX2-over-EX/MEM age priority and x0 suppression.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Simplify the EX1 operand mux inputs to use EX2, EX/MEM, or the write-first register-file read, with no functional change to load forwarding or stalls.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Update forwarding wiring to drop the redundant MEM/WB forwarding source while retaining the existing WB write-first regfile path and top-level RVFI contract.\"}],\"fitness\":480.9,\"delta_pct\":21.33,\"fmax_mhz\":208.72,\"lut4\":10135,\"implementation_notes\":\"\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
