{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.id == \\\"hyp-20260710-001-r6s0\\\" or .id == \\\"hyp-20260710-001-r7s0\\\" or .id == \\\"hyp-20260710-001-r3s0\\\") | \\\"ID: \\\\(.id)\\\\nTITLE: \\\\(.title)\\\\nHYPOTHESIS:\\\\n\\\\(.hypothesis.hypothesis // .hypothesis)\\\\nCHANGES:\\\\n\\\\(.changes // [])\\\\nOUTCOME: \\\\(.outcome) \\\\(.delta_pct // \\\"\\\")\\\\nERROR: \\\\(.error // \\\"\\\")\\\\nNOTES:\\\\n\\\\(.implementation_notes // \\\"\\\")\\\\n---\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"ID: hyp-20260710-001-r3s0\nTITLE: Share a native-width RV32M multiplier\nHYPOTHESIS:\nReplace the parallel signed-signed, unsigned-unsigned, and signed-unsigned\nproducts with one native 32x32 unsigned product. Use sign-dependent high\nhalf correction terms to implement MULH and MULHSU exactly, while taking\nthe unchanged low half for MUL and the unsigned high half for MULHU. Keep\nthe existing one-cycle EX interface, divider behavior, RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\nsubstitutions, and RVFI timing unchanged. This should remove redundant\nmultiplier hardware and routing pressure without the critical-path penalty\nof the prior 33x33 implementation, improving Fmax and/or fitting margin\nwhile preserving CoreMark IPC.\n\nCHANGES:\n[{\"file\":\"rtl/alu.sv\",\"description\":\"Use one native-width unsigned 32x32 product and sign-correction arithmetic for exact MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU results; retain ALTOPS and divider semantics.\"}]\nOUTCOME: improvement 2.18\nERROR: \nNOTES:\n\n---\nID: hyp-20260710-001-r6s0\nTITLE: Share the combinational divide and remainder datapath\nHYPOTHESIS:\nRewrite the real RV32M division logic around one combinational unsigned\nmagnitude divider that produces both quotient and remainder, then apply\noperand-sign correction and the RISC-V divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 rules\nto select DIV, DIVU, REM, or REMU. Keep the ALTOPS formal substitutions\nunchanged and preserve combinational latency, so dependent instructions,\nRVFI ordering, and dmem-stall behavior do not acquire new bubbles. Sharing\nthe expensive divide work should reduce LUT/routing load and improve Fmax\nwithout the throughput loss of a globally held iterative unit.\n\nCHANGES:\n[{\"file\":\"rtl/alu.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace the independent real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operators with one shared quotient-and-remainder datapath, including exact RV32M signedness, zero-divisor, and overflow handling while retaining the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS branch.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_alu.py\",\"description\":\"Extend ALU coverage for shared-divider signed and unsigned quotient/remainder pairs, divide-by-zero, INT_MIN/-1 overflow, and back-to-back operations to guard the refactor.\"}]\nOUTCOME: broken \nERROR: build_failed: yosys synth: ERROR: Latch inferred for signal `\\alu.\\div_bit' from always_comb process `\\alu.$proc$cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv:61$9'.\nNOTES:\n\n---\nID: hyp-20260710-001-r7s0\nTITLE: Remove redundant MEM/WB forwarding leg\nHYPOTHESIS:\nEliminate the MEM/WB source from the EX1 forwarding priority, retaining only\nthe freshest EX2 result, the EX/MEM result or load value, and the\nwrite-first register-file read as the fallback.  Simplify the forwarding\ninterfaces and wiring so the WB value is supplied solely by the existing\nregister-file bypass.  Because WB writes are visible combinationally and\nEX1 re-reads operands when an instruction is held, dependent ALU, load-use,\nbus-stall, redirect, RVFI, and x0 behavior should remain unchanged while\nthe operand-capture path becomes smaller and faster.\n\nCHANGES:\n[{\"file\":\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Remove the MEM/WB equality comparison and forwarding selection while preserving EX2-over-EX/MEM age priority and x0 suppression.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Simplify the EX1 operand mux inputs to use EX2, EX/MEM, or the write-first register-file read, with no functional change to load forwarding or stalls.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Update forwarding wiring to drop the redundant MEM/WB forwarding source while retaining the existing WB write-first regfile path and top-level RVFI contract.\"}]\nOUTCOME: improvement 21.33\nERROR: \nNOTES:\n\n---\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
