{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r11s0.yaml && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r11s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-001-r11s0\ntitle: \"Share the RV32M quotient and remainder datapath\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The real ALU currently expresses DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU as separate\n  arithmetic operators, which can infer multiple large divider networks even\n  though quotient and remainder come from the same division operation. A prior\n  sharing attempt was build-broken because its combinational loop iterator\n  inferred a latch, so this is a focused repair of a potentially high-cost\n  datapath rather than a pipeline change.\nhypothesis: |\n  Implement one fully combinational unsigned magnitude divider that produces\n  both quotient and remainder, then apply operand-sign correction and the\n  specified divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 rules to select DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU.\n  Keep the one-cycle ALU interface, preserve the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n  substitutions, and use an automatic or fully assigned loop index so Yosys\n  infers no latch. Sharing the divider should reduce LUT/routing pressure and\n  improve Fmax without adding a global divide stall or changing RVFI timing.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Replace the independent real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operators with one latch-free combinational magnitude divider and exact signedness, zero-divisor, and overflow correction; retain the shared multiplier and ALTOPS branch.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Add exact vectors for quotient/remainder signed and unsigned pairs, divide-by-zero, INT_MIN/-1 overflow, sign combinations, and repeated back-to-back operations.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
