{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'\nfor line in open(p):\n    x=json.loads(line)\n    if x.get('category')=='micro_opt':\n        print(x['id'], x.get('outcome'), x.get('delta_pct'), x.get('fitness'), x.get('fmax_mhz'), x.get('title'))\nPY\nrg -n 'r7s0|r3s0|r5s1|r11s0|forward|ALU|critical|timing|fanout|adder|decode' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | tail -100\"","aggregated_output":"baseline-bench-4ddfa22 improvement 0.0 282.82 127.03 Baseline retest for cores/bench\nhyp-20260710-001-r1s0 broken None None None Zero-bubble load-use forwarding\nhyp-20260710-001-r2s0 regression -7.63 286.85 122.19 Share the RV32M multiplier datapath\nhyp-20260710-001-r3s0 improvement 2.18 317.32 135.17 Share a native-width RV32M multiplier\nhyp-20260710-001-r4s0 regression -18.78 257.74 109.79 Reuse the EX adder for control-flow targets\nhyp-20260710-001-r5s0 regression -20.38 252.64 103.34 Zero-bubble zero-wait load-use bypass\nhyp-20260710-001-r6s0 broken None None None Share the combinational divide and remainder datapath\nhyp-20260710-001-r7s0 improvement 21.33 480.9 208.72 Remove redundant MEM/WB forwarding leg\nhyp-20260710-001-r8s0 broken None None None Qualify load-use hazard source comparisons\nhyp-20260710-001-r9s0 broken None None None Opcode-qualified load-use interlock\nhyp-20260710-001-r10s0 regression -55.42 214.39 93.05 Explicit byte-lane load extraction\nhyp-20260710-001-r11s0 regression -77.6 107.72 46.75 Share the RV32M quotient and remainder datapath\n2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Zero-bubble load-use forwarding\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current five-stage pipeline unconditionally stalls one cycle for every\\nload-use dependency, even though the Tang Nano bench presents combinational\\nzero-wait read data. CoreMark has frequent load-dependent address, compare,\\nand arithmetic instructions, so this bubble directly reduces iterations per\\ncycle. The existing P&R report also shows the EX/MEM-to-EX forwarding path as\\nthe dominant timing path, making a dedicated load-data bypass a focused\\nhigh-value datapath optimization.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current five-stage pipeline unconditionally stalls one cycle for every\\nload-use dependency, even though the Tang Nano bench presents combinational\\nzero-wait read data. CoreMark has frequent load-dependent address, compare,\\nand arithmetic instructions, so this bubble directly reduces iterations per\\ncycle. The existing P&R report also shows the EX/MEM-to-EX forwarding path as\\nthe dominant timing path, making a dedicated load-data bypass a focused\\nhigh-value datapath optimization.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a dedicated EX/MEM load-data bypass from the memory stage's extracted\\nbyte/half/word value into the EX operand mux, and remove the unconditional\\nload-use bubble. When dmemReady is low, hold the dependent instruction and\\nsuppress redirects or side effects until the load completes; when it is high,\\nforward the load value directly and retire the dependent instruction without\\na bubble. This should preserve arbitrary bus-stall correctness while\\nimproving CoreMark IPC on the zero-wait FPGA path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the unconditional load-use bubble with replay-safe holding on an outstanding dmem stall, and provide control to block redirects while the dependent instruction waits.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a highest-priority EX/MEM load-result forwarding selection, with normal ALU and MEM/WB forwarding retained as fallbacks.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the already sign/zero-extended load value as a combinational forwarding source while retaining the existing 