{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r13s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r13s2\ntitle: \"Single-entry JALR target cache\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The proven static predictor removes most direct-JAL and backward-loop\n  redirects, but JALR returns still resolve in EX and pay a redirect bubble.\n  Larger dynamic predictors and RAS variants regressed this fixture because\n  IF-stage decode, table lookup, or target selection extended the fetch\n  critical path. Repeated hot return sites are a narrower opportunity.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a one-entry EX-trained indirect-target cache for JALR control transfers.\n  When a JALR resolves, capture its instruction PC and resolved target; on a\n  later fetch of the same PC, use an exact PC match to supply the saved target\n  directly, without decoding the fetched instruction, adding a target adder,\n  or maintaining history/counter state in IF. Retain the existing static\n  backward-branch/direct-JAL predictor as the fallback, carry the prediction\n  metadata through the existing pipeline, and keep EX authoritative so stale\n  entries merely cause the existing prediction-mismatch redirect. This should\n  remove recurring JALR return bubbles at much lower timing and area cost than\n  a RAS or multi-entry BTB.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add an exact-PC, one-entry indirect-target lookup that overrides only the unpredicted JALR case, while preserving the current static predictor, redirect priority, and prediction metadata behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Expose the resolved JALR instruction PC, target, and valid update event so the indirect-target entry is trained only by an older, architecturally resolved JALR.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the EX JALR training record into IF without changing the external buses, pipeline retirement boundary, or RVFI contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
