{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -c 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260710-001-r7s0\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-001-r3s0\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-001-r5s1\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r7s1\\\") | {id,title,motivation,hypothesis,changes,outcome,fitness,delta_pct,fmax_mhz,implementation_notes}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-001-r3s0\",\"title\":\"Share a native-width RV32M multiplier\",\"motivation\":\"The predictor-enhanced bench core has already recovered the important\\nCoreMark control-flow bubbles, but it uses 10554 LUT4s and its ALU still\\ninstantiates three full-width multiplier expressions for the MUL family.\\nThe previous sharing attempt used a 33x33 signed multiplier and reduced\\nFmax substantially, so the next optimization should preserve the FPGA's\\nnative 32x32 mapping rather than widen the arithmetic cone.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The predictor-enhanced bench core has already recovered the important\\nCoreMark control-flow bubbles, but it uses 10554 LUT4s and its ALU still\\ninstantiates three full-width multiplier expressions for the MUL family.\\nThe previous sharing attempt used a 33x33 signed multiplier and reduced\\nFmax substantially, so the next optimization should preserve the FPGA's\\nnative 32x32 mapping rather than widen the arithmetic cone.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Replace the parallel signed-signed, unsigned-unsigned, and signed-unsigned\\nproducts with one native 32x32 unsigned product. Use sign-dependent high\\nhalf correction terms to implement MULH and MULHSU exactly, while taking\\nthe unchanged low half for MUL and the unsigned high half for MULHU. Keep\\nthe existing one-cycle EX interface, divider behavior, RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\\nsubstitutions, and RVFI timing unchanged. This should remove redundant\\nmultiplier hardware and routing pressure without the critical-path penalty\\nof the prior 33x33 implementation, improving Fmax and/or fitting margin\\nwhile preserving CoreMark IPC.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":3,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/alu.sv\",\"description\":\"Use one native-width unsigned 32x32 product and sign-correction arithmetic for exact MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU results; retain ALTOPS and divider semantics.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/alu.sv\",\"description\":\"Use one native-width unsigned 32x32 product and sign-correction arithmetic for exact MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU results; retain ALTOPS and divider semantics.\"}],\"outcome\":\"improvement\",\"fitness\":317.32,\"delta_pct\":2.18,\"fmax_mhz\":135.17,\"implementation_notes\":\"\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-001-r7s0\",\"title\":\"Remove redundant MEM/WB forwarding leg\",\"motivation\":\"The retimed core already captures forwarded operands in EX1, but its\\nforwarding network still performs a third age comparison and selects a\\nMEM/WB value.  The register file has an explicit write-first WB bypass, and\\nEX1 re-reads the held instruction's registers, so this MEM/WB leg duplicates\\na value that is already available at the register-file read ports.  Removing\\nthe duplicate compare and mux should reduce EX1 capture delay and routing\\nwithout changing the arithmetic or memory pipeline.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The retimed core already captures forwarded operands in EX1, but its\\nforwarding network still performs a third age comparison and selects a\\nMEM/WB value.  The register file has an explicit write-first WB bypass, and\\nEX1 re-reads the held instruction's registers, so this MEM/WB leg duplicates\\na value that is already available at the register-file read ports.  Removing\\nthe duplicate compare and mux should reduce EX1 capture delay and routing\\nwithout changing the arithmetic or memory pipeline.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Eliminate the MEM/WB source from the EX1 forwarding priority, retaining only\\nthe freshest EX2 result, the EX/MEM result or load value, and the\\nwrite-first register-file read as the fallback.  Simplify the forwarding\\ninterfaces and wiring so the WB value is supplied solely by the existing\\nregister-file bypass.  Because WB writes are visible combinationally and\\nEX1 re-reads operands when an instruction is held, dependent ALU, load-use,\\nbus-stall, redirect, RVFI, and x0 behavior should remain unchanged while\\nthe operand-capture path becomes smaller and faster.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":2,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Remove the MEM/WB equality comparison and forwarding selection while preserving EX2-over-EX/MEM age priority and x0 suppression.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Simplify the EX1 operand mux inputs to use EX2, EX/MEM, or the write-first register-file read, with no functional change to load forwarding or stalls.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Update forwarding wiring to drop the redundant MEM/WB forwarding source while retaining the existing WB write-first regfile path and top-level RVFI contract.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Remove the MEM/WB equality comparison and forwarding selection while preserving EX2-over-EX/MEM age priority and x0 suppression.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Simplify the EX1 operand mux inputs to use EX2, EX/MEM, or the write-first register-file read, with no functional change to load forwarding or stalls.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Update forwarding wiring to drop the redundant MEM/WB forwarding source while retaining the existing WB write-first regfile path and top-level RVFI contract.\"}],\"outcome\":\"improvement\",\"fitness\":480.9,\"delta_pct\":21.33,\"fmax_mhz\":208.72,\"implementation_notes\":\"\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r7s1\",\"title\":\"Elastic in-order memory backend\",\"motivation\":\"The retimed EX1/EX2 pipeline now has useful independent work available, but\\nthe current MEM control still freezes it whenever io_dmemReady is low for a\\nload or store.  The benchmark injects roughly 22% data-bus stalls, so this\\ncoupling directly reduces CoreMark iterations per cycle.  The previous store\\nbuffer attempt regressed because queue occupancy remained on the global\\ndmem-stall path; the next design should decouple waiting memory requests from\\nyounger non-memory work while retaining strict retirement order.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The retimed EX1/EX2 pipeline now has useful independent work available, but\\nthe current MEM control still freezes it whenever io_dmemReady is low for a\\nload or store.  The benchmark injects roughly 22% data-bus stalls, so this\\ncoupling directly reduces CoreMark iterations per cycle.  The previous store\\nbuffer attempt regressed because queue occupancy remained on the global\\ndmem-stall path; the next design should decouple waiting memory requests from\\nyounger non-memory work while retaining strict retirement order.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Add a small age-ordered completion queue after EX2 together with a dedicated\\nmemory-request slot.  A load or store occupies the memory slot until its\\ndmem handshake completes, while younger non-memory instructions can execute\\nand wait in the completion queue instead of freezing the whole backend.\\nBlock younger memory operations and consumers of a pending load, and apply\\nbackpressure only when the queue is full.  Retire and expose RVFI strictly\\nfrom the oldest queue entry, with queue-aware forwarding for values that are\\ncomplete but not yet retired.  This should hide a meaningful fraction of\\nrandom dmem stalls without adding logic to the IF critical path or changing\\nthe external bus and single-channel RVFI contracts.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":5,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Define the age-ordered completion-entry and pending-memory metadata needed by the elastic backend while preserving the existing RVFI payload fields.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate the memory request slot and completion queue, making the oldest entry the sole WB/RVFI retirement source without changing top-level IO.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Separate memory-request capture, dmem-ready handshake, and load-response completion so a waiting request no longer freezes unrelated EX work.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace the global memory-stall coupling with queue-full, pending-load dependency, and younger-memory ordering controls.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Add age-correct forwarding from completed-but-unretired queue entries while keeping pending-load results unavailable until the response arrives.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/wb_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Drive register writes and retirement data from the oldest completed queue entry exactly once, preserving RVFI order and memory metadata.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Define the age-ordered completion-entry and pending-memory metadata needed by the elastic backend while preserving the existing RVFI payload fields.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate the memory request slot and completion queue, making the oldest entry the sole WB/RVFI retirement source without changing top-level IO.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Separate memory-request capture, dmem-ready handshake, and load-response completion so a waiting request no longer freezes unrelated EX work.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace the global memory-stall coupling with queue-full, pending-load dependency, and younger-memory ordering controls.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Add age-correct forwarding from completed-but-unretired queue entries while keeping pending-load results unavailable until the response arrives.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/wb_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Drive register writes and retirement data from the oldest completed queue entry exactly once, preserving RVFI order and memory metadata.\"}],\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"fitness\":null,\"delta_pct\":null,\"fmax_mhz\":null,\"implementation_notes\":null}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
