{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r14s0.yaml && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r14s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-001-r14s0\ntitle: \"Register the sequential fetch PC increment\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The winning bench core already gets its large gain from EX1/EX2 retiming and\n  the lightweight static predictor.  The remaining ordinary fetch path still\n  computes a 32-bit `pc + 4` adder and feeds it through the prediction mux on\n  every non-control instruction.  This is a high-fanout, always-active piece\n  of the IF next-PC cone even when no prediction is selected.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a registered `pc_plus4` sidecar to the IF stage and use it as the\n  sequential fall-through value, while leaving backward-branch/direct-JAL\n  target arithmetic and EX-authoritative redirect recovery unchanged.  Update\n  the sidecar coherently with reset, normal sequential advance, redirect, and\n  stall; on a redirect load `redirect_target + 4`, and on a normal advance\n  derive the next sidecar from the current PC so the extra increment is not on\n  the PC selection path.  This should remove the common `pc + 4` adder from\n  the fetch critical path without changing prediction metadata, valid/flush\n  behavior, or RVFI PC fields.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add and maintain a coherent registered PC-plus-four value, use it for the non-predicted fall-through path, and preserve redirect priority, stalls, static predictions, and IF/ID metadata.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
