etto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-luna-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-001-r9s0/formal/last_run-17210.log\\nPer-check logs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-luna-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-001-r9s0/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-17210/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 9, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r9s0 (broken, n/a): Opcode-qualified load-use comparisons in the hazard unit still failed the RVFI register check, so removing bubbles requires proving the raw-instruction source map remains aligned with valid, held, and redirected ID/EX entries across the full instruction stream.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:27:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r9s1\", \"title\": \"Two-read-port operand snapshot pipeline\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current pipeline exposes four combinational register-file read ports:\\ntwo for decode and two more for EX1 to reread an instruction held in\\nID/EX.  That duplicated read topology consumes LUTs and adds fanout and\\nmuxing around the operand-forwarding boundary, which is especially costly\\nwhen the design is already close to the Tang Nano LUT budget.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current pipeline exposes four combinational register-file read ports:\\ntwo for decode and two more for EX1 to reread an instruction held in\\nID/EX.  That duplicated read topology consumes LUTs and adds fanout and\\nmuxing around the operand-forwarding boundary, which is especially costly\\nwhen the design is already close to the Tang Nano LUT budget.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Remove the dedicated EX1 register-file reread ports and make the ID/EX\\noperand snapshot authoritative.  When ID/EX is held for a load-use or\\ndmem stall, refresh only its stored rs1/rs2 values from the existing two\\ndecode read ports, including their write-first WB behavior; otherwise\\ncapture operands normally.  EX1 will still apply the existing age-ordered\\nEX2 and EX/MEM forwarding, while all source addresses and RVFI fields stay\\nunchanged.  This should reduce register-file replication and operand-path\\nfanout without adding a new critical datapath stage.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/reg_file.sv\", \"description\": \"Collapse the register file from four combinational read ports to the existing two decode ports, retaining x0 behavior and write-first WB bypassing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Refresh the held ID/EX operand snapshots from the decode read ports on every stall so delayed load-use and dmem-stall cases see newly retired register values.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the ID/EX operand snapshots as the non-forwarded EX1 inputs and remove the redundant EX1 register-file reread interface while preserving EX2-over-EX/MEM forwarding priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Reconnect the reduced register-file interface and operand path without changing the external buses, pipeline retirement boundary, or single-channel RVFI contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/reg_file.sv\", \"description\": \"Collapse the register file from four combinational read ports to the existing two decode ports, retaining x0 behavior and write-first WB bypassing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Refresh the held ID/EX operand snapshots from the decode read ports on every stall so delayed load-use and dmem-stall cases see newly retired register values.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the ID/EX operand snapshots as the non-forwarded EX1 inputs and remove the redundant EX1 register-file reread interface while preserving EX2-over-EX/MEM forwarding priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Reconnect the reduced register-file interface and operand path without changing the external buses, pipeline retirement boundary, or single-channel RVFI contract.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 207.92, \"delta_pct\": -56.76, \"vs_baseline\": -26.48, \"fmax_mhz\": 90.24, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4340155, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10561, \"ff\": 2176, \"seeds\": [90.24, 92.71, 90.13], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T22:58:09.262832Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 9, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r9s1 (regression, -56.76%): Replacing EX1's dedicated register-file reread with stall-gated ID/EX snapshot refresh shifted complexity into decode-address muxing and an added WB forwarding compare/mux, so removing read ports can severely hurt CoreMark unless the operand-path timing and stall behavior are measured together.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:28:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r9s2\", \"title\": \"Single-adder static branch predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current decode-only predictor is the only predictor variant that has\\nimproved CoreMark, while BHT, gshare, loop, RAS, and return-cache variants\\nlost fitness primarily through extra IF-path timing and lookup logic. The\\ncurrent IF stage independently forms branch and JAL targets before selecting\\none, so the proven prediction policy still carries avoidable target-generation\\narea and muxing cost on the fetch path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current decode-only predictor is the only predictor variant that has\\nimproved CoreMark, while BHT, gshare, loop, RAS, and return-cache variants\\nlost fitness primarily through extra IF-path timing and lookup logic. The\\ncurrent IF stage independently forms branch and JAL targets before selecting\\none, so the proven prediction policy still carries avoidable target-generation\\narea and muxing cost on the fetch path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Preserve the existing backward-conditional-taken and direct-JAL prediction\\npolicy, but factor their target generation into one shared PC-relative adder:\\nselect a validated B- or J-immediate first, then perform a single target\\naddition only for the recognized prediction class. Keep forward branches and\\nJALR unpredicted, and carry the existing prediction metadata and EX mismatch\\nrecovery unchanged. Removing duplicated target arithmetic and an unnecessary\\npost-adder selection should improve Fmax and LUT pressure without adding\\npredictor state, aliasing, warm-up misses, or architectural risk.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Refactor the existing static BTFNT/direct-JAL predictor to select one validated PC-relative immediate and use a single shared target adder, preserving prediction validity, redirect behavior, and prediction metadata.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Refactor the existing static BTFNT/direct-JAL predictor to select one validated PC-relative immediate and use a single shared target adder, preserving prediction validity, redirect behavior, and prediction metadata.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 192.8, \"delta_pct\": -59.91, \"vs_baseline\": -31.83, \"fmax_mhz\": 83.68, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4340155, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10031, \"ff\": 2082, \"seeds\": [83.68, 94.22, 83.61], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T22:52:02.613436Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 9, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r9s2 (regression, -59.91%): Sharing B/J target generation through a selected-immediate mux and an unconditional `pc + selected_imm` adder left more decode logic on the IF next-PC cone, showing that arithmetic sharing can trade area for severe CoreMark timing loss.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:29:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r10s0\", \"title\": \"Explicit byte-lane load extraction\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The memory stage currently extracts subword load data with a variable 32-bit\\nright shift whose amount is formed from the byte offset multiplied by eight.\\nOn the Tang Nano FPGA this can infer a wider barrel-shifter-style mux than\\nthe four legal byte positions require, adding LUTs and delay on the load\\nresponse and forwarding path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The memory stage currently extracts subword load data with a variable 32-bit\\nright shift whose amount is formed from the byte offset multiplied by eight.\\nOn the Tang Nano FPGA this can infer a wider barrel-shifter-style mux than\\nthe four legal byte positions require, adding LUTs and delay on the load\\nresponse and forwarding path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the variable shift in the memory stage with explicit four-way byte\\nlane selection, and derive the halfword value from the selected aligned\\npair.  Keep the existing access masks, sign/zero-extension rules, aligned\\nRVFI memory address and data fields, and dmem-ready hold behavior unchanged.\\nThe smaller constant-index mux should reduce LUT pressure and shorten the\\nload-formatting path without changing CPI or pipeline ordering.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the variable load-data shift with explicit byte-offset lane selection and equivalent sign/zero extension, preserving dmem handshakes, masks, forwarding, and RVFI metadata.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the variable load-data shift with explicit byte-offset lane selection and equivalent sign/zero extension, preserving dmem handshakes, masks, forwarding, and RVFI metadata.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 214.39, \"delta_pct\": -55.42, \"vs_baseline\": -24.2, \"fmax_mhz\": 93.05, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4340155, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10665, \"ff\": 2082, \"seeds\": [93.05, 86.57, 95.13], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"# Implementation notes\\n\\n## Change\\n\\n- Updated `cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv` to extract load bytes with an\\n  explicit four-way `addr[1:0]` lane select.\\n- Halfword loads now select the low or high aligned 16-bit pair with\\n  `addr[1]`, followed by the existing sign/zero-extension logic.\\n- Store replication, access masks, misalignment trapping, dmem handshake\\n  gating, forwarding, and RVFI metadata paths were left unchanged.\\n\\n## Deviations and concerns\\n\\nNo architectural deviations. The halfword result for misaligned offsets is\\nnot architecturally observable because those accesses are trapped and do not\\nissue a dmem request.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- Verilator lint: pass (`verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv\\n  +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`).\\n- Local formal: environment-blocked before elaboration. `formal/run_all.sh`\\n  requires staging under `formal/riscv-formal/cores/`, but the sandbox rejects\\n  both cleanup of the existing PID directory and creation of a fresh staging\\n  directory with `Operation not permitted`. No RTL counterexample was\\n  produced; no formal retry was applicable.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T23:11:52.867964Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 10, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r10s0 (regression, -55.42%): Replacing the load-stage variable shift with explicit byte-lane and halfword muxes did not improve CoreMark and likely lengthened the load-response/forwarding cone, so FPGA resource-oriented mux simplification must be validated against the implemented timing path.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:30:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r10s1\", \"title\": \"Replicate register-file read banks\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current high-performing pipeline needs four combinational register-file\\nreads: two for decode and two for EX1's delayed operand reread.  Keeping all\\nfour reads in one physical array increases routing fanout from every\\nregister bit and can make the operand path placement-sensitive near the\\nTang Nano LUT budget.  The recent two-read-port experiment showed that\\nremoving ports moves too much timing work into decode and writeback, so the\\nbetter structural target is physical locality without changing the logical\\ninterface or operand timing.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current high-performing pipeline needs four combinational register-file\\nreads: two for decode and two for EX1's delayed operand reread.  Keeping all\\nfour reads in one physical array increases routing fanout from every\\nregister bit and can make the operand path placement-sensitive near the\\nTang Nano LUT budget.  The recent two-read-port experiment showed that\\nremoving ports moves too much timing work into decode and writeback, so the\\nbetter structural target is physical locality without changing the logical\\ninterface or operand timing.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Physically replicate the 32x32 register storage into an ID-read copy and an\\nEX1-read copy, with reset and every architectural write applied to both\\ncopies.  Keep the existing two read ports on each copy, including x0\\nhardwiring and write-first WB bypasses, so decode and EX1 retain their\\ncurrent independent read timing and RVFI-visible values.  Partitioning the\\nread mux trees and register-bit fanout should improve placement and Fmax\\nwhile spending flip-flops instead of adding a new forwarding mux, pipeline\\nstage, or memory-side queue.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/reg_file.sv\", \"description\": \"Duplicate the physical register array into decode-read and EX1-read copies, synchronize reset and WB writes to both, and preserve the existing four logical read ports with write-first and x0 behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/reg_file.sv\", \"description\": \"Duplicate the physical register array into decode-read and EX1-read copies, synchronize reset and WB writes to both, and preserve the existing four logical read ports with write-first and x0 behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 229.28, \"delta_pct\": -52.32, \"vs_baseline\": -18.93, \"fmax_mhz\": 99.51, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4340155, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10247, \"ff\": 2076, \"seeds\": [92.81, 99.51, 100.13], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T23:08:32.477478Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 10, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r10s1 (regression, -52.32%): Replicating the full 32x32 register file for ID and EX1 preserves logical read timing but can make FPGA resource, reset, and write-fanout costs overwhelm locality gains, so bank replication needs post-place evidence that the shared read mux is the binding constraint.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:31:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r10s2\", \"title\": \"Exact one-entry forward branch predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The proven backward-taken/direct-JAL predictor is the only predictor family\\nthat has improved this fixture. PC-indexed BHT/gshare, loop, RAS, and return\\npredictors all lost more Fmax than their extra prediction accuracy returned,\\nlargely because their lookup and state logic sat on the IF next-PC path.\\nCoreMark still pays the occasional forward-branch redirect, so a much smaller\\npredictor should target that residual cost without changing the successful\\nstatic policy.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The proven backward-taken/direct-JAL predictor is the only predictor family\\nthat has improved this fixture. PC-indexed BHT/gshare, loop, RAS, and return\\npredictors all lost more Fmax than their extra prediction accuracy returned,\\nlargely because their lookup and state logic sat on the IF next-PC path.\\nCoreMark still pays the occasional forward-branch redirect, so a much smaller\\npredictor should target that residual cost without changing the successful\\nstatic policy.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a single-entry exact-PC predictor containing one recently resolved forward\\nconditional branch and a two-bit direction counter. Consult it only when the\\nfetched instruction is a forward conditional branch; on a tag miss, retain\\nthe existing not-taken behavior, while backward branches remain statically\\npredicted taken and direct JALs retain their current prediction. Reuse the\\nexisting branch immediate/target arithmetic and update the entry only from a\\nprecise, non-stalled EX resolution event. The exact tag prevents the harmful\\naliasing seen in the tiny BHT, and the one-entry state avoids a table read,\\nglobal-history cone, loop bookkeeping, or return-target datapath.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a reset-valid one-entry exact-PC/two-bit predictor for forward conditional branches, preserving static backward-taken and direct-JAL prediction and the existing mismatch recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose a precise forward-branch predictor update event with the resolved branch PC and taken outcome, suppressed while EX is held by a data-memory stall.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the EX branch update event into IF without changing the external buses, pipeline retirement boundary, or single-channel RVFI contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a reset-valid one-entry exact-PC/two-bit predictor for forward conditional branches, preserving static backward-taken and direct-JAL prediction and the existing mismatch recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose a precise forward-branch predictor update event with the resolved branch PC and taken outcome, suppressed while EX is held by a data-memory stall.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the EX branch update event into IF without changing the external buses, pipeline retirement boundary, or single-channel RVFI contract.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 295.29, \"delta_pct\": -38.6, \"vs_baseline\": 4.41, \"fmax_mhz\": 128.16, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4340155, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10806, \"ff\": 2117, \"seeds\": [128.63, 126.29, 128.16], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T23:15:33.535467Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 10, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r10s2 (regression, -38.60%): Even a one-entry exact-PC forward-branch predictor can severely regress CoreMark when its fetched-branch decode, tag compare, and counter state feed the IF next-PC cone, so residual forward-redirect savings do not justify adding predictor logic to the fetch critical path.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:32:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r11s0\", \"title\": \"Share the RV32M quotient and remainder datapath\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The real ALU currently expresses DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU as separate\\narithmetic operators, which can infer multiple large divider networks even\\nthough quotient and remainder come from the same division operation. A prior\\nsharing attempt was build-broken because its combinational loop iterator\\ninferred a latch, so this is a focused repair of a potentially high-cost\\ndatapath rather than a pipeline change.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The real ALU currently expresses DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU as separate\\narithmetic operators, which can infer multiple large divider networks even\\nthough quotient and remainder come from the same division operation. A prior\\nsharing attempt was build-broken because its combinational loop iterator\\ninferred a latch, so this is a focused repair of a potentially high-cost\\ndatapath rather than a pipeline change.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Implement one fully combinational unsigned magnitude divider that produces\\nboth quotient and remainder, then apply operand-sign correction and the\\nspecified divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 rules to select DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU.\\nKeep the one-cycle ALU interface, preserve the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\\nsubstitutions, and use an automatic or fully assigned loop index so Yosys\\ninfers no latch. Sharing the divider should reduce LUT/routing pressure and\\nimprove Fmax without adding a global divide stall or changing RVFI timing.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the independent real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operators with one latch-free combinational magnitude divider and exact signedness, zero-divisor, and overflow correction; retain the shared multiplier and ALTOPS branch.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Add exact vectors for quotient/remainder signed and unsigned pairs, divide-by-zero, INT_MIN/-1 overflow, sign combinations, and repeated back-to-back operations.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the independent real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operators with one latch-free combinational magnitude divider and exact signedness, zero-divisor, and overflow correction; retain the shared multiplier and ALTOPS branch.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Add exact vectors for quotient/remainder signed and unsigned pairs, divide-by-zero, INT_MIN/-1 overflow, sign combinations, and repeated back-to-back operations.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 107.72, \"delta_pct\": -77.6, \"vs_baseline\": -61.91, \"fmax_mhz\": 46.75, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4340155, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 8069, \"ff\": 2070, \"seeds\": [46.75, 49.0, 45.51], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T23:28:27.221436Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 11, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r11s0 (regression, -77.60%): A latch-free shared 32-iteration restoring divider can catastrophically regress CoreMark by putting a long compare/subtract loop in the combinational ALU path, so divider sharing must be evaluated for timing depth rather than area reduction alone.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:33:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r11s1\", \"title\": \"Compact memory-sideband pipeline\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current EX/MEM to MEM/WB path carries the full retirement payload and\\ncontrol bundle through the dmem request, raw read-data, and load-formatting\\nlogic.  The prior broad memory-response retiming failed placement because\\nit added wide request/response payloads and global backpressure.  A narrower\\nstructural partition can target the memory-facing timing and routing without\\nrepeating that large backend transformation.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current EX/MEM to MEM/WB path carries the full retirement payload and\\ncontrol bundle through the dmem request, raw read-data, and load-formatting\\nlogic.  The prior broad memory-response retiming failed placement because\\nit added wide request/response payloads and global backpressure.  A narrower\\nstructural partition can target the memory-facing timing and routing without\\nrepeating that large backend transformation.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Split the memory stage into a compact memory-facing request/response island\\nand a separate retirement sideband.  The island should carry only the\\naddress, store data, byte enables, read/write bits, load width/sign metadata,\\nand the minimum destination information required for load forwarding and\\nwriteback; keep PC, instruction, source operands, and RVFI metadata on a\\nparallel sideband that does not traverse the dmem read/formatting cone.\\nPreserve one memory operation per cycle when io_dmemReady is high, localize\\nready/hold state to the outstanding request, and keep the existing strict\\nin-order MEM/WB retirement and RVFI ordering.  This should reduce routing\\npressure and isolate load extraction from the wide retirement path without\\nadding a completion queue or changing the external IO contract.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define compact memory request/response and retirement-sideband records so dmem-facing logic does not carry the full EX/MEM or MEM/WB payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Refactor the memory stage around the narrow request/response records, keeping dmem-ready hold behavior, load forwarding, byte masks, and RVFI data exact while isolating load formatting from retirement metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the compact memory island and parallel retirement sideband through the existing pipeline without changing the top-level buses, single-channel RVFI ports, or retirement boundary.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Update memory-operation hold and load-use controls to follow the compact request acceptance/completion signals without introducing global queue backpressure or duplicate side effects.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define compact memory request/response and retirement-sideband records so dmem-facing logic does not carry the full EX/MEM or MEM/WB payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Refactor the memory stage around the narrow request/response records, keeping dmem-ready hold behavior, load forwarding, byte masks, and RVFI data exact while isolating load formatting from retirement metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the compact memory island and parallel retirement sideband through the existing pipeline without changing the top-level buses, single-channel RVFI ports, or retirement boundary.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Update memory-operation hold and load-use controls to follow the compact request acceptance/completion signals without introducing global queue backpressure or duplicate side effects.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 337.15, \"delta_pct\": -29.89, \"vs_baseline\": 19.21, \"fmax_mhz\": 146.33, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4340155, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10169, \"ff\": 2076, \"seeds\": [146.33, 159.06, 131.56], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T23:31:25.823833Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 11, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r11s1 (regression, -29.89%): A combinational `mem_req_t`/`mem_retire_t` split does not by itself create physical isolation, and the added request-acceptance handshake can outweigh routing savings, so memory-sideband partitioning needs post-place critical-path and fanout evidence or a genuinely registered boundary.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:34:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r11s2\", \"title\": \"Static operand-identity branch prediction\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The proven backward-taken/direct-JAL predictor improves CoreMark, while\\nevery stateful predictor tested so far has added enough IF timing cost to\\nlose fitness. Some conditional branches have an architecturally certain\\ndirection when rs1 and rs2 name the same register, so this is a predictor\\nopportunity that needs no table, tags, history, or training state.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The proven backward-taken/direct-JAL predictor improves CoreMark, while\\nevery stateful predictor tested so far has added enough IF timing cost to\\nlose fitness. Some conditional branches have an architecturally certain\\ndirection when rs1 and rs2 name the same register, so this is a predictor\\nopportunity that needs no table, tags, history, or training state.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Extend the existing IF static predictor to recognize conditional branches\\nwith identical rs1 and rs2 fields. Predict BEQ, BGE, and BGEU as taken when\\nthe operands are the same; leave the complementary always-not-taken cases\\non the existing sequential path. Preserve backward-taken and direct-JAL\\nprediction, carry the current prediction metadata, and retain EX as the\\nauthoritative mismatch recovery point. The added five-bit identity check\\nshould be much cheaper than a dynamic lookup while eliminating redirects for\\ncompiler-emitted unconditional or known-direction branch idioms.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 1, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a stateless exact-direction branch check for identical source-register fields, combine only its taken cases with the existing backward-branch/direct-JAL predictor, and preserve current target, redirect, stall, and prediction metadata behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 1, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a stateless exact-direction branch check for identical source-register fields, combine only its taken cases with the existing backward-branch/direct-JAL predictor, and preserve current target, redirect, stall, and prediction metadata behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 327.48, \"delta_pct\": -31.9, \"vs_baseline\": 15.79, \"fmax_mhz\": 142.13, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4340155, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10314, \"ff\": 2082, \"seeds\": [143.64, 141.84, 142.13], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T23:24:19.862151Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 11, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r11s2 (regression, -31.90%): Even a stateless five-bit `rs1 == rs2` check plus funct3 decode can regress CoreMark when added to the IF next-PC cone, so architecturally certain branch identities are not worth predicting unless their decode cost is timing-neutral.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:35:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r12s0\", \"title\": \"Factor duplicate EX control-flow adders\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The high-performing bench pipeline already keeps operand forwarding out of\\nthe EX2 ALU cone, but ex_stage still spells the same PC-plus-immediate and\\nPC-plus-four sums in several branch, jump, prediction, and payload paths.\\nThose duplicated wide adders can increase LUT usage and routing pressure on\\nthe Tang Nano 20K even though they do not represent independent results.\\nPrior experiments show that reusing the main ALU through a new operand mux\\nis harmful, so the remaining opportunity is a local common-subexpression\\ncleanup that leaves ALU selection and redirect timing unchanged.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The high-performing bench pipeline already keeps operand forwarding out of\\nthe EX2 ALU cone, but ex_stage still spells the same PC-plus-immediate and\\nPC-plus-four sums in several branch, jump, prediction, and payload paths.\\nThose duplicated wide adders can increase LUT usage and routing pressure on\\nthe Tang Nano 20K even though they do not represent independent results.\\nPrior experiments show that reusing the main ALU through a new operand mux\\nis harmful, so the remaining opportunity is a local common-subexpression\\ncleanup that leaves ALU selection and redirect timing unchanged.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"In ex_stage, compute one EX2-local PC-plus-immediate sum and one PC-plus-four\\nsum, then reuse those wires for branch targets, direct-JAL targets,\\nfall-through recovery, prediction comparison, and the JAL link result.\\nPreserve the existing separate rs1-plus-immediate JALR sum, misalignment\\ntrapping, prediction metadata, dmem-stall behavior, and RVFI pc_next values.\\nExplicitly factoring only identical additions should let synthesis share the\\narithmetic without putting control-flow target selection on the normal ALU\\nresult path, potentially improving Fmax and LUT/routing utilization with no\\nIPC or architectural change.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 1, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Introduce local PC-plus-immediate and PC-plus-four wires in EX2 and replace duplicate equivalent additions while preserving the existing ALU, JALR, redirect, misalignment, stall, and RVFI behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 1, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Introduce local PC-plus-immediate and PC-plus-four wires in EX2 and replace duplicate equivalent additions while preserving the existing ALU, JALR, redirect, misalignment, stall, and RVFI behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 378.72, \"delta_pct\": -21.25, \"vs_baseline\": 33.91, \"fmax_mhz\": 164.37, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4340155, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10356, \"ff\": 2076, \"seeds\": [162.97, 164.37, 168.29], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T23:47:31.119417Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 12, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r12s0 (regression, -21.25%): Factoring identical EX2 `pc + imm` and `pc + 4` expressions can still regress CoreMark, so replacing duplicate adders with high-fanout shared wires must be validated for FPGA routing/timing rather than assumed to be a free common-subexpression optimization.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:36:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r12s1\", \"title\": \"Bank the register file for shallower read muxes\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current winning pipeline relies on four independent combinational\\nregister-file reads: two in decode and two for the delayed EX1 operand\\ncapture.  Removing a forwarding leg improved Fmax by shortening this\\noperand path, but physically replicating the entire register file increased\\nstorage and write fanout enough to regress severely.  A banked organization\\ncan attack the remaining 32-entry read-mux depth without paying the area\\nand reset cost of a second full copy.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current winning pipeline relies on four independent combinational\\nregister-file reads: two in decode and two for the delayed EX1 operand\\ncapture.  Removing a forwarding leg improved Fmax by shortening this\\noperand path, but physically replicating the entire register file increased\\nstorage and write fanout enough to regress severely.  A banked organization\\ncan attack the remaining 32-entry read-mux depth without paying the area\\nand reset cost of a second full copy.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Reorganize the single architectural register array as four 8-entry banks\\nselected by the upper register-index bits.  Implement each read as an\\n8-entry bank-local mux followed by a small bank select, while retaining all\\nfour existing logical read ports, x0 hardwiring, synchronous writes, and\\nwrite-first WB bypass behavior.  Decode and EX1 therefore keep identical\\noperand timing and RVFI-visible values, but the physical read muxes and\\nregister-bit routing become localized and shallower.  Keep the bank write\\ndecode explicit so reset, x0, and every architectural write update exactly\\none bank without introducing replicated storage or extra pipeline stages.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/reg_file.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the monolithic 32-entry read implementation with four 8-entry register banks, preserving all decode and EX1 read ports, x0 behavior, reset, and write-first WB bypass semantics while keeping one physical copy of the architectural state.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/reg_file.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the monolithic 32-entry read implementation with four 8-entry register banks, preserving all decode and EX1 read ports, x0 behavior, reset, and write-first WB bypass semantics while keeping one physical copy of the architectural state.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 297.27, \"delta_pct\": -38.18, \"vs_baseline\": 5.11, \"fmax_mhz\": 129.02, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4340155, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10191, \"ff\": 2078, \"seeds\": [147.08, 129.02, 128.34], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T23:57:09.919995Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 12, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r12s1 (regression, -38.18%): Banking one 32x32 register file into four 8-entry arrays did not guarantee shallower FPGA read muxes, while four combinational ports still paid bank-select, decode, and routing cost, so physical isolation must be confirmed before trading a simple array for banked RTL.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:37:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r12s2\", \"title\": \"Decode-elided backward branch prediction\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The existing static backward-taken/direct-JAL predictor is the only predictor\\nfamily that has improved this fixture, while dynamic tables, return state,\\nand extra branch identity checks have lost more Fmax than their saved flushes\\nrepay. Its IF path still spends logic validating branch funct3 before making\\na speculative prediction, even though EX already treats illegal encodings as\\ntraps and performs authoritative mismatch recovery.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The existing static backward-taken/direct-JAL predictor is the only predictor\\nfamily that has improved this fixture, while dynamic tables, return state,\\nand extra branch identity checks have lost more Fmax than their saved flushes\\nrepay. Its IF path still spends logic validating branch funct3 before making\\na speculative prediction, even though EX already treats illegal encodings as\\ntraps and performs authoritative mismatch recovery.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Preserve the successful backward-conditional-taken and direct-JAL policy, but\\nmake the IF predictor recognize a backward branch using only the branch opcode\\nand displacement sign. Do not qualify the speculative prediction with funct3;\\nan illegal or reserved encoding may fetch the target transiently, then EX will\\nresolve it as a trap and redirect to the sequential PC through the existing\\nprediction-mismatch path. Keep prediction metadata, target arithmetic, JALR\\nbehavior, and all RVFI retirement semantics unchanged. Removing the funct3\\ncompare and its validation cone should recover Fmax without predictor state,\\naliasing, warm-up misses, or additional redirect latency.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Simplify the existing static predictor to use opcode and displacement sign for speculative backward-branch prediction, while retaining direct-JAL prediction and current prediction metadata and redirect behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Simplify the existing static predictor to use opcode and displacement sign for speculative backward-branch prediction, while retaining direct-JAL prediction and current prediction metadata and redirect behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 295.31, \"delta_pct\": -38.59, \"vs_baseline\": 4.42, \"fmax_mhz\": 128.17, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4340155, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10222, \"ff\": 2082, \"seeds\": [125.5, 130.75, 128.17], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T23:42:18.284430Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 12, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r12s2 (regression, -38.59%): Eliding the IF predictor's `funct3` legality check still regressed CoreMark, showing that removing one decode predicate is insufficient when the remaining opcode/sign recognition and backward-target arithmetic stay on the fetch next-PC path.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:38:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r13s0\", \"title\": \"Trim dead pipeline sidebands\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The winning bench pipeline still carries control and branch metadata that\\nhas no consumer after EX2.  `is_lui` is already encoded by ALU_LUI plus\\nalu_src, while ex_mem branch_taken/branch_target are used only to form the\\nlocal redirect and are never needed by MEM, WB, or RVFI.  These bits add\\nrouted state and fanout across pipeline bundles despite not affecting\\narchitectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The winning bench pipeline still carries control and branch metadata that\\nhas no consumer after EX2.  `is_lui` is already encoded by ALU_LUI plus\\nalu_src, while ex_mem branch_taken/branch_target are used only to form the\\nlocal redirect and are never needed by MEM, WB, or RVFI.  These bits add\\nrouted state and fanout across pipeline bundles despite not affecting\\narchitectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Remove the dead `is_lui` bit from the internal control bundle and remove the\\nunused branch_taken/branch_target fields from the EX/MEM bundle, leaving the\\ndecoder's standalone is_lui output intact for its unit-test interface.\\nKeep branch comparison, target generation, redirect recovery, pc_next, and\\nall RVFI fields local to EX2 and preserve the existing valid/hold behavior.\\nThe narrower pipeline records should reduce flip-flops, routing congestion,\\nand control fanout without adding a mux or changing CoreMark instruction\\ntiming.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 1, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete the unused ctrl_t is_lui field and the unused EX/MEM branch_taken and branch_target sidebands while retaining all fields consumed by MEM, WB, hazards, and RVFI.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Stop copying the decoder's standalone is_lui indication into the pipeline control record; retain the decoder port and LUI ALU control encoding unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove assignments of dead branch sidebands to the EX/MEM payload while keeping local branch resolution, misalignment trapping, redirect generation, and pc_next behavior identical.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 1, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Delete the unused ctrl_t is_lui field and the unused EX/MEM branch_taken and branch_target sidebands while retaining all fields consumed by MEM, WB, hazards, and RVFI.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Stop copying the decoder's standalone is_lui indication into the pipeline control record; retain the decoder port and LUI ALU control encoding unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove assignments of dead branch sidebands to the EX/MEM payload while keeping local branch resolution, misalignment trapping, redirect generation, and pc_next behavior identical.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 271.4, \"delta_pct\": -43.56, \"vs_baseline\": -4.04, \"fmax_mhz\": 117.79, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4340155, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10161, \"ff\": 2076, \"seeds\": [119.47, 117.79, 113.71], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"# Implementation notes\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- Removed `is_lui` from the internal `ctrl_t` pipeline bundle.\\n- Kept the decoder's standalone `is_lui` output and decoder unit-test interface;\\n  `id_stage` still connects that output but no longer copies it into `ctrl_t`.\\n- Removed `branch_taken` and `branch_target` from `ex_mem_t`.\\n- Kept branch comparison, target generation, misalignment trapping, redirect\\n  generation, and `pc_next` resolution local to EX2.\\n- Removed only the EX/MEM payload assignments for those dead branch fields.\\n\\n## Deviations and concerns\\n\\nNo architectural or valid/hold behavior changes were made. The local\\n`branch_taken` and `branch_target` signals remain in `ex_stage.sv` because\\nthey are required by EX2 redirect and misalignment logic.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- Verilator lint: pass.\\n- Formal: not executable in this environment. The repository harness points\\n  at a read-only shared `riscv-formal` tree, so its generated work directory\\n  could not be cleaned/created. A temporary writable copy generated the\\n  checks, but every SBY task failed before execution because the installed\\n  `sby` could not import Python module `click` (`ModuleNotFoundError`). No\\n  RTL counterexample was produced.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T00:08:25.738618Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 13, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r13s0 (regression, -43.56%): Removing architecturally dead fields from packed `ctrl_t` and `ex_mem_t` records can still perturb FPGA synthesis/placement enough to hurt CoreMark, so pipeline-sideband trimming needs post-implementation timing evidence rather than an assumed routing win.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:39:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r13s1\", \"title\": \"Isolate the RV32M multiply pipeline\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current EX2 ALU structurally contains a full-width multiply alongside\\nthe ordinary integer datapath.  The successful EX1/EX2 retiming shortened\\nthe forwarding-to-ALU path, but ordinary CoreMark instructions still pay\\nthe shared M-operation mux and routing footprint.  A dedicated, narrow\\nmultiply lane is a more targeted structural change than another global\\nqueue or front-end buffer.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current EX2 ALU structurally contains a full-width multiply alongside\\nthe ordinary integer datapath.  The successful EX1/EX2 retiming shortened\\nthe forwarding-to-ALU path, but ordinary CoreMark instructions still pay\\nthe shared M-operation mux and routing footprint.  A dedicated, narrow\\nmultiply lane is a more targeted structural change than another global\\nqueue or front-end buffer.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Split RV32M multiplication from the base ALU into a small registered\\nmultiply lane.  Launch MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU operands from EX1, capture the\\nresult through a one-cycle M-unit pipeline, and add precise interlock and\\nforwarding only for the in-flight multiply and its consumers; ordinary\\nALU, branch, load/store, and divide instructions continue through the\\nexisting EX2 path.  Remove multiply hardware from the normal ALU instance\\nwhile retaining exact signed high-half correction, RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\\nbehavior, RV32M corner cases, in-order retirement, and unchanged external\\nbuses and RVFI ports.  The isolated lane should reduce the normal EX2\\ncone and routing pressure while imposing latency only on the relatively\\ninfrequent multiply dependency chains.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Refactor the base ALU so multiply operations are supplied by a separate M-unit interface, preserving the formal ALTOPS branch and exact RV32M arithmetic semantics for the dedicated lane.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the registered multiply execution lane, select its completion into EX/MEM, and preserve EX2 control-flow, memory, misalignment, forwarding, and RVFI metadata behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add precise multiply busy and dependency interlocks so the in-order pipeline cannot overwrite or consume an incomplete M result, without stalling unrelated instructions unnecessarily.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire multiply start/completion and the age-ordered multiply forwarding source through the existing single-issue datapath without changing top-level IO.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Refactor the base ALU so multiply operations are supplied by a separate M-unit interface, preserving the formal ALTOPS branch and exact RV32M arithmetic semantics for the dedicated lane.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the registered multiply execution lane, select its completion into EX/MEM, and preserve EX2 control-flow, memory, misalignment, forwarding, and RVFI metadata behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add precise multiply busy and dependency interlocks so the in-order pipeline cannot overwrite or consume an incomplete M result, without stalling unrelated instructions unnecessarily.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire multiply start/completion and the age-ordered multiply forwarding source through the existing single-issue datapath without changing top-level IO.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: pc_fwd_ch0\\nting trace to Verilog testbench: engine_0/trace_tb.v\\nSBY 21:15:11 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:18  Writing trace to constraints file: engine_0/trace.smtc\\nSBY 21:15:11 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:18  Writing trace to Yosys witness file: engine_0/trace.yw\\nSBY 21:15:11 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:18  Status: failed\\nSBY 21:15:11 [reg_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=1)\\nSBY 21:15:11 [reg_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: FAIL\\nSBY 21:15:11 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:18 (18)\\nSBY 21:15:11 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:15 (15)\\nSBY 21:15:11 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned FAIL\\nSBY 21:15:11 [reg_ch0] summary: counterexample trace: reg_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY 21:15:11 [reg_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_reg_check_sv_44_60 at rvfi_reg_check.sv:44.6-44.59 step 20\\nSBY 21:15:11 [reg_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\n\\nFormal: 51 passed, 2 failed\\nFailed: pc_fwd_ch0 reg_ch0\\n\\n--- pc_fwd_ch0/logfile.txt (last 30 lines) ---\\nSBY 21:14:53 [pc_fwd_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 8..\\nSBY 21:14:53 [pc_fwd_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 9..\\nSBY 21:14:53 [pc_fwd_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 10..\\nSBY 21:14:53 [pc_fwd_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 11..\\nSBY 21:14:53 [pc_fwd_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 12..\\nSBY 21:14:53 [pc_fwd_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 13..\\nSBY 21:14:53 [pc_fwd_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipp