assert_rvfi_pc_fwd_check_sv_41_55 at rvfi_pc_fwd_check.sv:41.6-41.69 step 20\\nSBY 21:14:54 [pc_fwd_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\n\\nFull run log: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-luna-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-002-r13s1/formal/last_run-6736.log\\nPer-check logs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-luna-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-002-r13s1/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-6736/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 13, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r13s1 (broken, n/a): A forked registered MUL completion lane cannot expose only a result/rd bypass while suppressing the normal EX2 entry; its valid bit, writeback payload, PC-next, and RVFI metadata must transfer atomically or `pc_fwd` and register checks diverge.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:40:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r13s2\", \"title\": \"Single-entry JALR target cache\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The proven static predictor removes most direct-JAL and backward-loop\\nredirects, but JALR returns still resolve in EX and pay a redirect bubble.\\nLarger dynamic predictors and RAS variants regressed this fixture because\\nIF-stage decode, table lookup, or target selection extended the fetch\\ncritical path. Repeated hot return sites are a narrower opportunity.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The proven static predictor removes most direct-JAL and backward-loop\\nredirects, but JALR returns still resolve in EX and pay a redirect bubble.\\nLarger dynamic predictors and RAS variants regressed this fixture because\\nIF-stage decode, table lookup, or target selection extended the fetch\\ncritical path. Repeated hot return sites are a narrower opportunity.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a one-entry EX-trained indirect-target cache for JALR control transfers.\\nWhen a JALR resolves, capture its instruction PC and resolved target; on a\\nlater fetch of the same PC, use an exact PC match to supply the saved target\\ndirectly, without decoding the fetched instruction, adding a target adder,\\nor maintaining history/counter state in IF. Retain the existing static\\nbackward-branch/direct-JAL predictor as the fallback, carry the prediction\\nmetadata through the existing pipeline, and keep EX authoritative so stale\\nentries merely cause the existing prediction-mismatch redirect. This should\\nremove recurring JALR return bubbles at much lower timing and area cost than\\na RAS or multi-entry BTB.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an exact-PC, one-entry indirect-target lookup that overrides only the unpredicted JALR case, while preserving the current static predictor, redirect priority, and prediction metadata behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the resolved JALR instruction PC, target, and valid update event so the indirect-target entry is trained only by an older, architecturally resolved JALR.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the EX JALR training record into IF without changing the external buses, pipeline retirement boundary, or RVFI contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an exact-PC, one-entry indirect-target lookup that overrides only the unpredicted JALR case, while preserving the current static predictor, redirect priority, and prediction metadata behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the resolved JALR instruction PC, target, and valid update event so the indirect-target entry is trained only by an older, architecturally resolved JALR.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the EX JALR training record into IF without changing the external buses, pipeline retirement boundary, or RVFI contract.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 314.75, \"delta_pct\": -34.55, \"vs_baseline\": 11.29, \"fmax_mhz\": 135.98, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4320227, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10485, \"ff\": 2149, \"seeds\": [149.01, 129.35, 135.98], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T00:10:59.726703Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 13, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r13s2 (regression, -34.55%): Even a one-entry EX-trained JALR target cache with only an exact-PC compare and target mux on the IF next-PC path can cost more CoreMark timing than recurring return bubbles save, so minimal indirect prediction must still be timing-neutral in fetch.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:41:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r14s0\", \"title\": \"Register the sequential fetch PC increment\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The winning bench core already gets its large gain from EX1/EX2 retiming and\\nthe lightweight static predictor.  The remaining ordinary fetch path still\\ncomputes a 32-bit `pc + 4` adder and feeds it through the prediction mux on\\nevery non-control instruction.  This is a high-fanout, always-active piece\\nof the IF next-PC cone even when no prediction is selected.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The winning bench core already gets its large gain from EX1/EX2 retiming and\\nthe lightweight static predictor.  The remaining ordinary fetch path still\\ncomputes a 32-bit `pc + 4` adder and feeds it through the prediction mux on\\nevery non-control instruction.  This is a high-fanout, always-active piece\\nof the IF next-PC cone even when no prediction is selected.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a registered `pc_plus4` sidecar to the IF stage and use it as the\\nsequential fall-through value, while leaving backward-branch/direct-JAL\\ntarget arithmetic and EX-authoritative redirect recovery unchanged.  Update\\nthe sidecar coherently with reset, normal sequential advance, redirect, and\\nstall; on a redirect load `redirect_target + 4`, and on a normal advance\\nderive the next sidecar from the current PC so the extra increment is not on\\nthe PC selection path.  This should remove the common `pc + 4` adder from\\nthe fetch critical path without changing prediction metadata, valid/flush\\nbehavior, or RVFI PC fields.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add and maintain a coherent registered PC-plus-four value, use it for the non-predicted fall-through path, and preserve redirect priority, stalls, static predictions, and IF/ID metadata.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add and maintain a coherent registered PC-plus-four value, use it for the non-predicted fall-through path, and preserve redirect priority, stalls, static predictions, and IF/ID metadata.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 219.12, \"delta_pct\": -54.44, \"vs_baseline\": -22.52, \"fmax_mhz\": 95.1, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4340155, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10103, \"ff\": 2116, \"seeds\": [95.1, 96.3, 94.08], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T00:27:29.671298Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 14, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r14s0 (regression, -54.44%): A registered IF `pc_plus4` sidecar can hurt CoreMark despite removing the sequential adder from the next-PC mux, because its extra state, fanout, and `pc + 8` maintenance path still perturb FPGA timing; fetch arithmetic retiming needs post-implementation evidence.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:42:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r14s1\", \"title\": \"Register the compact load-response boundary\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current memory stage places the FPGA data-memory response, variable\\nbyte-lane extraction, sign extension, and MEM/WB capture in one timing\\ninterval.  The earlier broad memory retiming attempt failed placement\\nbecause it carried wide request and retirement payloads through added\\ncontrol.  A narrower boundary can target the likely memory critical path\\nwithout replicating the whole backend or adding a completion queue.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current memory stage places the FPGA data-memory response, variable\\nbyte-lane extraction, sign extension, and MEM/WB capture in one timing\\ninterval.  The earlier broad memory retiming attempt failed placement\\nbecause it carried wide request and retirement payloads through added\\ncontrol.  A narrower boundary can target the likely memory critical path\\nwithout replicating the whole backend or adding a completion queue.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a registered, compact memory-response stage between the existing\\nEX/MEM request and MEM/WB retirement paths.  Capture only the accepted raw\\ndmem read word plus byte offset, width/sign metadata, operation kind, and\\nthe minimum destination/valid token; perform load extraction and\\nsign-extension after that register while carrying the existing retirement\\nsideband in age order.  Stores and loads must remain one operation per\\ncycle when io_dmemReady is high, while a dmem stall holds the request and\\nresponse token atomically.  This should isolate FPGA memory-output timing\\nfrom the load-formatting cone and improve Fmax with one extra load latency,\\nwhile preserving precise load-use forwarding, store ordering, RVFI memory\\nfields, rvfi_order, and all external buses.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define a narrow registered memory-response payload containing raw read data, lane/width/sign metadata, operation validity, and the retirement token needed to align loads and stores.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Split memory request acceptance from response formatting, registering the compact response only on dmem-ready and preserving byte masks, load semantics, store effects, and deterministic RVFI payloads.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Adjust dmem-stall, load-use, and forwarding timing for the extra response boundary without allowing duplicate requests or retirement.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the compact response and delayed load-forwarding result into the existing single-issue pipeline while retaining the unchanged top-level IO and RVFI contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define a narrow registered memory-response payload containing raw read data, lane/width/sign metadata, operation validity, and the retirement token needed to align loads and stores.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Split memory request acceptance from response formatting, registering the compact response only on dmem-ready and preserving byte masks, load semantics, store effects, and deterministic RVFI payloads.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Adjust dmem-stall, load-use, and forwarding timing for the extra response boundary without allowing duplicate requests or retirement.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the compact response and delayed load-forwarding result into the existing single-issue pipeline while retaining the unchanged top-level IO and RVFI contract.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 316.02, \"delta_pct\": -34.29, \"vs_baseline\": 11.74, \"fmax_mhz\": 144.86, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4583906, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10426, \"ff\": 2064, \"seeds\": [150.24, 136.15, 144.86], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T00:33:08.716049Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 14, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r14s1 (regression, -34.29%): Even a compact registered dmem response can regress CoreMark when the added raw-word/metadata token changes load-use forwarding and stall control, so memory retiming must preserve one-cycle load throughput and atomic response/retirement alignment rather than merely narrow the payload.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:43:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r14s2\", \"title\": \"Short-loop filtered backward prediction\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The existing backward-taken/direct-JAL predictor is the only predictor\\nfamily that improved this fixture, but it predicts every backward\\nconditional branch as taken.  That policy pays a full recovery flush for\\nbackward control transfers that are not tight loops, especially uncommon\\nerror or exit paths.  Dynamic tables, return predictors, and extra IF\\nlookups have already shown that their timing cost is too high for this\\ncore, so the useful remaining opportunity is a stateless refinement of the\\nproven predictor.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The existing backward-taken/direct-JAL predictor is the only predictor\\nfamily that improved this fixture, but it predicts every backward\\nconditional branch as taken.  That policy pays a full recovery flush for\\nbackward control transfers that are not tight loops, especially uncommon\\nerror or exit paths.  Dynamic tables, return predictors, and extra IF\\nlookups have already shown that their timing cost is too high for this\\ncore, so the useful remaining opportunity is a stateless refinement of the\\nproven predictor.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Restrict the existing backward-conditional prediction to short backward\\ndisplacements, using the already decoded branch immediate sign/upper bits\\nas a loop-size heuristic, while retaining direct-JAL prediction and the\\ncurrent EX-authoritative mismatch recovery.  A small negative displacement\\nis much more likely to be a hot loop back edge than a long-range backward\\ntransfer; leaving the latter predicted not-taken avoids its taken-path\\nflush without adding BHT/RAS state, tags, or a new IF target lookup.  The\\nprediction metadata and target arithmetic remain unchanged, and illegal or\\nmisclassified branches still recover through the existing redirect path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a simple short-negative-displacement filter to backward conditional prediction, preserving direct-JAL prediction, prediction metadata, redirect priority, and EX mismatch recovery.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a simple short-negative-displacement filter to backward conditional prediction, preserving direct-JAL prediction, prediction metadata, redirect priority, and EX mismatch recovery.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 219.81, \"delta_pct\": -54.29, \"vs_baseline\": -22.28, \"fmax_mhz\": 95.54, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4346393, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10321, \"ff\": 2082, \"seeds\": [96.8, 95.54, 93.44], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T00:29:51.423454Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 14, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r14s2 (regression, -54.29%): Filtering backward-branch prediction with a wide `branch_imm[31:8]` equality added enough decode and immediate logic to the IF next-PC path that saved long-exit flushes could not repay the fetch timing cost, so stateless predictor refinements must be timing-neutral.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
