{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r1s0.yaml && ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r1s0.yaml\\\").slice(\\\"id\\\",\\\"category\\\",\\\"expected_impact\\\")' && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r1s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-001-r1s0\ntitle: \"Zero-bubble load-use forwarding\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current five-stage pipeline unconditionally stalls one cycle for every\n  load-use dependency, even though the Tang Nano bench presents combinational\n  zero-wait read data. CoreMark has frequent load-dependent address, compare,\n  and arithmetic instructions, so this bubble directly reduces iterations per\n  cycle. The existing P&R report also shows the EX/MEM-to-EX forwarding path as\n  the dominant timing path, making a dedicated load-data bypass a focused\n  high-value datapath optimization.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a dedicated EX/MEM load-data bypass from the memory stage's extracted\n  byte/half/word value into the EX operand mux, and remove the unconditional\n  load-use bubble. When dmemReady is low, hold the dependent instruction and\n  suppress redirects or side effects until the load completes; when it is high,\n  forward the load value directly and retire the dependent instruction without\n  a bubble. This should preserve arbitrary bus-stall correctness while\n  improving CoreMark IPC on the zero-wait FPGA path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Replace the unconditional load-use bubble with replay-safe holding on an outstanding dmem stall, and provide control to block redirects while the dependent instruction waits.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add a highest-priority EX/MEM load-result forwarding selection, with normal ALU and MEM/WB forwarding retained as fallbacks.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Expose the already sign/zero-extended load value as a combinational forwarding source while retaining the existing RVFI extraction and stall behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Consume the load-data bypass and ensure a stalled dependent instruction cannot generate a redirect or architectural side effect before its operand is valid.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the load-result bypass and dmem-stall qualification through the pipeline without changing the top-level IO or RVFI contract.\"\n{\"id\"=>\"hyp-20260710-001-r1s0\", \"category\"=>\"micro_opt\", \"expected_impact\"=>{\"fitness_delta_pct\"=>5, \"confidence\"=>\"medium\"}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
