{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r5s0.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r5s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-001-r5s0\ntitle: \"Zero-bubble zero-wait load-use bypass\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The five-stage pipeline currently inserts a load-use bubble even when the\n  data bus is zero-wait, which is the normal FPGA bench case and a substantial\n  part of the CoreMark memory/arithmetic stream. A prior unrestricted bypass\n  attempt was broken because it allowed a dependent instruction to advance\n  while dmemReady was low. The optimization should therefore be qualified by\n  the actual ready signal and leave the existing stalled-bus sequencing intact.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a combinational EX/MEM load-result bypass using the memory stage's\n  already sign- or zero-extended load value. Suppress the load-use bubble only\n  when io_dmemReady is high; in that case the dependent instruction advances\n  immediately and selects the load value ahead of the normal ALU/MEM-WB\n  forwarding paths. When dmemReady is low, retain the current load-use bubble,\n  EX/MEM hold, MEM/WB valid suppression, and redirect behavior so no dependent\n  instruction, register write, or RVFI record can observe incomplete memory\n  data. This preserves the arbitrary-stall correctness contract while removing\n  one cycle from each zero-wait load dependency.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Qualify load-use stalling with dmemReady so only zero-wait loads use the new bypass, while preserving the existing dmem-stall and flush precedence.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Expose the current load's extracted sign/zero-extended value as a combinational forwarding source without changing MEM/WB capture or RVFI metadata.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add an EX/MEM load-result forwarding selection with priority over the normal EX/MEM ALU and MEM/WB selections.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the ready-qualified memory load bypass into EX while retaining the unchanged external IO and single-channel RVFI contract.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Select the forwarded load value for dependent ALU, address, and branch operands, with no bypass use when the memory request is stalled.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
