{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \".\" cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r6s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"1:id: hyp-20260710-001-r6s0\n2:title: \"Share the combinational divide and remainder datapath\"\n3:category: micro_opt\n4:motivation: |\n5:  The ALU currently spells out signed and unsigned DIV and REM as separate\n6:  operators. On the FPGA this can leave redundant quotient/remainder divider\n7:  cones and wide result-mux routing in the already timing-sensitive EX2\n8:  stage. The previous iterative-divider experiment showed that adding a\n9:  multi-cycle stall is too expensive, so the useful opportunity is to reduce\n10:  hardware while retaining the existing single-cycle ALU contract.\n11:hypothesis: |\n12:  Rewrite the real RV32M division logic around one combinational unsigned\n13:  magnitude divider that produces both quotient and remainder, then apply\n14:  operand-sign correction and the RISC-V divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 rules\n15:  to select DIV, DIVU, REM, or REMU. Keep the ALTOPS formal substitutions\n16:  unchanged and preserve combinational latency, so dependent instructions,\n17:  RVFI ordering, and dmem-stall behavior do not acquire new bubbles. Sharing\n18:  the expensive divide work should reduce LUT/routing load and improve Fmax\n19:  without the throughput loss of a globally held iterative unit.\n20:expected_impact:\n21:  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n22:  confidence: medium\n23:changes:\n24:  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n25:    description: \"Replace the independent real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operators with one shared quotient-and-remainder datapath, including exact RV32M signedness, zero-divisor, and overflow handling while retaining the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS branch.\"\n26:  - file: test/test_alu.py\n27:    description: \"Extend ALU coverage for shared-divider signed and unsigned quotient/remainder pairs, divide-by-zero, INT_MIN/-1 overflow, and back-to-back operations to guard the refactor.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
