{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.category==\\\"structural\\\") | [.id,.title,.outcome,(.fitness//\\\"\\\"),(.delta_pct//\\\"\\\"),(.fmax_mhz//\\\"\\\"),(.lut4//\\\"\\\"),(.lesson//\\\"\\\")] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20260710-002-r1s1\tAdd a decoupled instruction prefetch FIFO\tregression\t270.21\t-4.46\t127.15\t10041\t\nhyp-20260710-002-r2s1\tDecouple long-latency M execution\tregression\t267.72\t-13.79\t114.04\t5901\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r2s1 (regression, -13.79%): A radix-2 iterative divider that holds the in-order pipeline for its full multi-cycle latency can lose more CoreMark throughput than removing divide operators from the EX cone gains in timing, so divider frequency and stall cost must be measured before coupling DIV/REM to a global EX hold.\nhyp-20260710-002-r3s1\tAdd a minimal elastic fetch skid buffer\tregression\t278.09\t-10.46\t119.99\t10193\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r3s1 (regression, -10.46%): A registered one-entry IF skid buffer must preserve empty-slot or simultaneous pop/push bypass behavior and redirect refill latency, or its added fetch bubbles outweigh the isolated imem-stall cycles it hides.\nhyp-20260710-002-r4s1\tResolve control flow in decode\tbroken\t\t\t\t\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r4s1 (broken, n/a): Moving branch/JALR resolution into ID requires age-ordered operand bypasses and synchronized `resolved_valid`/redirect/flush/RVFI metadata, because a partial early redirect path can make the retired instruction stream, PC-next values, and register checks disagree even when the EX fallback remains.\nhyp-20260710-002-r5s1\tRetimed two-phase execute pipeline\timprovement\t396.37\t24.91\t172.03\t10388\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r5s1 (improvement, +24.91%): Splitting execute into an operand/forwarding EX1 and arithmetic/control EX2 stage can materially improve CoreMark fitness by removing the forwarding muxes from the ALU cone, provided EX2-to-EX1 age-ordered bypasses and precise bubble/hold control preserve dependent ALU, load-use, and dmem-stall ordering.\nhyp-20260710-002-r6s1\tAdd a one-entry nonblocking store buffer\tregression\t211.24\t-46.71\t90.98\t10769\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r6s1 (regression, -46.71%): A one-entry store buffer does not hide dmem stalls if queue occupancy still feeds the global `dmem_stall` and a combinational `store_dmem_valid` priority mux arbitrates the external bus, so capture/drain handshakes must be decoupled without lengthening the memory timing path or serializing later accesses.\nhyp-20260710-002-r7s1\tElastic in-order memory backend\tbroken\t\t\t\t\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r7s1 (broken, n/a): Moving the retirement boundary behind an elastic completion queue can make the causal RVFI/dmem assumptions unsatisfiable at a shallow step and cascade into every instruction check, so queue issue, memory-handshake, forwarding, and in-order retirement metadata must remain formally coherent before measuring stall hiding.\nhyp-20260710-002-r8s1\tRetimed two-phase memory response\tplacement_failed\t\t\t\t\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r8s1 (placement_failed, n/a): Registering the dmem request/response boundary is not free on this FPGA: carrying full `mem_req_t`/`mem_resp_t` payloads plus request-stall and extra load-forwarding control can make placement fail, so isolate the memory read/format cone with compact metadata and localized backpressure rather than a wide retimed backend.\nhyp-20260710-002-r9s1\tTwo-read-port operand snapshot pipeline\tregression\t207.92\t-56.76\t90.24\t10561\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r9s1 (regression, -56.76%): Replacing EX1's dedicated register-file reread with stall-gated ID/EX snapshot refresh shifted complexity into decode-address muxing and an added WB forwarding compare/mux, so removing read ports can severely hurt CoreMark unless the operand-path timing and stall behavior are measured together.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
