{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -c 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r2s1\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-001-r3s0\\\")' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r2s1\",\"title\":\"Decouple long-latency M execution\",\"category\":\"structural\",\"motivation\":\"The current five-stage core places full-width multiply and divide/remainder\\narithmetic directly in the EX combinational cone. That cone is a poor\\nstructural match for the Tang Nano timing budget: the best run is only\\n132.29 MHz while already using 10554 LUT4s, and the prior structural FIFO\\nattempt showed that extra front-end state can lower Fmax. CoreMark's hot\\npath is predominantly integer and memory work, so isolating infrequent\\ndivide/remainder operations should improve timing without adding bubbles to\\nordinary ALU instructions.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The current five-stage core places full-width multiply and divide/remainder\\narithmetic directly in the EX combinational cone. That cone is a poor\\nstructural match for the Tang Nano timing budget: the best run is only\\n132.29 MHz while already using 10554 LUT4s, and the prior structural FIFO\\nattempt showed that extra front-end state can lower Fmax. CoreMark's hot\\npath is predominantly integer and memory work, so isolating infrequent\\ndivide/remainder operations should improve timing without adding bubbles to\\nordinary ALU instructions.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Replace the combinational divide/remainder portion of the ALU with a shared\\niterative radix-2 M execution unit. A DIV, DIVU, REM, or REMU entering EX\\nholds the in-order pipeline while the unit runs, then writes one RV32M-correct\\nresult through the existing EX/MEM and RVFI paths; ordinary ALU, load/store,\\nbranch, and multiply operations retain their single-cycle path. Add explicit\\nbusy/done control and operand/result registers so the divider is removed from\\nthe normal EX critical path, while preserving the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\\nbehavior and all trap, memory-stall, and retirement ordering invariants.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":6,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/alu.sv\",\"description\":\"Remove the normal-path / and % operators for DIV/REM and expose a clean divider request/result interface while retaining the ALTOPS and exact RV32M corner-case behavior.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate the iterative M unit as a replay-safe multi-cycle EX operation, holding the instruction and preventing duplicate side effects until its result is ready.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Add divider-busy backpressure that freezes younger pipeline state but allows the in-flight divide to complete and retire exactly once.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire divider start, busy, and completion signals through the pipeline without changing the external bus or single-channel RVFI contract.\"}]},\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":6,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/alu.sv\",\"description\":\"Remove the normal-path / and % operators for DIV/REM and expose a clean divider request/result interface while retaining the ALTOPS and exact RV32M corner-case behavior.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate the iterative M unit as a replay-safe multi-cycle EX operation, holding the instruction and preventing duplicate side effects until its result is ready.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Add divider-busy backpressure that freezes younger pipeline state but allows the in-flight divide to complete and retire exactly once.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire divider start, busy, and completion signals through the pipeline without changing the external bus or single-channel RVFI contract.\"}],\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"fitness\":267.72,\"delta_pct\":-13.79,\"vs_baseline\":-5.34,\"fmax_mhz\":114.04,\"ipc_coremark\":0.000002,\"cycles\":4259699,\"iterations\":10,\"lut4\":5901,\"ff\":2227,\"seeds\":[114.04,122.97,111.92],\"formal_passed\":true,\"cosim_passed\":true,\"error\":null,\"implementation_notes\":\"\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-07-10T20:33:22.624502Z\",\"slot\":1,\"round_id\":2,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r2s1 (regression, -13.79%): A radix-2 iterative divider that holds the in-order pipeline for its full multi-cycle latency can lose more CoreMark throughput than removing divide operators from the EX cone gains in timing, so divider frequency and stall cost must be measured before coupling DIV/REM to a global EX hold.\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-001-r3s0\",\"title\":\"Share a native-width RV32M multiplier\",\"category\":\"micro_opt\",\"motivation\":\"The predictor-enhanced bench core has already recovered the important\\nCoreMark control-flow bubbles, but it uses 10554 LUT4s and its ALU still\\ninstantiates three full-width multiplier expressions for the MUL family.\\nThe previous sharing attempt used a 33x33 signed multiplier and reduced\\nFmax substantially, so the next optimization should preserve the FPGA's\\nnative 32x32 mapping rather than widen the arithmetic cone.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The predictor-enhanced bench core has already recovered the important\\nCoreMark control-flow bubbles, but it uses 10554 LUT4s and its ALU still\\ninstantiates three full-width multiplier expressions for the MUL family.\\nThe previous sharing attempt used a 33x33 signed multiplier and reduced\\nFmax substantially, so the next optimization should preserve the FPGA's\\nnative 32x32 mapping rather than widen the arithmetic cone.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Replace the parallel signed-signed, unsigned-unsigned, and signed-unsigned\\nproducts with one native 32x32 unsigned product. Use sign-dependent high\\nhalf correction terms to implement MULH and MULHSU exactly, while taking\\nthe unchanged low half for MUL and the unsigned high half for MULHU. Keep\\nthe existing one-cycle EX interface, divider behavior, RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\\nsubstitutions, and RVFI timing unchanged. This should remove redundant\\nmultiplier hardware and routing pressure without the critical-path penalty\\nof the prior 33x33 implementation, improving Fmax and/or fitting margin\\nwhile preserving CoreMark IPC.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":3,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/alu.sv\",\"description\":\"Use one native-width unsigned 32x32 product and sign-correction arithmetic for exact MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU results; retain ALTOPS and divider semantics.\"}]},\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":3,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/alu.sv\",\"description\":\"Use one native-width unsigned 32x32 product and sign-correction arithmetic for exact MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU results; retain ALTOPS and divider semantics.\"}],\"outcome\":\"improvement\",\"fitness\":317.32,\"delta_pct\":2.18,\"vs_baseline\":12.2,\"fmax_mhz\":135.17,\"ipc_coremark\":0.000002,\"cycles\":4259699,\"iterations\":10,\"lut4\":10283,\"ff\":1895,\"seeds\":[135.17,123.08,138.24],\"formal_passed\":true,\"cosim_passed\":true,\"error\":null,\"implementation_notes\":\"\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-07-10T20:49:37.121156Z\",\"slot\":0,\"round_id\":3,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r3s0 (improvement, +2.18%): One native-width unsigned `a * b` plus sign-dependent high-half correction terms implements RV32M `MUL`, `MULH`, `MULHU`, and `MULHSU` without the timing penalty of a widened multiplier, preserving CoreMark throughput while reducing redundant multiply hardware.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
