{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -c 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r5s1\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-001-r7s0\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-003-r1s2\\\")' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-003-r1s2\",\"title\":\"Early static backward-branch prediction\",\"category\":\"predictor\",\"motivation\":\"The bench core resolves conditional branches and jumps in EX, then flushes\\nyounger work and redirects the fetch PC. CoreMark contains many tight loops,\\nso taken backward branches repeatedly pay this avoidable redirect penalty.\\nThe fixture is already close to its LUT budget, making a table-based BTB/BHT\\na riskier tradeoff than a small decode-only predictor.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The bench core resolves conditional branches and jumps in EX, then flushes\\nyounger work and redirects the fetch PC. CoreMark contains many tight loops,\\nso taken backward branches repeatedly pay this avoidable redirect penalty.\\nThe fixture is already close to its LUT budget, making a table-based BTB/BHT\\na riskier tradeoff than a small decode-only predictor.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Add an IF-stage static control-flow predictor that predicts valid backward\\nconditional branches taken and predicts direct JAL instructions to their\\nimmediately computed targets; leave forward branches and JALR unpredicted.\\nCarry the predicted next PC through ID/EX and make EX redirect only when the\\nresolved next PC differs from the prediction, recovering to the actual\\ntarget or fall-through PC on a miss. This should remove most EX redirect\\nbubbles from CoreMark loop branches with little area and timing overhead.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":4,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Compute aligned B/J immediates from the fetched instruction and select a predicted target for backward conditional branches and direct JALs before the EX redirect path.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Extend the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles with prediction-valid/target metadata needed to compare the prediction against the resolved next PC.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch the IF-stage prediction metadata alongside the decoded instruction so EX can validate or recover from the prediction.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Compare the resolved branch/jump next PC with the carried prediction and issue redirects only on mispredictions, preserving trap and RVFI pc_next semantics.\"}]},\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":4,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Compute aligned B/J immediates from the fetched instruction and select a predicted target for backward conditional branches and direct JALs before the EX redirect path.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Extend the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles with prediction-valid/target metadata needed to compare the prediction against the resolved next PC.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch the IF-stage prediction metadata alongside the decoded instruction so EX can validate or recover from the prediction.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Compare the resolved branch/jump next PC with the carried prediction and issue redirects only on mispredictions, preserving trap and RVFI pc_next semantics.\"}],\"outcome\":\"improvement\",\"fitness\":310.56,\"delta_pct\":9.81,\"vs_baseline\":9.81,\"fmax_mhz\":132.29,\"ipc_coremark\":0.000002,\"cycles\":4259699,\"iterations\":10,\"lut4\":10554,\"ff\":1897,\"seeds\":[128.47,132.29,133.98],\"formal_passed\":true,\"cosim_passed\":true,\"error\":null,\"implementation_notes\":\"\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-07-10T20:04:27.584939Z\",\"slot\":2,\"round_id\":1,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r1s2 (improvement, +9.81%): A small IF-stage predictor for backward conditional branches and direct JALs, with prediction metadata carried through ID/EX and EX redirects only on next-PC mismatch, removes most CoreMark loop redirect bubbles without the area cost of a BTB/BHT.\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r5s1\",\"title\":\"Retimed two-phase execute pipeline\",\"category\":\"structural\",\"motivation\":\"The current critical path starts at the ID/EX register and traverses the\\nEX forwarding muxes, ALU operand selection, and the 32-bit arithmetic cone\\nbefore reaching EX/MEM.  The successful static predictor already removes\\nmost loop redirect bubbles, while the earlier fetch-buffer and decode-\\nredirect structures lost more Fmax than they gained in IPC.  A physical\\nexecute-stage retiming therefore offers a more direct way to improve the\\nfitness product without adding predictor state or widening the interface.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The current critical path starts at the ID/EX register and traverses the\\nEX forwarding muxes, ALU operand selection, and the 32-bit arithmetic cone\\nbefore reaching EX/MEM.  The successful static predictor already removes\\nmost loop redirect bubbles, while the earlier fetch-buffer and decode-\\nredirect structures lost more Fmax than they gained in IPC.  A physical\\nexecute-stage retiming therefore offers a more direct way to improve the\\nfitness product without adding predictor state or widening the interface.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Split execute into an operand/forwarding EX1 stage and an arithmetic/control\\nEX2 stage, with a pipeline register between them.  EX1 captures the selected\\nforwarded operands, immediate, PC, control, and prediction metadata; EX2\\nperforms the ALU operation, memory-address calculation, branch or jump\\nresolution, and alignment checks, then drives the existing EX/MEM contract.\\nAdd age-correct EX2-to-EX2 and MEM/WB bypasses and stall/flush control so\\ndependent ALU instructions still sustain one instruction per cycle, while\\nload-use and dmem stalls retain precise RVFI validity and ordering.  The\\nextra register should remove the forwarding/operand mux delay from the\\narithmetic timing path and raise Fmax, with only the already-predicted\\ncontrol-flow cases avoiding an added redirect penalty.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":6,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add the internal EX1 pipeline bundle needed to carry forwarded operands, control, PC, and static-prediction metadata across the new execute-stage boundary while retaining the existing EX/MEM and RVFI bundle fields.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Retiming the execute logic into operand-capture EX1 and arithmetic/control EX2 registers, with precise forwarding, branch prediction comparison, misalignment traps, dmem-stall holds, and the unchanged EX/MEM output contract.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Recompute load-use, redirect flush, and dmem backpressure arbitration for the additional execute stage so bubbles and holds preserve age order and do not duplicate or skip RVFI retirements.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire the retimed execute-stage controls and forwarding sources through the existing five-stage top-level datapath without changing the external buses or single-channel RVFI port set.\"}]},\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":6,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add the internal EX1 pipeline bundle needed to carry forwarded operands, control, PC, and static-prediction metadata across the new execute-stage boundary while retaining the existing EX/MEM and RVFI bundle fields.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Retiming the execute logic into operand-capture EX1 and arithmetic/control EX2 registers, with precise forwarding, branch prediction comparison, misalignment traps, dmem-stall holds, and the unchanged EX/MEM output contract.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Recompute load-use, redirect flush, and dmem backpressure arbitration for the additional execute stage so bubbles and holds preserve age order and do not duplicate or skip RVFI retirements.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire the retimed execute-stage controls and forwarding sources through the existing five-stage top-level datapath without changing the external buses or single-channel RVFI port set.\"}],\"outcome\":\"improvement\",\"fitness\":396.37,\"delta_pct\":24.91,\"vs_baseline\":40.15,\"fmax_mhz\":172.03,\"ipc_coremark\":0.000002,\"cycles\":4340155,\"iterations\":10,\"lut4\":10388,\"ff\":2076,\"seeds\":[179.99,172.03,166.97],\"formal_passed\":true,\"cosim_passed\":true,\"error\":null,\"implementation_notes\":\"\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-07-10T21:45:33.543025Z\",\"slot\":1,\"round_id\":5,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r5s1 (improvement, +24.91%): Splitting execute into an operand/forwarding EX1 and arithmetic/control EX2 stage can materially improve CoreMark fitness by removing the forwarding muxes from the ALU cone, provided EX2-to-EX1 age-ordered bypasses and precise bubble/hold control preserve dependent ALU, load-use, and dmem-stall ordering.\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-001-r7s0\",\"title\":\"Remove redundant MEM/WB forwarding leg\",\"category\":\"micro_opt\",\"motivation\":\"The retimed core already captures forwarded operands in EX1, but its\\nforwarding network still performs a third age comparison and selects a\\nMEM/WB value.  The register file has an explicit write-first WB bypass, and\\nEX1 re-reads the held instruction's registers, so this MEM/WB leg duplicates\\na value that is already available at the register-file read ports.  Removing\\nthe duplicate compare and mux should reduce EX1 capture delay and routing\\nwithout changing the arithmetic or memory pipeline.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The retimed core already captures forwarded operands in EX1, but its\\nforwarding network still performs a third age comparison and selects a\\nMEM/WB value.  The register file has an explicit write-first WB bypass, and\\nEX1 re-reads the held instruction's registers, so this MEM/WB leg duplicates\\na value that is already available at the register-file read ports.  Removing\\nthe duplicate compare and mux should reduce EX1 capture delay and routing\\nwithout changing the arithmetic or memory pipeline.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Eliminate the MEM/WB source from the EX1 forwarding priority, retaining only\\nthe freshest EX2 result, the EX/MEM result or load value, and the\\nwrite-first register-file read as the fallback.  Simplify the forwarding\\ninterfaces and wiring so the WB value is supplied solely by the existing\\nregister-file bypass.  Because WB writes are visible combinationally and\\nEX1 re-reads operands when an instruction is held, dependent ALU, load-use,\\nbus-stall, redirect, RVFI, and x0 behavior should remain unchanged while\\nthe operand-capture path becomes smaller and faster.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":2,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Remove the MEM/WB equality comparison and forwarding selection while preserving EX2-over-EX/MEM age priority and x0 suppression.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Simplify the EX1 operand mux inputs to use EX2, EX/MEM, or the write-first register-file read, with no functional change to load forwarding or stalls.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Update forwarding wiring to drop the redundant MEM/WB forwarding source while retaining the existing WB write-first regfile path and top-level RVFI contract.\"}]},\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":2,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Remove the MEM/WB equality comparison and forwarding selection while preserving EX2-over-EX/MEM age priority and x0 suppression.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Simplify the EX1 operand mux inputs to use EX2, EX/MEM, or the write-first register-file read, with no functional change to load forwarding or stalls.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Update forwarding wiring to drop the redundant MEM/WB forwarding source while retaining the existing WB write-first regfile path and top-level RVFI contract.\"}],\"outcome\":\"improvement\",\"fitness\":480.9,\"delta_pct\":21.33,\"vs_baseline\":70.04,\"fmax_mhz\":208.72,\"ipc_coremark\":0.000002,\"cycles\":4340155,\"iterations\":10,\"lut4\":10135,\"ff\":2076,\"seeds\":[214.55,208.72,203.96],\"formal_passed\":true,\"cosim_passed\":true,\"error\":null,\"implementation_notes\":\"\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-07-10T22:14:26.680923Z\",\"slot\":0,\"round_id\":7,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r7s0 (improvement, +21.33%): Removing a redundant MEM/WB forwarding compare and mux improved CoreMark because EX1's write-first register-file reread already exposes WB data, so forwarding should retain only younger values unavailable at the read ports while preserving EX2-over-EX/MEM priority.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -c 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r9s1\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r10s1\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r8s1\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r7s1\\\") | {id,title,motivation,hypothesis,changes,outcome,delta_pct,implementation_notes,error}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -c 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r9s1\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r10s1\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r8s1\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r7s1\\\") | {id,title,motivation,hypothesis,changes,outcome,delta_pct,implementation_notes,error}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r7s1\",\"title\":\"Elastic in-order memory backend\",\"motivation\":\"The retimed EX1/EX2 pipeline now has useful independent work available, but\\nthe current MEM control still freezes it whenever io_dmemReady is low for a\\nload or store.  The benchmark injects roughly 22% data-bus stalls, so this\\ncoupling directly reduces CoreMark iterations per cycle.  The previous store\\nbuffer attempt regressed because queue occupancy remained on the global\\ndmem-stall path; the next design should decouple waiting memory requests from\\nyounger non-memory work while retaining strict retirement order.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The retimed EX1/EX2 pipeline now has useful independent work available, but\\nthe current MEM control still freezes it whenever io_dmemReady is low for a\\nload or store.  The benchmark injects roughly 22% data-bus stalls, so this\\ncoupling directly reduces CoreMark iterations per cycle.  The previous store\\nbuffer attempt regressed because queue occupancy remained on the global\\ndmem-stall path; the next design should decouple waiting memory requests from\\nyounger non-memory work while retaining strict retirement order.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Add a small age-ordered completion queue after EX2 together with a dedicated\\nmemory-request slot.  A load or store occupies the memory slot until its\\ndmem handshake completes, while younger non-memory instructions can execute\\nand wait in the completion queue instead of freezing the whole backend.\\nBlock younger memory operations and consumers of a pending load, and apply\\nbackpressure only when the queue is full.  Retire and expose RVFI strictly\\nfrom the oldest queue entry, with queue-aware forwarding for values that are\\ncomplete but not yet retired.  This should hide a meaningful fraction of\\nrandom dmem stalls without adding logic to the IF critical path or changing\\nthe external bus and single-channel RVFI contracts.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":5,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Define the age-ordered completion-entry and pending-memory metadata needed by the elastic backend while preserving the existing RVFI payload fields.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate the memory request slot and completion queue, making the oldest entry the sole WB/RVFI retirement source without changing top-level IO.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Separate memory-request capture, dmem-ready handshake, and load-response completion so a waiting request no longer freezes unrelated EX work.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace the global memory-stall coupling with queue-full, pending-load dependency, and younger-memory ordering controls.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Add age-correct forwarding from completed-but-unretired queue entries while keeping pending-load results unavailable until the response arrives.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/wb_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Drive register writes and retirement data from the oldest completed queue entry exactly once, preserving RVFI order and memory metadata.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Define the age-ordered completion-entry and pending-memory metadata needed by the elastic backend while preserving the existing RVFI payload fields.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate the memory request slot and completion queue, making the oldest entry the sole WB/RVFI retirement source without changing top-level IO.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Separate memory-request capture, dmem-ready handshake, and load-response completion so a waiting request no longer freezes unrelated EX work.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace the global memory-stall coupling with queue-full, pending-load dependency, and younger-memory ordering controls.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Add age-correct forwarding from completed-but-unretired queue entries while keeping pending-load results unavailable until the response arrives.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/wb_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Drive register writes and retirement data from the oldest completed queue entry exactly once, preserving RVFI order and memory metadata.\"}],\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"delta_pct\":null,\"implementation_notes\":null,\"error\":\"formal_failed: causal_ch0\\n19:23:02 [cover] summary:   reached cover statement rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__cover_cover_stmts_vh_1_49 at cover_stmts.vh:1.23-1.55 step 20\\nSBY 19:23:02 [cover] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\\nSBY 19:23:02 [liveness_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:07  Status: passed\\nSBY 19:23:02 [liveness_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=0)\\nSBY 19:23:02 [liveness_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\\nSBY 19:23:02 [liveness_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:08 (8)\\nSBY 19:23:02 [liveness_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:05 (5)\\nSBY 19:23:02 [liveness_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\\nSBY 19:23:02 [liveness_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\\nSBY 19:23:02 [liveness_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\\nmake: Target `all' not remade because of errors.\\n\\nFormal: 6 passed, 47 failed\\nFailed: causal_ch0 ill_ch0 insn_add_ch0 insn_addi_ch0 insn_and_ch0 insn_andi_ch0 insn_auipc_ch0 insn_beq_ch0 insn_bge_ch0 insn_bgeu_ch0 insn_blt_ch0 insn_bltu_ch0 insn_bne_ch0 insn_div_ch0 insn_divu_ch0 insn_jal_ch0 insn_jalr_c