 Assumptions are unsatisfiable!\\nSBY 19:22:55 [causal_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Status: PREUNSAT\\nSBY 19:22:55 [causal_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=1)\\nSBY 19:22:55 [causal_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: ERROR\\nSBY 19:22:55 [causal_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:01 (1)\\nSBY 19:22:55 [causal_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:01 (1)\\nSBY 19:22:55 [causal_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned ERROR\\nSBY 19:22:55 [causal_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\\nSBY 19:22:55 [causal_ch0] DONE (ERROR, rc=16)\\n\\nFull run log: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-luna-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-002-r7s1/formal/last_run-53729.log\\nPer-check logs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-luna-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-002-r7s1/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-53729/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r8s1\",\"title\":\"Retimed two-phase memory response\",\"motivation\":\"The retimed EX1/EX2 core has already removed the forwarding muxes from the\\narithmetic critical path, and the failed queue experiments show that broad\\nbackend decoupling is too risky.  The remaining memory-stage path combines\\nthe FPGA data-memory read, byte extraction, sign extension, and MEM/WB\\ncapture in one timing interval.  CoreMark uses enough loads for this path to\\naffect both Fmax and the load-use schedule.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The retimed EX1/EX2 core has already removed the forwarding muxes from the\\narithmetic critical path, and the failed queue experiments show that broad\\nbackend decoupling is too risky.  The remaining memory-stage path combines\\nthe FPGA data-memory read, byte extraction, sign extension, and MEM/WB\\ncapture in one timing interval.  CoreMark uses enough loads for this path to\\naffect both Fmax and the load-use schedule.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Split the memory stage into a registered request stage and a registered\\nresponse/format stage.  The request stage drives the existing dmem address,\\nwrite data, and byte enables and holds precisely when io_dmemReady is low;\\nthe response stage first captures raw read data and memory metadata, then\\nperforms byte-lane extraction and sign extension into the existing writeback\\npayload.  Pipeline the stages at one request per cycle so zero-wait memory\\nretains throughput while the added register isolates the FPGA memory output\\nfrom the load-formatting cone.  Update hazards and valid/hold sequencing so\\nstores, loads, load-use forwarding, RVFI metadata, and rvfi_order remain\\nage-correct under both ready and stalled data buses.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":5,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add request/response pipeline payload fields needed to carry memory operation metadata and raw read data across the retimed backend stages.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace the single memory combinational path with a ready-aware request register and a response register that performs load extraction and writeback payload formation.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Recompute data-bus stall, load-use, and pipeline hold/bubble controls for the extra memory-response latency without allowing duplicate memory effects.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire the retimed memory-stage controls and forwarding timing while preserving the existing external buses and single-channel RVFI contract.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add request/response pipeline payload fields needed to carry memory operation metadata and raw read data across the retimed backend stages.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace the single memory combinational path with a ready-aware request register and a response register that performs load extraction and writeback payload formation.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Recompute data-bus stall, load-use, and pipeline hold/bubble controls for the extra memory-response latency without allowing duplicate memory effects.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire the retimed memory-stage controls and forwarding timing while preserving the existing external buses and single-channel RVFI contract.\"}],\"outcome\":\"placement_failed\",\"delta_pct\":null,\"implementation_notes\":null,\"error\":\"placement_failed\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r9s1\",\"title\":\"Two-read-port operand snapshot pipeline\",\"motivation\":\"The current pipeline exposes four combinational register-file read ports:\\ntwo for decode and two more for EX1 to reread an instruction held in\\nID/EX.  That duplicated read topology consumes LUTs and adds fanout and\\nmuxing around the operand-forwarding boundary, which is especially costly\\nwhen the design is already close to the Tang Nano LUT budget.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The current pipeline exposes four combinational register-file read ports:\\ntwo for decode and two more for EX1 to reread an instruction held in\\nID/EX.  That duplicated read topology consumes LUTs and adds fanout and\\nmuxing around the operand-forwarding boundary, which is especially costly\\nwhen the design is already close to the Tang Nano LUT budget.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Remove the dedicated EX1 register-file reread ports and make the ID/EX\\noperand snapshot authoritative.  When ID/EX is held for a load-use or\\ndmem stall, refresh only its stored rs1/rs2 values from the existing two\\ndecode read ports, including their write-first WB behavior; otherwise\\ncapture operands normally.  EX1 will still apply the existing age-ordered\\nEX2 and EX/MEM forwarding, while all source addresses and RVFI fields stay\\nunchanged.  This should reduce register-file replication and operand-path\\nfanout without adding a new critical datapath stage.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":5,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/reg_file.sv\",\"description\":\"Collapse the register file from four combinational read ports to the existing two decode ports, retaining x0 behavior and write-first WB bypassing.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Refresh the held ID/EX operand snapshots from the decode read ports on every stall so delayed load-use and dmem-stall cases see newly retired register values.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Use the ID/EX operand snapshots as the non-forwarded EX1 inputs and remove the redundant EX1 register-file reread interface while preserving EX2-over-EX/MEM forwarding priority.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Reconnect the reduced register-file interface and operand path without changing the external buses, pipeline retirement boundary, or single-channel RVFI contract.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/reg_file.sv\",\"description\":\"Collapse the register file from four combinational read ports to the existing two decode ports, retaining x0 behavior and write-first WB bypassing.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Refresh the held ID/EX operand snapshots from the decode read ports on every stall so delayed load-use and dmem-stall cases see newly retired register values.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Use the ID/EX operand snapshots as the non-forwarded EX1 inputs and remove the redundant EX1 register-file reread interface while preserving EX2-over-EX/MEM forwarding priority.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Reconnect the reduced register-file interface and operand path without changing the external buses, pipeline retirement boundary, or single-channel RVFI contract.\"}],\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"delta_pct\":-56.76,\"implementation_notes\":\"\",\"error\":null}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r10s1\",\"title\":\"Replicate register-file read banks\",\"motivation\":\"The current high-performing pipeline needs four combinational register-file\\nreads: two for decode and two for EX1's delayed operand reread.  Keeping all\\nfour reads in one physical array increases routing fanout from every\\nregister bit and can make the operand path placement-sensitive near the\\nTang Nano LUT budget.  The recent two-read-port experiment showed that\\nremoving ports moves too much timing work into decode and writeback, so the\\nbetter structural target is physical locality without changing the logical\\ninterface or operand timing.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The current high-performing pipeline needs four combinational register-file\\nreads: two for decode and two for EX1's delayed operand reread.  Keeping all\\nfour reads in one physical array increases routing fanout from every\\nregister bit and can make the operand path placement-sensitive near the\\nTang Nano LUT budget.  The recent two-read-port experiment showed that\\nremoving ports moves too much timing work into decode and writeback, so the\\nbetter structural target is physical locality without changing the logical\\ninterface or operand timing.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Physically replicate the 32x32 register storage into an ID-read copy and an\\nEX1-read copy, with reset and every architectural write applied to both\\ncopies.  Keep the existing two read ports on each copy, including x0\\nhardwiring and write-first WB bypasses, so decode and EX1 retain their\\ncurrent independent read timing and RVFI-visible values.  Partitioning the\\nread mux trees and register-bit fanout should improve placement and Fmax\\nwhile spending flip-flops instead of adding a new forwarding mux, pipeline\\nstage, or memory-side queue.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":4,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/reg_file.sv\",\"description\":\"Duplicate the physical register array into decode-read and EX1-read copies, synchronize reset and WB writes to both, and preserve the existing four logical read ports with write-first and x0 behavior.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/reg_file.sv\",\"description\":\"Duplicate the physical register array into decode-read and EX1-read copies, synchronize reset and WB writes to both, and preserve the existing four logical read ports with write-first and x0 behavior.\"}],\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"delta_pct\":-52.32,\"implementation_notes\":\"\",\"error\":null}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
