{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r13s1.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r13s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r13s1\ntitle: \"Isolate the RV32M multiply pipeline\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current EX2 ALU structurally contains a full-width multiply alongside\n  the ordinary integer datapath.  The successful EX1/EX2 retiming shortened\n  the forwarding-to-ALU path, but ordinary CoreMark instructions still pay\n  the shared M-operation mux and routing footprint.  A dedicated, narrow\n  multiply lane is a more targeted structural change than another global\n  queue or front-end buffer.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split RV32M multiplication from the base ALU into a small registered\n  multiply lane.  Launch MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU operands from EX1, capture the\n  result through a one-cycle M-unit pipeline, and add precise interlock and\n  forwarding only for the in-flight multiply and its consumers; ordinary\n  ALU, branch, load/store, and divide instructions continue through the\n  existing EX2 path.  Remove multiply hardware from the normal ALU instance\n  while retaining exact signed high-half correction, RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n  behavior, RV32M corner cases, in-order retirement, and unchanged external\n  buses and RVFI ports.  The isolated lane should reduce the normal EX2\n  cone and routing pressure while imposing latency only on the relatively\n  infrequent multiply dependency chains.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Refactor the base ALU so multiply operations are supplied by a separate M-unit interface, preserving the formal ALTOPS branch and exact RV32M arithmetic semantics for the dedicated lane.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add the registered multiply execution lane, select its completion into EX/MEM, and preserve EX2 control-flow, memory, misalignment, forwarding, and RVFI metadata behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add precise multiply busy and dependency interlocks so the in-order pipeline cannot overwrite or consume an incomplete M result, without stalling unrelated instructions unnecessarily.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire multiply start/completion and the age-ordered multiply forwarding source through the existing single-issue datapath without changing top-level IO.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
