nFull run log: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-luna-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-002-r13s1/formal/last_run-6736.log\\nPer-check logs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-luna-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-002-r13s1/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-6736/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 13, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r13s1 (broken, n/a): A forked registered MUL completion lane cannot expose only a result/rd bypass while suppressing the normal EX2 entry; its valid bit, writeback payload, PC-next, and RVFI metadata must transfer atomically or `pc_fwd` and register checks diverge.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.category==\\\"structural\\\") | [.id,.title,.outcome,(.fitness // \\\"\\\"),(.fmax_mhz // \\\"\\\"),(.delta_pct // \\\"\\\")] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl && jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r5s1\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-001-r7s0\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r8s1\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r13s1\\\") | {id,title,category,outcome,fitness,fmax_mhz,delta_pct,motivation,hypothesis,changes,implementation_notes,error}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.category==\\\"structural\\\") | [.id,.title,.outcome,(.fitness // \\\"\\\"),(.fmax_mhz // \\\"\\\"),(.delta_pct // \\\"\\\")] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl && jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r5s1\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-001-r7s0\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r8s1\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r13s1\\\") | {id,title,category,outcome,fitness,fmax_mhz,delta_pct,motivation,hypothesis,changes,implementation_notes,error}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20260710-002-r1s1\tAdd a decoupled instruction prefetch FIFO\tregression\t270.21\t127.15\t-4.46\nhyp-20260710-002-r2s1\tDecouple long-latency M execution\tregression\t267.72\t114.04\t-13.79\nhyp-20260710-002-r3s1\tAdd a minimal elastic fetch skid buffer\tregression\t278.09\t119.99\t-10.46\nhyp-20260710-002-r4s1\tResolve control flow in decode\tbroken\t\t\t\nhyp-20260710-002-r5s1\tRetimed two-phase execute pipeline\timprovement\t396.37\t172.03\t24.91\nhyp-20260710-002-r6s1\tAdd a one-entry nonblocking store buffer\tregression\t211.24\t90.98\t-46.71\nhyp-20260710-002-r7s1\tElastic in-order memory backend\tbroken\t\t\t\nhyp-20260710-002-r8s1\tRetimed two-phase memory response\tplacement_failed\t\t\t\nhyp-20260710-002-r9s1\tTwo-read-port operand snapshot pipeline\tregression\t207.92\t90.24\t-56.76\nhyp-20260710-002-r10s1\tReplicate register-file read banks\tregression\t229.28\t99.51\t-52.32\nhyp-20260710-002-r11s1\tCompact memory-sideband pipeline\tregression\t337.15\t146.33\t-29.89\nhyp-20260710-002-r12s1\tBank the register file for shallower read muxes\tregression\t297.27\t129.02\t-38.18\nhyp-20260710-002-r13s1\tIsolate the RV32M multiply pipeline\tbroken\t\t\t\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r5s1\",\n  \"title\": \"Retimed two-phase execute pipeline\",\n  \"category\": \"structural\",\n  \"outcome\": \"improvement\",\n  \"fitness\": 396.37,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 172.03,\n  \"delta_pct\": 24.91,\n  \"motivation\": \"The current critical path starts at the ID/EX register and traverses the\\nEX forwarding muxes, ALU operand selection, and the 32-bit arithmetic cone\\nbefore reaching EX/MEM.  The successful static predictor already removes\\nmost loop redirect bubbles, while the earlier fetch-buffer and decode-\\nredirect structures lost more Fmax than they gained in IPC.  A physical\\nexecute-stage retiming therefore offers a more direct way to improve the\\nfitness product without adding predictor state or widening the interface.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The current critical path starts at the ID/EX register and traverses the\\nEX forwarding muxes, ALU operand selection, and the 32-bit arithmetic cone\\nbefore reaching EX/MEM.  The successful static predictor already removes\\nmost loop redirect bubbles, while the earlier fetch-buffer and decode-\\nredirect structures lost more Fmax than they gained in IPC.  A physical\\nexecute-stage retiming therefore offers a more direct way to improve the\\nfitness product without adding predictor state or widening the interface.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Split execute into an operand/forwarding EX1 stage and an arithmetic/control\\nEX2 stage, with a pipeline register between them.  EX1 captures the selected\\nforwarded operands, immediate, PC, control, and prediction metadata; EX2\\nperforms the ALU operation, memory-address calculation, branch or jump\\nresolution, and alignment checks, then drives the existing EX/MEM contract.\\nAdd age-correct EX2-to-EX2 and MEM/WB bypasses and stall/flush control so\\ndependent ALU instructions still sustain one instruction per cycle, while\\nload-use and dmem stalls retain precise RVFI validity and ordering.  The\\nextra register should remove the forwarding/operand mux delay from the\\narithmetic timing path and raise Fmax, with only the already-predicted\\ncontrol-flow cases avoiding an added redirect penalty.\\n\",\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"fitness_delta_pct\": 6,\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    \"changes\": [\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Add the internal EX1 pipeline bundle needed to carry forwarded operands, control, PC, and static-prediction metadata across the new execute-stage boundary while retaining the existing EX/MEM and RVFI bundle fields.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Retiming the execute logic into operand-capture EX1 and arithmetic/control EX2 registers, with precise forwarding, branch prediction comparison, misalignment traps, dmem-stall holds, and the unchanged EX/MEM output contract.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Recompute load-use, redirect flush, and dmem backpressure arbitration for the additional execute stage so bubbles and holds preserve age order and do not duplicate or skip RVFI retirements.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Wire the retimed execute-stage controls and forwarding sources through the existing five-stage top-level datapath without changing the external buses or single-channel RVFI port set.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Add the internal EX1 pipeline bundle needed to carry forwarded operands, control, PC, and static-prediction metadata across the new execute-stage boundary while retaining the existing EX/MEM and RVFI bundle fields.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Retiming the execute logic into operand-capture EX1 and arithmetic/control EX2 registers, with precise forwarding, branch prediction comparison, misalignment traps, dmem-stall holds, and the unchanged EX/MEM output contract.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Recompute load-use, redirect flush, and dmem backpressure arbitration for the additional execute stage so bubbles and holds preserve age order and do not duplicate or skip RVFI retirements.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Wire the retimed execute-stage controls and forwarding sources through the existing five-stage top-level datapath without changing the external buses or single-channel RVFI port set.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\",\n  \"error\": null\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r7s0\",\n  \"title\": \"Remove redundant MEM/WB forwarding leg\",\n  \"category\": \"micro_opt\",\n  \"outcome\": \"improvement\",\n  \"fitness\": 480.9,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 208.72,\n  \"delta_pct\": 21.33,\n  \"motivation\": \"The retimed core already captures forwarded operands in EX1, but its\\nforwarding network still performs a third age comparison and selects a\\nMEM/WB value.  The register file has an explicit write-first WB bypass, and\\nEX1 re-reads the held instruction's registers, so this MEM/WB leg duplicates\\na value that is already available at the register-file read ports.  Removing\\nthe duplicate compare and mux should reduce EX1 capture delay and routing\\nwithout changing the arithmetic or memory pipeline.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The retimed core already captures forwarded operands in EX1, but its\\nforwarding network still performs a third age comparison and selects a\\nMEM/WB value.  The register file has an explicit write-first WB bypass, and\\nEX1 re-reads the held instruction's registers, so this MEM/WB leg duplicates\\na value that is already available at the register-file read ports.  Removing\\nthe duplicate compare and mux should reduce EX1 capture delay and routing\\nwithout changing the arithmetic or memory pipeline.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Eliminate the MEM/WB source from the EX1 forwarding priority, retaining only\\nthe freshest EX2 result, the EX/MEM result or load value, and the\\nwrite-first register-file read as the fallback.  Simplify the forwarding\\ninterfaces and wiring so the WB value is supplied solely by the existing\\nregister-file bypass.  Because WB writes are visible combinationally and\\nEX1 re-reads operands when an instruction is held, dependent ALU, load-use,\\nbus-stall, redirect, RVFI, and x0 behavior should remain unchanged while\\nthe operand-capture path becomes smaller and faster.\\n\",\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"fitness_delta_pct\": 2,\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    \"changes\": [\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Remove the MEM/WB equality comparison and forwarding selection while preserving EX2-over-EX/MEM age priority and x0 suppression.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Simplify the EX1 operand mux inputs to use EX2, EX/MEM, or the write-first register-file read, with no functional change to load forwarding or stalls.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Update forwarding wiring to drop the redundant MEM/WB forwarding source while retaining the existing WB write-first regfile path and top-level RVFI contract.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Remove the MEM/WB equality comparison and forwarding selection while preserving EX2-over-EX/MEM age priority and x0 suppression.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Simplify the EX1 operand mux inputs to use EX2, EX/MEM, or the write-first register-file read, with no functional change to load forwarding or stalls.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Update forwarding wiring to drop the redundant MEM/WB forwarding source while retaining the existing WB write-first regfile path and top-level RVFI contract.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\",\n  \"error\": null\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r8s1\",\n  \"title\": \"Retimed two-phase memory response\",\n  \"category\": \"structural\",\n  \"outcome\": \"placement_failed\",\n  \"fitness\": null,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": null,\n  \"delta_pct\": null,\n  \"motivation\": \"The retimed EX1/EX2 core has already removed the forwarding muxes from the\\narithmetic critical path, and the failed queue experiments show that broad\\nbackend decoupling is too risky.  The remaining memory-stage path combines\\nthe FPGA data-memory read, byte extraction, sign extension, and MEM/WB\\ncapture in one timing interval.  CoreMark uses enough loads for this path to\\naffect both Fmax and the load-use schedule.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The retimed EX1/EX2 core has already removed the forwarding muxes from the\\narithmetic critical path, and the failed queue experiments show that broad\\nbackend decoupling is too risky.  The remaining memory-stage path combines\\nthe FPGA data-memory read, byte extraction, sign extension, and MEM/WB\\ncapture in one timing interval.  CoreMark uses enough loads for this path to\\naffect both Fmax and the load-use schedule.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Split the memory stage into a registered request stage and a registered\\nresponse/format stage.  The request stage drives the existing dmem address,\\nwrite data, and byte enables and holds precisely when io_dmemReady is low;\\nthe response stage first captures raw read data and memory metadata, then\\nperforms byte-lane extraction and sign extension into the existing writeback\\npayload.  Pipeline the stages at one request per cycle so zero-wait memory\\nretains throughput while the added register isolates the FPGA memory output\\nfrom the load-formatting cone.  Update hazards and valid/hold sequencing so\\nstores, loads, load-use forwarding, RVFI metadata, and rvfi_order remain\\nage-correct under both ready and stalled data buses.\\n\",