{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.category==\\\"structural\\\") | [.id,.title,.outcome,(.delta_pct // \\\"\\\"),(.fitness // \\\"\\\"),(.fmax_mhz // \\\"\\\"),(.implementation_notes // \\\"\\\"),(.lesson // \\\"\\\")] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20260710-002-r1s1\tAdd a decoupled instruction prefetch FIFO\tregression\t-4.46\t270.21\t127.15\t\t\nhyp-20260710-002-r2s1\tDecouple long-latency M execution\tregression\t-13.79\t267.72\t114.04\t\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r2s1 (regression, -13.79%): A radix-2 iterative divider that holds the in-order pipeline for its full multi-cycle latency can lose more CoreMark throughput than removing divide operators from the EX cone gains in timing, so divider frequency and stall cost must be measured before coupling DIV/REM to a global EX hold.\nhyp-20260710-002-r3s1\tAdd a minimal elastic fetch skid buffer\tregression\t-10.46\t278.09\t119.99\t\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r3s1 (regression, -10.46%): A registered one-entry IF skid buffer must preserve empty-slot or simultaneous pop/push bypass behavior and redirect refill latency, or its added fetch bubbles outweigh the isolated imem-stall cycles it hides.\nhyp-20260710-002-r4s1\tResolve control flow in decode\tbroken\t\t\t\t\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r4s1 (broken, n/a): Moving branch/JALR resolution into ID requires age-ordered operand bypasses and synchronized `resolved_valid`/redirect/flush/RVFI metadata, because a partial early redirect path can make the retired instruction stream, PC-next values, and register checks disagree even when the EX fallback remains.\nhyp-20260710-002-r5s1\tRetimed two-phase execute pipeline\timprovement\t24.91\t396.37\t172.03\t\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r5s1 (improvement, +24.91%): Splitting execute into an operand/forwarding EX1 and arithmetic/control EX2 stage can materially improve CoreMark fitness by removing the forwarding muxes from the ALU cone, provided EX2-to-EX1 age-ordered bypasses and precise bubble/hold control preserve dependent ALU, load-use, and dmem-stall ordering.\nhyp-20260710-002-r6s1\tAdd a one-entry nonblocking store buffer\tregression\t-46.71\t211.24\t90.98\t\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r6s1 (regression, -46.71%): A one-entry store buffer does not hide dmem stalls if queue occupancy still feeds the global `dmem_stall` and a combinational `store_dmem_valid` priority mux arbitrates the external bus, so capture/drain handshakes must be decoupled without lengthening the memory timing path or serializing later accesses.\nhyp-20260710-002-r7s1\tElastic in-order memory backend\tbroken\t\t\t\t\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r7s1 (broken, n/a): Moving the retirement boundary behind an elastic completion queue can make the causal RVFI/dmem assumptions unsatisfiable at a shallow step and cascade into every instruction check, so queue issue, memory-handshake, forwarding, and in-order retirement metadata must remain formally coherent before measuring stall hiding.\nhyp-20260710-002-r8s1\tRetimed two-phase memory response\tplacement_failed\t\t\t\t\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r8s1 (placement_failed, n/a): Registering the dmem request/response boundary is not free on this FPGA: carrying full `mem_req_t`/`mem_resp_t` payloads plus request-stall and extra load-forwarding control can make placement fail, so isolate the memory read/format cone with compact metadata and localized backpressure rather than a wide retimed backend.\nhyp-20260710-002-r9s1\tTwo-read-port operand snapshot pipeline\tregression\t-56.76\t207.92\t90.24\t\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r9s1 (regression, -56.76%): Replacing EX1's dedicated register-file reread with stall-gated ID/EX snapshot refresh shifted complexity into decode-address muxing and an added WB forwarding compare/mux, so removing read ports can severely hurt CoreMark unless the operand-path timing and stall behavior are measured together.\nhyp-20260710-002-r10s1\tReplicate register-file read banks\tregression\t-52.32\t229.28\t99.51\t\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r10s1 (regression, -52.32%): Replicating the full 32x32 register file for ID and EX1 preserves logical read timing but can make FPGA resource, reset, and write-fanout costs overwhelm locality gains, so bank replication needs post-place evidence that the shared read mux is the binding constraint.\nhyp-20260710-002-r11s1\tCompact memory-sideband pipeline\tregression\t-29.89\t337.15\t146.33\t\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r11s1 (regression, -29.89%): A combinational `mem_req_t`/`mem_retire_t` split does not by itself create physical isolation, and the added request-acceptance handshake can outweigh routing savings, so memory-sideband partitioning needs post-place critical-path and fanout evidence or a genuinely registered boundary.\nhyp-20260710-002-r12s1\tBank the register file for shallower read muxes\tregression\t-38.18\t297.27\t129.02\t\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r12s1 (regression, -38.18%): Banking one 32x32 register file into four 8-entry arrays did not guarantee shallower FPGA read muxes, while four combinational ports still paid bank-select, decode, and routing cost, so physical isolation must be confirmed before trading a simple array for banked RTL.\nhyp-20260710-002-r13s1\tIsolate the RV32M multiply pipeline\tbroken\t\t\t\t\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r13s1 (broken, n/a): A forked registered MUL completion lane cannot expose only a result/rd bypass while suppressing the normal EX2 entry; its valid bit, writeback payload, PC-next, and RVFI metadata must transfer atomically or `pc_fwd` and register checks diverge.\nhyp-20260710-002-r14s1\tRegister the compact load-response boundary\tregression\t-34.29\t316.02\t144.86\t\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r14s1 (regression, -34.29%): Even a compact registered dmem response can regress CoreMark when the added raw-word/metadata token changes load-use forwarding and stall control, so memory retiming must preserve one-cycle load throughput and atomic response/retirement alignment rather than merely narrow the payload.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
