{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r1s1.yaml\ngit status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r1s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r1s1\ntitle: \"Add a decoupled instruction prefetch FIFO\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current fetch stage has no buffering: whenever io_imemReady is low it\n  flushes the IF/ID view and stalls the whole front end, even if an earlier\n  instruction could still be consumed. The benchmark deliberately injects\n  roughly 22% instruction-bus stalls, making this front-end coupling a direct\n  IPC loss.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the single PC/IF-ID coupling with a small redirect-aware two-entry\n  instruction prefetch FIFO. Fetch into the FIFO whenever imemReady is high,\n  consume one entry per cycle into ID, and invalidate both entries on an EX\n  redirect while restarting the fetch pointer at the resolved target. This\n  should absorb isolated imem stalls and remove front-end bubbles without\n  changing retirement order or the external bus contract.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Implement a two-entry instruction prefetch FIFO with fetch and consume pointers, ready-aware capture, and redirect flushing/restart.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Reconnect the fetch-buffer output to the existing ID stage and preserve the current redirect, stall, and RVFI ordering behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Adjust front-end stall/flush arbitration so an imem stall stops FIFO filling but does not discard already buffered instructions.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
