{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r2s1.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r2s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r2s1\ntitle: \"Decouple long-latency M execution\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current five-stage core places full-width multiply and divide/remainder\n  arithmetic directly in the EX combinational cone. That cone is a poor\n  structural match for the Tang Nano timing budget: the best run is only\n  132.29 MHz while already using 10554 LUT4s, and the prior structural FIFO\n  attempt showed that extra front-end state can lower Fmax. CoreMark's hot\n  path is predominantly integer and memory work, so isolating infrequent\n  divide/remainder operations should improve timing without adding bubbles to\n  ordinary ALU instructions.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the combinational divide/remainder portion of the ALU with a shared\n  iterative radix-2 M execution unit. A DIV, DIVU, REM, or REMU entering EX\n  holds the in-order pipeline while the unit runs, then writes one RV32M-correct\n  result through the existing EX/MEM and RVFI paths; ordinary ALU, load/store,\n  branch, and multiply operations retain their single-cycle path. Add explicit\n  busy/done control and operand/result registers so the divider is removed from\n  the normal EX critical path, while preserving the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n  behavior and all trap, memory-stall, and retirement ordering invariants.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Remove the normal-path / and % operators for DIV/REM and expose a clean divider request/result interface while retaining the ALTOPS and exact RV32M corner-case behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Integrate the iterative M unit as a replay-safe multi-cycle EX operation, holding the instruction and preventing duplicate side effects until its result is ready.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add divider-busy backpressure that freezes younger pipeline state but allows the in-flight divide to complete and retire exactly once.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire divider start, busy, and completion signals through the pipeline without changing the external bus or single-channel RVFI contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
