{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The evidence points to a narrow front-end structural change: the existing two-entry FIFO regressed, while the current core still couples `io_imemReady` directly to pipeline bubbles. I’m selecting a minimal one-entry elastic fetch skid buffer to absorb isolated instruction stalls with less control/routing overhead, while preserving the proven static branch predictor."}}
