{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r3s1.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r3s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r3s1\ntitle: \"Add a minimal elastic fetch skid buffer\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current IF stage exposes the instruction bus directly to ID, so any\n  cycle with io_imemReady low flushes the fetched instruction and stalls the\n  front end. The benchmark injects roughly 22% instruction-bus stalls, making\n  this coupling an IPC cost. The earlier two-entry prefetch FIFO regressed,\n  suggesting that a smaller elastic structure is a better timing/area tradeoff\n  for the already predictor-enhanced core.\nhypothesis: |\n  Insert a single-entry registered fetch skid buffer between the instruction\n  bus and ID. Capture the fetched instruction, PC, and existing static\n  prediction metadata whenever the bus handshakes, consume the buffered entry\n  when ID can advance, and hold it across an imem stall instead of injecting a\n  front-end bubble. On an EX redirect, invalidate the entry and restart the\n  fetch address at the resolved target; preserve the existing load-use,\n  dmem-stall, RVFI ordering, and predictor-metadata rules. The one-entry\n  elastic path should recover isolated iStall cycles while avoiding the pointer\n  and mux overhead that hurt the prior two-entry FIFO's Fmax.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Replace the direct IF/ID coupling with a one-entry ready-aware fetch skid buffer that stores the PC, instruction, validity, and static prediction metadata, and flushes precisely on redirects.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Separate fetch-buffer fill stalls from back-end pipeline stalls so an imem bus stall preserves a buffered instruction without discarding valid front-end work.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Reconnect the elastic IF output and advance/hold controls while retaining the current static predictor, redirect priority, memory handshakes, and single-channel RVFI contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
