utput\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-luna-rep2\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r1s0 (broken, n/a): A zero-bubble EX/MEM load-data bypass must keep the extracted value, pipeline valid bits, and RVFI metadata aligned while `dmemReady` is low; merely holding the memory stage and suppressing redirects lets dependent instructions observe or retire mismatched register state.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r1s2 (improvement, +9.81%): A small IF-stage predictor for backward conditional branches and direct JALs, with prediction metadata carried through ID/EX and EX redirects only on next-PC mismatch, removes most CoreMark loop redirect bubbles without the area cost of a BTB/BHT.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r2s1 (regression, -13.79%): A radix-2 iterative divider that holds the in-order pipeline for its full multi-cycle latency can lose more CoreMark throughput than removing divide operators from the EX cone gains in timing, so divider frequency and stall cost must be measured before coupling DIV/REM to a global EX hold.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r2s2 (regression, -9.22%): A 16-entry BHT indexed only by `pc[5:2]` aliases CoreMark conditional branches, and weak-taken reset can turn the tuned static forward-not-taken behavior into costly early mispredictions, so tiny dynamic predictors need an aliasing-aware initialization and benchmark profile check.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r3s0 (improvement, +2.18%): One native-width unsigned `a * b` plus sign-dependent high-half correction terms implements RV32M `MUL`, `MULH`, `MULHU`, and `MULHSU` without the timing penalty of a widened multiplier, preserving CoreMark throughput while reducing redundant multiply hardware.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r3s1 (regression, -10.46%): A registered one-entry IF skid buffer must preserve empty-slot or simultaneous pop/push bypass behavior and redirect refill latency, or its added fetch bubbles outweigh the isolated imem-stall cycles it hides.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r3s2 (regression, -14.14%): Even a four-entry RAS can regress CoreMark when its combinational 4-way `ras_top` mux and return-form decode sit directly on the IF next-PC path, so return-prediction savings must be weighed against fetch timing before adding predictor state.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r4s0 (regression, -18.78%): Reusing the EX ALU sum for branch/JAL/JALR targets can make control-flow resolution depend on added operand-selection muxing, so removing target adders is not worthwhile if it lengthens the fetch redirect path and costs CoreMark throughput.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r4s1 (broken, n/a): Moving branch/JALR resolution into ID requires age-ordered operand bypasses and synchronized `resolved_valid`/redirect/flush/RVFI metadata, because a partial early redirect path can make the retired instruction stream, PC-next values, and register checks disagree even when the EX fallback remains.\\n- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r4s2 (regression, -22.88%): A tagged loop predictor that adds IF-stage tag/state lookup to suppress only final-iteration backward-branch redirects can cost more fetch performance than the occasional exit flush it removes, even when exact tags avoid BHT aliasing.\\n2:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-001-r1s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Zero-bubble load-use forwarding\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current five-stage pipeline unconditionally stalls one cycle for every\\\\nload-use dependency, even though the Tang Nano bench presents combinational\\\\nzero-wait read data. CoreMark has frequent load-dependent address, compare,\\\\nand arithmetic instructions, so this bubble directly reduces iterations per\\\\ncycle. The existing P&R report also shows the EX/MEM-to-EX forwarding path as\\\\nthe dominant timing path, making a dedicated load-data bypass a focused\\\\nhigh-value datapath optimization.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current five-stage pipeline unconditionally stalls one cycle for every\\\\nload-use dependency, even though the Tang Nano bench presents combinational\\\\nzero-wait read data. CoreMark has frequent load-dependent address, compare,\\\\nand arithmetic instructions, so this bubble directly reduces iterations per\\\\ncycle. The existing P&R report also shows the EX/MEM-to-EX forwarding path as\\\\nthe dominant timing path, making a dedicated load-data bypass a focused\\\\nhigh-value datapath optimization.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a dedicated EX/MEM load-data bypass from the memory stage's extracted\\\\nbyte/half/word value into the EX operand mux, and remove the unconditional\\\\nload-use bubble. When dmemReady is low, hold the dependent instruction and\\\\nsuppress redirects or side effects until the load completes; when it is high,\\\\nforward the load value directly and retire the dependent instruction without\\\\na bubble. This should preserve arbitrary bus-stall correctness while\\\\nimproving CoreMark IPC on the zero-wait FPGA path.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace the unconditional load-use bubble with replay-safe holding on an outstanding dmem stall, and provide control to block redirects while the dependent instruction waits.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a highest-priority EX/MEM load-result forwarding selection, with normal ALU and MEM/WB forwarding retained as fallbacks.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose the already sign/zero-extended load value as a combinational forwarding source while retaining the existing RVFI extraction and stall behavior.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Consume the load-data bypass and ensure a stalled dependent instruction cannot generate a redirect or architectural side effect before its operand is valid.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire the load-result bypass and dmem-stall qualification through the pipeline without changing the top-level IO or RVFI contract.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace the unconditional load-use bubble with replay-safe holding on an outstanding dmem stall, and provide control to block redirects while the dependent instruction waits.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a highest-priority EX/MEM load-result forwarding selection, with normal ALU and MEM/WB forwarding retained as fallbacks.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose the already sign/zero-extended load value as a combinational forwarding source while retaining the existing RVFI extraction and stall behavior.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Consume the load-data bypass and ensure a stalled dependent instruction cannot generate a redirect or architectural side effect before its operand is valid.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire the load-result bypass and dmem-stall qualification through the pipeline without changing the top-level IO or RVFI contract.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"broken\\\", \\\"formal_passed\\\": false, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": false, \\\"error\\\": \\\"formal_failed: reg_ch0\\\\nvcd\\\\nSBY 17:04:15 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:20  Writing trace to Verilog testbench: engine_0/trace_tb.v\\\\nSBY 17:04:15 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:20  Writing trace to constraints file: engine_0/trace.smtc\\\\nSBY 17:04:15 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:20  Writing trace to Yosys witness file: engine_0/trace.yw\\\\nSBY 17:04:15 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:20  St