lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r4s1 (broken, n/a): Moving branch/JALR resolution into ID requires age-ordered operand bypasses and synchronized `resolved_valid`/redirect/flush/RVFI metadata, because a partial early redirect path can make the retired instruction stream, PC-next values, and register checks disagree even when the EX fallback remains.\\\"}\\n13:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r4s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Add a tagged loop-exit predictor\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The successful static predictor already removes most taken backward-branch\\\\nredirects, but it predicts the final iteration of every loop as taken and\\\\npays an EX redirect when the loop exits. A general 16-entry BHT regressed\\\\nbecause of aliasing and weak-taken startup behavior, while a RAS regressed\\\\nFmax by adding a wide IF-stage mux. CoreMark's repeated counted loops make a\\\\nspecialized, low-aliasing loop predictor a better targeted opportunity.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The successful static predictor already removes most taken backward-branch\\\\nredirects, but it predicts the final iteration of every loop as taken and\\\\npays an EX redirect when the loop exits. A general 16-entry BHT regressed\\\\nbecause of aliasing and weak-taken startup behavior, while a RAS regressed\\\\nFmax by adding a wide IF-stage mux. CoreMark's repeated counted loops make a\\\\nspecialized, low-aliasing loop predictor a better targeted opportunity.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a very small tagged loop predictor for backward conditional branches.\\\\nKeep the current static backward-taken prediction on a cold or tag-mismatch\\\\nlookup, then learn a branch's repeated taken sequence and expected exit so a\\\\nmatching loop PC can predict not-taken on its final iteration. Use exact PC\\\\ntags and a compact remaining-iterations/confidence state rather than a\\\\nbroadly aliased BHT, and update entries only from resolved EX branches.\\\\nCarry the existing prediction metadata and retain the current redirect-on-\\\\nmismatch recovery, so wrong or changing trip counts remain architecturally\\\\nharmless while common CoreMark loop exits avoid an extra flush.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 3, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a tiny exact-tag loop predictor that overrides the existing backward-taken heuristic only for learned loop exits, with a static-prediction fallback and a narrow lookup path.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose the resolved backward conditional-branch PC and taken/not-taken outcome as a precise loop-predictor update event without changing redirect or RVFI behavior.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire the EX loop-branch update event into IF and preserve prediction metadata, bus-stall handling, and the existing single-channel RVFI contract.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 3, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a tiny exact-tag loop predictor that overrides the existing backward-taken heuristic only for learned loop exits, with a static-prediction fallback and a narrow lookup path.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose the resolved backward conditional-branch PC and taken/not-taken outcome as a precise loop-predictor update event without changing redirect or RVFI behavior.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire the EX loop-branch update event into IF and preserve prediction metadata, bus-stall handling, and the existing single-channel RVFI contract.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 244.72, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -22.88, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": -13.47, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 104.48, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4269318, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 13301, \\\"ff\\\": 3141, \\\"seeds\\\": [104.48, 100.13, 104.93], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-10T21:20:20.478409Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 2, \\\"round_id\\\": 4, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r4s2 (regression, -22.88%): A tagged loop predictor that adds IF-stage tag/state lookup to suppress only final-iteration backward-branch redirects can cost more fetch performance than the occasional exit flush it removes, even when exact tags avoid BHT aliasing.\\\"}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"find cores/bench -maxdepth 3 -type f \\\\\\\\( -name '*.rpt' -o -name '*.log' -o -name '*timing*' \\\\\\\\) -print | head -n 80 && rg -n -i 'critical path|worst path|slack|delay|timing' cores/bench --glob '\\\"'!experiments/log.jsonl'\\\"' --glob '\\\"'!LESSONS.md'\\\"' | head -n 80\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"find cores/bench -maxdepth 3 -type f \\\\\\\\( -name '*.rpt' -o -name '*.log' -o -name '*timing*' \\\\\\\\) -print | head -n 80 && rg -n -i 'critical path|worst path|slack|delay|timing' cores/bench --glob '\\\"'!experiments/log.jsonl'\\\"' --glob '\\\"'!LESSONS.md'\\\"' | head -n 80\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"cores/bench/generated/pnr_seed2/nextpnr.log\\ncores/bench/generated/pnr_seed3/nextpnr.log\\ncores/bench/generated/pnr_seed1/nextpnr.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-002-r2s1.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-003-r2s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-002-r4s1.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-003-r4s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-002-r1s1.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-003-r3s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-003-r1s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-002-r3s1.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-003-r5s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-002-r5s1.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-001-r4s0.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-001-r2s0.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-001-r5s0.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-001-r3s0.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-001-r1s0.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:2:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-001-r1s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Zero-bubble load-use forwarding\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current five-stage pipeline unconditionally stalls one cycle for every\\\\nload-use dependency, even though the Tang Nano bench presents combinational\\\\nzero-wait read data. CoreMark has frequent load-dependent address, compare,\\\\nand arithmetic instructions, so this bubble directly reduces iterations per\\\\ncycle. The existing P&R report also shows the EX/MEM-to-EX forwarding path as\\\\nthe dominant timing path, making a dedicated load-data bypass a focused\\\\nhigh-value datapath optimization.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current five-stage pipeline unconditionally stalls one cycle for every\\\\nload-use dependency, even though the Tang Nano bench presents combinational\\\\nzero-wait read data. CoreMark has frequent load-dependent address, compare,\\\\nand arithmetic instructions, so this bubble directly reduces iterations per\\\\ncycle. The existing P&R report also shows the EX/MEM-to-EX forwarding path as\\\\nthe dominant timing path, making a dedicated load-data bypass a focused\\\\nhigh-value datapath optimization.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a dedicated EX/MEM load-data bypass from the memory stage's extracted\\\\nbyte/half/word value into the EX operand mux, and remove the unconditional\\\\nload-use bubble. When dmemReady is low, hold the dependent instruction and\\\\nsuppress redirects or side effects until the load completes; when it is high,\\\\nforward the load value directly and retire the dependent instruction without\\\\na bubble. This should preserve arbitrary bus-stall correctness while\\\\nimproving CoreMark IPC on the zero-wait FPGA path.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace the unconditional load-use bubble with replay-safe holding on an outstanding dmem stall, and provide control to block redirects while the dependent instruction waits.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a highest-priority EX/MEM load-result forwarding selection, with normal ALU and MEM/WB forwarding retained as fallbacks.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose the already sign/zero-extended load value as a combinational forwarding source while retaining the existing RVFI extraction and stall behavior.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Consume the load-data bypass and ensure a stalled dependent instruction cannot generate a redirect or architectural side effect before its operand is valid.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire the load-result bypass and dmem-stall qualification through the pipeline without changing the top-level IO or RVFI contract.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Replace the unconditional load-use bubble with replay-safe holding on an outstanding dmem stall, and provide control to block redirects while the dependent instruction waits.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a highest-priority EX/MEM load-result forwarding selection, with normal ALU and MEM/WB forwarding retained as fallbacks.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Expose the already sign/zero-extended load value as a combinational forwarding source while retaining the existing RVFI extraction and stall behavior.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Consume the load-data bypass and ensure a stalled dependent instruction cannot generate a redirect or architectural side effect before its operand is valid.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire the load-result bypass and dmem-stall qualification through the pipeline without changing the top-level IO or RVFI contract.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"broken\\\", \\\"formal_passed\\\": false, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": false, \\\"error\\\": \\\"formal_failed: reg_ch0\\\\nvcd\\\\nSBY 17:04:15 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:20  Writing trace to Verilog testbench: engine_0/trace_tb.v\\\\nSBY 17:04:15 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:20  Writing trace to constraints file: engine_0/trace.smtc\\\\nSBY 17:04:15 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:20  Writing trace to Yosys witness file: engine_0/trace.yw\\\\nSBY 17:04:15 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:20  Status: failed\\\\nSBY 17:04:15 [reg_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=1)\\\\nSBY 17:04:15 [reg_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: FAIL\\\\nSBY 17:04:15 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:21 (21)\\\\nSBY 17:04:15 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:12 (12)\\\\nSBY 17:04:15 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_