{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r2s1\\\") | {motivation,hypothesis,fitness,delta_pct,fmax_mhz,cycles,lut4,ff,seeds,implementation_notes}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"motivation\": \"The current five-stage core places full-width multiply and divide/remainder\\narithmetic directly in the EX combinational cone. That cone is a poor\\nstructural match for the Tang Nano timing budget: the best run is only\\n132.29 MHz while already using 10554 LUT4s, and the prior structural FIFO\\nattempt showed that extra front-end state can lower Fmax. CoreMark's hot\\npath is predominantly integer and memory work, so isolating infrequent\\ndivide/remainder operations should improve timing without adding bubbles to\\nordinary ALU instructions.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The current five-stage core places full-width multiply and divide/remainder\\narithmetic directly in the EX combinational cone. That cone is a poor\\nstructural match for the Tang Nano timing budget: the best run is only\\n132.29 MHz while already using 10554 LUT4s, and the prior structural FIFO\\nattempt showed that extra front-end state can lower Fmax. CoreMark's hot\\npath is predominantly integer and memory work, so isolating infrequent\\ndivide/remainder operations should improve timing without adding bubbles to\\nordinary ALU instructions.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational divide/remainder portion of the ALU with a shared\\niterative radix-2 M execution unit. A DIV, DIVU, REM, or REMU entering EX\\nholds the in-order pipeline while the unit runs, then writes one RV32M-correct\\nresult through the existing EX/MEM and RVFI paths; ordinary ALU, load/store,\\nbranch, and multiply operations retain their single-cycle path. Add explicit\\nbusy/done control and operand/result registers so the divider is removed from\\nthe normal EX critical path, while preserving the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\\nbehavior and all trap, memory-stall, and retirement ordering invariants.\\n\",\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"fitness_delta_pct\": 6,\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    \"changes\": [\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Remove the normal-path / and % operators for DIV/REM and expose a clean divider request/result interface while retaining the ALTOPS and exact RV32M corner-case behavior.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Integrate the iterative M unit as a replay-safe multi-cycle EX operation, holding the instruction and preventing duplicate side effects until its result is ready.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Add divider-busy backpressure that freezes younger pipeline state but allows the in-flight divide to complete and retire exactly once.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Wire divider start, busy, and completion signals through the pipeline without changing the external bus or single-channel RVFI contract.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"fitness\": 267.72,\n  \"delta_pct\": -13.79,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 114.04,\n  \"cycles\": 4259699,\n  \"lut4\": 5901,\n  \"ff\": 2227,\n  \"seeds\": [\n    114.04,\n    122.97,\n    111.92\n  ],\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
