me the buffered entry\\nwhen ID can advance, and hold it across an imem stall instead of injecting a\\nfront-end bubble. On an EX redirect, invalidate the entry and restart the\\nfetch address at the resolved target; preserve the existing load-use,\\ndmem-stall, RVFI ordering, and predictor-metadata rules. The one-entry\\nelastic path should recover isolated iStall cycles while avoiding the pointer\\nand mux overhead that hurt the prior two-entry FIFO's Fmax.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the direct IF/ID coupling with a one-entry ready-aware fetch skid buffer that stores the PC, instruction, validity, and static prediction metadata, and flushes precisely on redirects.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate fetch-buffer fill stalls from back-end pipeline stalls so an imem bus stall preserves a buffered instruction without discarding valid front-end work.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Reconnect the elastic IF output and advance/hold controls while retaining the current static predictor, redirect priority, memory handshakes, and single-channel RVFI contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the direct IF/ID coupling with a one-entry ready-aware fetch skid buffer that stores the PC, instruction, validity, and static prediction metadata, and flushes precisely on redirects.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate fetch-buffer fill stalls from back-end pipeline stalls so an imem bus stall preserves a buffered instruction without discarding valid front-end work.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Reconnect the elastic IF output and advance/hold controls while retaining the current static predictor, redirect priority, memory handshakes, and single-channel RVFI contract.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 278.09, \"delta_pct\": -10.46, \"vs_baseline\": -1.67, \"fmax_mhz\": 119.99, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4314735, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10193, \"ff\": 2000, \"seeds\": [113.56, 124.73, 119.99], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T20:54:36.294499Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 3, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r3s1 (regression, -10.46%): A registered one-entry IF skid buffer must preserve empty-slot or simultaneous pop/push bypass behavior and redirect refill latency, or its added fetch bubbles outweigh the isolated imem-stall cycles it hides.\"}\n12:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r4s1\", \"title\": \"Resolve control flow in decode\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipeline currently resolves conditional branches and JALR in\\nEX, so a misprediction or unpredicted indirect jump flushes younger work\\nafter the front end has already advanced. The successful static predictor\\nremoves most backward-loop penalties, while the RAS attempt showed that\\nadding more prediction state directly to IF can damage Fmax. Resolving\\ncontrol flow one stage earlier attacks the remaining redirect bubbles without\\nadding a table or mux to the fetch next-PC path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The five-stage pipeline currently resolves conditional branches and JALR in\\nEX, so a misprediction or unpredicted indirect jump flushes younger work\\nafter the front end has already advanced. The successful static predictor\\nremoves most backward-loop penalties, while the RAS attempt showed that\\nadding more prediction state directly to IF can damage Fmax. Resolving\\ncontrol flow one stage earlier attacks the remaining redirect bubbles without\\nadding a table or mux to the fetch next-PC path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move branch-condition, branch-target, and JALR-target resolution into ID,\\nusing narrow bypasses from EX/MEM and MEM/WB plus the existing write-first\\nregister-file behavior. Feed the resolved target into the current redirect\\nand prediction-metadata machinery so correctly predicted transfers do not\\nredirect twice, while retaining an EX fallback for misalignment and any\\nunresolved operand case. This should reduce the wrong-path window for\\nforward branches and eliminate most of the remaining JALR return penalty at\\nsingle-issue throughput, with less IF timing cost than a dynamic return\\npredictor.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add decode-stage branch/JALR target and condition resolution with EX/MEM and MEM/WB operand bypasses, including aligned-target qualification and precise redirect metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the ID-stage redirect and target into fetch and coordinate it with EX redirects, flushes, and the existing single-channel RVFI retirement path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Adjust stall and flush arbitration so load-dependent control transfers wait for a valid bypassed operand and wrong-path instructions are killed exactly once.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the carried resolved-next-PC metadata to suppress duplicate EX redirects while preserving EX misalignment trapping and RVFI pc_wdata correctness.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add decode-stage branch/JALR target and condition resolution with EX/MEM and MEM/WB operand bypasses, including aligned-target qualification and precise redirect metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the ID-stage redirect and target into fetch and coordinate it with EX redirects, flushes, and the existing 