return pattern with substantially less state and timing\\noverhead.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add reset-valid shadow registers for x1 and x5, updated at writeback from\\nthe ordinary architectural write stream. In IF, when the fetched\\ninstruction is the canonical return-form JALR (rd=x0, funct3=0, rs1=x1 or\\nx5), use the corresponding shadow link value plus the decoded immediate as\\nthe predicted target; otherwise retain the current backward-branch and\\ndirect-JAL predictor. Carry the existing prediction metadata unchanged so\\nEX still resolves every return and redirects only on a mismatch. This\\nremoves repeated return bubbles without a tag compare, BHT aliasing, RAS\\nstack mux, or multi-entry target-table lookup; stale or nonstandard link\\nvalues remain harmless because the existing precise redirect recovery\\nremains authoritative.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add two valid shadow link registers and a narrow canonical-return JALR prediction path that uses x1/x5 plus the decoded immediate, while preserving existing static predictions and redirect fallback.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect the writeback architectural write-enable, destination, and data to IF so the shadow link registers track committed x1/x5 values without changing the external IO or RVFI contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add two valid shadow link registers and a narrow canonical-return JALR prediction path that uses x1/x5 plus the decoded immediate, while preserving existing static predictions and redirect fallback.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect the writeback architectural write-enable, destination, and data to IF so the shadow link registers track committed x1/x5 values without changing the external IO 