{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r7s1.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r7s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r7s1\ntitle: \"Elastic in-order memory backend\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The retimed EX1/EX2 pipeline now has useful independent work available, but\n  the current MEM control still freezes it whenever io_dmemReady is low for a\n  load or store.  The benchmark injects roughly 22% data-bus stalls, so this\n  coupling directly reduces CoreMark iterations per cycle.  The previous store\n  buffer attempt regressed because queue occupancy remained on the global\n  dmem-stall path; the next design should decouple waiting memory requests from\n  younger non-memory work while retaining strict retirement order.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a small age-ordered completion queue after EX2 together with a dedicated\n  memory-request slot.  A load or store occupies the memory slot until its\n  dmem handshake completes, while younger non-memory instructions can execute\n  and wait in the completion queue instead of freezing the whole backend.\n  Block younger memory operations and consumers of a pending load, and apply\n  backpressure only when the queue is full.  Retire and expose RVFI strictly\n  from the oldest queue entry, with queue-aware forwarding for values that are\n  complete but not yet retired.  This should hide a meaningful fraction of\n  random dmem stalls without adding logic to the IF critical path or changing\n  the external bus and single-channel RVFI contracts.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Define the age-ordered completion-entry and pending-memory metadata needed by the elastic backend while preserving the existing RVFI payload fields.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Integrate the memory request slot and completion queue, making the oldest entry the sole WB/RVFI retirement source without changing top-level IO.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Separate memory-request capture, dmem-ready handshake, and load-response completion so a waiting request no longer freezes unrelated EX work.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Replace the global memory-stall coupling with queue-full, pending-load dependency, and younger-memory ordering controls.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add age-correct forwarding from completed-but-unretired queue entries while keeping pending-load results unavailable until the response arrives.\"\n  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n    description: \"Drive register writes and retirement data from the oldest completed queue entry exactly once, preserving RVFI order and memory metadata.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
