{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -c 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260710-001-r7s0\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r5s1\\\")' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl && sed -n '1,220p' fpga/core_bench_si.sv 2>/dev/null | head -120\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r5s1\",\"title\":\"Retimed two-phase execute pipeline\",\"category\":\"structural\",\"motivation\":\"The current critical path starts at the ID/EX register and traverses the\\nEX forwarding muxes, ALU operand selection, and the 32-bit arithmetic cone\\nbefore reaching EX/MEM.  The successful static predictor already removes\\nmost loop redirect bubbles, while the earlier fetch-buffer and decode-\\nredirect structures lost more Fmax than they gained in IPC.  A physical\\nexecute-stage retiming therefore offers a more direct way to improve the\\nfitness product without adding predictor state or widening the interface.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The current critical path starts at the ID/EX register and traverses the\\nEX forwarding muxes, ALU operand selection, and the 32-bit arithmetic cone\\nbefore reaching EX/MEM.  The successful static predictor already removes\\nmost loop redirect bubbles, while the earlier fetch-buffer and decode-\\nredirect structures lost more Fmax than they gained in IPC.  A physical\\nexecute-stage retiming therefore offers a more direct way to improve the\\nfitness product without adding predictor state or widening the interface.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Split execute into an operand/forwarding EX1 stage and an arithmetic/control\\nEX2 stage, with a pipeline register between them.  EX1 captures the selected\\nforwarded operands, immediate, PC, control, and prediction metadata; EX2\\nperforms the ALU operation, memory-address calculation, branch or jump\\nresolution, and alignment checks, then drives the existing EX/MEM contract.\\nAdd age-correct EX2-to-EX2 and MEM/WB bypasses and stall/flush control so\\ndependent ALU instructions still sustain one instruction per cycle, while\\nload-use and dmem stalls retain precise RVFI validity and ordering.  The\\nextra register should remove the forwarding/operand mux delay from the\\narithmetic timing path and raise Fmax, with only the already-predicted\\ncontrol-flow cases avoiding an added redirect penalty.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":6,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add the internal EX1 pipeline bundle needed to carry forwarded operands, control, PC, and static-prediction metadata across the new execute-stage boundary while retaining the existing EX/MEM and RVFI bundle fields.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Retiming the execute logic into operand-capture EX1 and arithmetic/control EX2 registers, with precise forwarding, branch prediction comparison, misalignment traps, dmem-stall holds, and the unchanged EX/MEM output contract.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Recompute load-use, redirect flush, and dmem backpressure arbitration for the additional execute stage so bubbles and holds preserve age order and do not duplicate or skip RVFI retirements.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire the retimed execute-stage controls and forwarding sources through the existing five-stage top-level datapath without changing the external buses or single-channel RVFI port set.\"}]},\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":6,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add the internal EX1 pipeline bundle needed to carry forwarded operands, control, PC, and static-prediction metadata across the new execute-stage boundary while retaining the existing EX/MEM and RVFI bundle fields.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Retiming the execute logic into operand-capture EX1 and arithmetic/control EX2 registers, with precise forwarding, branch prediction comparison, misalignment traps, dmem-stall holds, and the unchanged EX/MEM output contract.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Recompute load-use, redirect flush, and dmem backpressure arbitration for the additional execute stage so bubbles and holds preserve age order and do not duplicate or skip RVFI retirements.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire the retimed execute-stage controls and forwarding sources through the existing five-stage top-level datapath without changing the external buses or single-channel RVFI port set.\"}],\"outcome\":\"improvement\",\"fitness\":396.37,\"delta_pct\":24.91,\"vs_baseline\":40.15,\"fmax_mhz\":172.03,\"ipc_coremark\":0.000002,\"cycles\":4340155,\"iterations\":10,\"lut4\":10388,\"ff\":2076,\"seeds\":[179.99,172.03,166.97],\"formal_passed\":true,\"cosim_passed\":true,\"error\":null,\"implementation_notes\":\"\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-07-10T21:45:33.543025Z\",\"slot\":1,\"round_id\":5,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r5s1 (improvement, +24.91%): Splitting execute into an operand/forwarding EX1 and arithmetic/control EX2 stage can materially improve CoreMark fitness by removing the forwarding muxes from the ALU cone, provided EX2-to-EX1 age-ordered bypasses and precise bubble/hold control preserve dependent ALU, load-use, and dmem-stall ordering.\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-001-r7s0\",\"title\":\"Remove redundant MEM/WB forwarding leg\",\"category\":\"micro_opt\",\"motivation\":\"The retimed core already captures forwarded operands in EX1, but its\\nforwarding network still performs a third age comparison and selects a\\nMEM/WB value.  The register file has an explicit write-first WB bypass, and\\nEX1 re-reads the held instruction's registers, so this MEM/WB leg duplicates\\na value that is already available at the register-file read ports.  Removing\\nthe duplicate compare and mux should reduce EX1 capture delay and routing\\nwithout changing the arithmetic or memory pipeline.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The retimed core already captures forwarded operands in EX1, but its\\nforwarding network still performs a third age comparison and selects a\\nMEM/WB value.  The register file has an explicit write-first WB bypass, and\\nEX1 re-reads the held instruction's registers, so this MEM/WB leg duplicates\\na value that is already available at the register-file read ports.  Removing\\nthe duplicate compare and mux should reduce EX1 capture delay and routing\\nwithout changing the arithmetic or memory pipeline.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Eliminate the MEM/WB source from the EX1 forwarding priority, retaining only\\nthe freshest EX2 result, the EX/MEM result or load value, and the\\nwrite-first register-file read as the fallback.  Simplify the forwarding\\ninterfaces and wiring so the WB value is supplied solely by the existing\\nregister-file bypass.  Because WB writes are visible combinationally and\\nEX1 re-reads operands when an instruction is held, dependent ALU, load-use,\\nbus-stall, redirect, RVFI, and x0 behavior should remain unchanged while\\nthe operand-capture path becomes smaller and faster.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":2,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Remove the MEM/WB equality comparison and forwarding selection while preserving EX2-over-EX/MEM age priority and x0 suppression.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Simplify the EX1 operand mux inputs to use EX2, EX/MEM, or the write-first register-file read, with no functional change to load forwarding or stalls.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Update forwarding wiring to drop the redundant MEM/WB forwarding source while retaining the existing WB write-first regfile path and top-level RVFI contract.\"}]},\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":2,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Remove the MEM/WB equality comparison and forwarding selection while preserving EX2-over-EX/MEM age priority and x0 suppression.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Simplify the EX1 operand mux inputs to use EX2, EX/MEM, or the write-first register-file read, with no functional change to load forwarding or stalls.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Update forwarding wiring to drop the redundant MEM/WB forwarding source while retaining the existing WB write-first regfile path and top-level RVFI contract.\"}],\"outcome\":\"improvement\",\"fitness\":480.9,\"delta_pct\":21.33,\"vs_baseline\":70.04,\"fmax_mhz\":208.72,\"ipc_coremark\":0.000002,\"cycles\":4340155,\"iterations\":10,\"lut4\":10135,\"ff\":2076,\"seeds\":[214.55,208.72,203.96],\"formal_passed\":true,\"cosim_passed\":true,\"error\":null,\"implementation_notes\":\"\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-07-10T22:14:26.680923Z\",\"slot\":0,\"round_id\":7,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r7s0 (improvement, +21.33%): Removing a redundant MEM/WB forwarding compare and mux improved CoreMark because EX1's write-first register-file reread already exposes WB data, so forwarding should retain only younger values unavailable at the read ports while preserving EX2-over-EX/MEM priority.\"}\n// fpga/core_bench_si.sv\n//\n// FPGA Fmax wrapper for single-issue (`nret 1`) cores. Same shape as\n// core_bench.sv but instantiates `core` with only the channel-0 RVFI port\n// set — no `_1` ports. Selected by the orchestrator (via BENCH env var in\n// synth.tcl) when cores/<target>/core.yaml declares nret: 1.\n//\n// See core_bench.sv for the full rationale on LFSR-driven imem, dmem\n// model, and the XOR-reduce LED that keeps RVFI fan-out alive through\n// dead-output elimination.\nmodule core_bench (\n  input  logic clock,\n  input  logic reset,\n  output logic led\n);\n\n  logic [31:0] lfsr;\n  always_ff @(posedge clock or posedge reset)\n    if (reset) lfsr <= 32'h1;\n    else       lfsr <= {lfsr[30:0], lfsr[31] ^ lfsr[21] ^ lfsr[1] ^ lfsr[0]};\n\n  logic [31:0] dmem [0:2047];\n  logic [31:0] dmem_rdata;\n  logic [31:0] dmem_addr;\n  logic [31:0] dmem_wdata;\n  logic [3:0]  dmem_wen;\n  logic        dmem_ren;\n\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (dmem_wen[0]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][7:0]   <= dmem_wdata[7:0];\n    if (dmem_wen[1]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][15:8]  <= dmem_wdata[15:8];\n    if (dmem_wen[2]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][23:16] <= dmem_wdata[23:16];\n    if (dmem_wen[3]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][31:24] <= dmem_wdata[31:24];\n  end\n  assign dmem_rdata = dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]];\n\n  logic [31:0] imem_addr;\n  // Single-channel RVFI fan-out (NRET=1 contract).\n  logic        rvfi_valid_0;\n  logic [63:0] rvfi_order_0;\n  logic [31:0] rvfi_insn_0, rvfi_pc_rdata_0, rvfi_pc_wdata_0;\n  logic [31:0] rvfi_rd_wdata_0, rvfi_rs1_rdata_0, rvfi_rs2_rdata_0;\n  logic [31:0] rvfi_mem_addr_0, rvfi_mem_rdata_0, rvfi_mem_wdata_0;\n  logic [4:0]  rvfi_rs1_addr_0, rvfi_rs2_addr_0, rvfi_rd_addr_0;\n  logic [3:0]  rvfi_mem_rmask_0, rvfi_mem_wmask_0;\n  logic [1:0]  rvfi_mode_0, rvfi_ixl_0;\n  logic        rvfi_trap_0, rvfi_halt_0, rvfi_intr_0;\n\n  core cpu (\n    .clock            (clock),\n    .reset            (reset),\n    .io_imemAddr      (imem_addr),\n    .io_imemData      (lfsr),\n    .io_imemReady     (1'b1),\n    .io_dmemAddr      (dmem_addr),\n    .io_dmemWData     (dmem_wdata),\n    .io_dmemRData     (dmem_rdata),\n    .io_dmemWEn       (dmem_wen),\n    .io_dmemREn       (dmem_ren),\n    .io_dmemReady     (1'b1),\n    .io_rvfi_valid_0    (rvfi_valid_0),\n    .io_rvfi_order_0    (rvfi_order_0),\n    .io_rvfi_insn_0     (rvfi_insn_0),\n    .io_rvfi_trap_0     (rvfi_trap_0),\n    .io_rvfi_halt_0     (rvfi_halt_0),\n    .io_rvfi_intr_0     (rvfi_intr_0),\n    .io_rvfi_mode_0     (rvfi_mode_0),\n    .io_rvfi_ixl_0      (rvfi_ixl_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rs1_addr_0 (rvfi_rs1_addr_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rs1_rdata_0(rvfi_rs1_rdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rs2_addr_0 (rvfi_rs2_addr_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rs2_rdata_0(rvfi_rs2_rdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rd_addr_0  (rvfi_rd_addr_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rd_wdata_0 (rvfi_rd_wdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_pc_rdata_0 (rvfi_pc_rdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_pc_wdata_0 (rvfi_pc_wdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_mem_addr_0 (rvfi_mem_addr_0),\n    .io_rvfi_mem_rmask_0(rvfi_mem_rmask_0),\n    .io_rvfi_mem_wmask_0(rvfi_mem_wmask_0),\n    .io_rvfi_mem_rdata_0(rvfi_mem_rdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_mem_wdata_0(rvfi_mem_wdata_0)\n  );\n\n  // XOR-reduce all CPU outputs to a single LED bit. Without this,\n  // dead-output elimination would prune the RVFI fan-out.\n  assign led = ^{rvfi_valid_0, rvfi_order_0, rvfi_insn_0, rvfi_trap_0, rvfi_halt_0, rvfi_intr_0,\n                 rvfi_mode_0, rvfi_ixl_0, rvfi_rs1_addr_0, rvfi_rs1_rdata_0,\n                 rvfi_rs2_addr_0, rvfi_rs2_rdata_0, rvfi_rd_addr_0, rvfi_rd_wdata_0,\n                 rvfi_pc_rdata_0, rvfi_pc_wdata_0, rvfi_mem_addr_0,\n                 rvfi_mem_rmask_0, rvfi_mem_wmask_0, rvfi_mem_rdata_0, rvfi_mem_wdata_0,\n                 imem_addr, dmem_rdata};\n\nendmodule\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
