{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r8s1.yaml && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r8s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r8s1\ntitle: \"Retimed two-phase memory response\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The retimed EX1/EX2 core has already removed the forwarding muxes from the\n  arithmetic critical path, and the failed queue experiments show that broad\n  backend decoupling is too risky.  The remaining memory-stage path combines\n  the FPGA data-memory read, byte extraction, sign extension, and MEM/WB\n  capture in one timing interval.  CoreMark uses enough loads for this path to\n  affect both Fmax and the load-use schedule.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split the memory stage into a registered request stage and a registered\n  response/format stage.  The request stage drives the existing dmem address,\n  write data, and byte enables and holds precisely when io_dmemReady is low;\n  the response stage first captures raw read data and memory metadata, then\n  performs byte-lane extraction and sign extension into the existing writeback\n  payload.  Pipeline the stages at one request per cycle so zero-wait memory\n  retains throughput while the added register isolates the FPGA memory output\n  from the load-formatting cone.  Update hazards and valid/hold sequencing so\n  stores, loads, load-use forwarding, RVFI metadata, and rvfi_order remain\n  age-correct under both ready and stalled data buses.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add request/response pipeline payload fields needed to carry memory operation metadata and raw read data across the retimed backend stages.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Replace the single memory combinational path with a ready-aware request register and a response register that performs load extraction and writeback payload formation.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Recompute data-bus stall, load-use, and pipeline hold/bubble controls for the extra memory-response latency without allowing duplicate memory effects.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the retimed memory-stage controls and forwarding timing while preserving the existing external buses and single-channel RVFI contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
