{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r9s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r9s1\ntitle: \"Two-read-port operand snapshot pipeline\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current pipeline exposes four combinational register-file read ports:\n  two for decode and two more for EX1 to reread an instruction held in\n  ID/EX.  That duplicated read topology consumes LUTs and adds fanout and\n  muxing around the operand-forwarding boundary, which is especially costly\n  when the design is already close to the Tang Nano LUT budget.\nhypothesis: |\n  Remove the dedicated EX1 register-file reread ports and make the ID/EX\n  operand snapshot authoritative.  When ID/EX is held for a load-use or\n  dmem stall, refresh only its stored rs1/rs2 values from the existing two\n  decode read ports, including their write-first WB behavior; otherwise\n  capture operands normally.  EX1 will still apply the existing age-ordered\n  EX2 and EX/MEM forwarding, while all source addresses and RVFI fields stay\n  unchanged.  This should reduce register-file replication and operand-path\n  fanout without adding a new critical datapath stage.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/reg_file.sv\n    description: \"Collapse the register file from four combinational read ports to the existing two decode ports, retaining x0 behavior and write-first WB bypassing.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Refresh the held ID/EX operand snapshots from the decode read ports on every stall so delayed load-use and dmem-stall cases see newly retired register values.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the ID/EX operand snapshots as the non-forwarded EX1 inputs and remove the redundant EX1 register-file reread interface while preserving EX2-over-EX/MEM forwarding priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Reconnect the reduced register-file interface and operand path without changing the external buses, pipeline retirement boundary, or single-channel RVFI contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
