{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.category==\\\"predictor\\\") | [.id,.title,.outcome,(.delta_pct // \\\"n/a\\\"),(.fitness // \\\"n/a\\\"),(.fmax_mhz // \\\"n/a\\\"),(.hypothesis.hypothesis // .hypothesis // \\\"\\\")] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20260710-003-r1s2\tEarly static backward-branch prediction\timprovement\t9.81\t310.56\t132.29\tAdd an IF-stage static control-flow predictor that predicts valid backward\\nconditional branches taken and predicts direct JAL instructions to their\\nimmediately computed targets; leave forward branches and JALR unpredicted.\\nCarry the predicted next PC through ID/EX and make EX redirect only when the\\nresolved next PC differs from the prediction, recovering to the actual\\ntarget or fall-through PC on a miss. This should remove most EX redirect\\nbubbles from CoreMark loop branches with little area and timing overhead.\\n\nhyp-20260710-003-r2s2\tAdd a tiny dynamic branch history predictor\tregression\t-9.22\t281.94\t118.96\tAdd a small PC-indexed 2-bit saturating branch history table in the IF stage.\\nUse the existing IF-stage B/J immediate target calculation, but consult the\\ntable for every valid conditional branch, with reset counters biased weakly\\ntaken so the existing backward-loop behavior is preserved. Update the\\ncounter at EX resolution for every conditional branch, carrying the existing\\nprediction metadata through the pipeline and redirecting only on a\\nnext-PC mismatch. This should retain the static predictor's loop benefit,\\nreduce forward-branch and repeated loop-exit mispredictions, and add only a\\nfew small registers plus a narrow update path.\\n\nhyp-20260710-003-r3s2\tAdd a compact return-address stack predictor\tregression\t-14.14\t266.64\t113.21\tAdd a small, low-associativity return-address stack (RAS) in IF for JALR\\ninstructions whose source is x1 or x5 and whose destination is x0. Predict\\nthe top stack entry as the next PC, while retaining the existing static\\nbackward-branch and direct-JAL predictions for other control flow. Update\\nthe RAS from resolved EX calls and returns, pushing pc+4 for link-register\\nJAL/JALR calls and popping on returns; use the existing prediction metadata\\nand next-PC comparison so a cold or imperfect RAS recovers through the\\ncurrent redirect path. A 4-entry stack should cover CoreMark's shallow call\\ndepth with substantially less tag-compare and aliasing cost than a BHT/BTB.\\n\nhyp-20260710-003-r4s2\tAdd a tagged loop-exit predictor\tregression\t-22.88\t244.72\t104.48\tAdd a very small tagged loop predictor for backward conditional branches.\\nKeep the current static backward-taken prediction on a cold or tag-mismatch\\nlookup, then learn a branch's repeated taken sequence and expected exit so a\\nmatching loop PC can predict not-taken on its final iteration. Use exact PC\\ntags and a compact remaining-iterations/confidence state rather than a\\nbroadly aliased BHT, and update entries only from resolved EX branches.\\nCarry the existing prediction metadata and retain the current redirect-on-\\nmismatch recovery, so wrong or changing trip counts remain architecturally\\nharmless while common CoreMark loop exits avoid an extra flush.\\n\nhyp-20260710-003-r5s2\tAdd a tiny exact-tag return target cache\tregression\t-21.52\t249.03\t105.82\tAdd a two-entry direct-mapped return-target cache indexed by one PC bit and\\ntagged with the full JALR PC. In IF, recognize only return-form JALR\\ninstructions (rd=x0 and rs1=x1 or x5); on an exact valid-tag hit, predict\\nthe cached target, otherwise retain the current sequential prediction.\\nUpdate the selected entry only when that return resolves in EX, carrying the\\nexisting prediction metadata so the normal mismatch redirect recovers from\\ncold entries and collisions. This should remove recurring JALR return\\nbubbles with less timing and state cost than a stack or general BTB, while\\nexact tags make an alias a harmless miss rather than a wrong-path fetch.\\n\nhyp-20260710-003-r6s2\tShadow-link return predictor\tregression\t-5.28\t375.45\t161.92\tAdd reset-valid shadow registers for x1 and x5, updated at writeback from\\nthe ordinary architectural write stream. In IF, when the fetched\\ninstruction is the canonical return-form JALR (rd=x0, funct3=0, rs1=x1 or\\nx5), use the corresponding shadow link value plus the decoded immediate as\\nthe predicted target; otherwise retain the current backward-branch and\\ndirect-JAL predictor. Carry the existing prediction metadata unchanged so\\nEX still resolves every return and redirects only on a mismatch. This\\nremoves repeated return bubbles without a tag compare, BHT aliasing, RAS\\nstack mux, or multi-entry target-table lookup; stale or nonstandard link\\nvalues remain harmless because the existing precise redirect recovery\\nremains authoritative.\\n\nhyp-20260710-003-r7s2\tSelective gshare forward-branch predictor\tregression\t1.74\t403.25\t174.67\tAdd a small 32-entry, 2-bit gshare direction table for forward conditional\\nbranches. Index the table with a low PC slice XORed with a short global\\nconditional-branch history, initialize counters weakly not-taken, and update\\nthe counter from the precise EX branch outcome. Use the table only when the\\nbranch immediate is forward; retain the existing static backward-taken and\\ndirect-JAL predictions for all other control flow. Carry the existing\\nprediction metadata and redirect on a resolved next-PC mismatch, so cold\\nentries and history aliasing recover precisely without changing RVFI or\\narchitectural behavior. The XOR history should separate recurring CoreMark\\nbranch contexts better than the failed PC-only BHT while adding only a small\\ncounter array and narrow update state.\\n\nhyp-20260710-003-r8s2\tNarrow zero-offset return predictor\tregression\t-18.69\t391.01\t168.63\tTrack only the committed value of x1 in one valid shadow register and predict\\nonly `jalr x0, 0(x1)` in IF. The prediction target is the shadow value itself,\\nwith no link-plus-immediate adder, tag array, history table, or x5 selection\\non the fetch path. Update the shadow from the existing writeback stream and\\ncarry the existing prediction metadata so EX remains authoritative and\\nredirects on a cold, stale, or noncanonical prediction. This should recover\\nrepeated ABI return bubbles at substantially lower Fmax risk than the prior\\ngeneral x1/x5 shadow predictor.\\n\nhyp-20260710-003-r9s2\tSingle-adder static branch predictor\tregression\t-59.91\t192.8\t83.68\tPreserve the existing backward-conditional-taken and direct-JAL prediction\\npolicy, but factor their target generation into one shared PC-relative adder:\\nselect a validated B- or J-immediate first, then perform a single target\\naddition only for the recognized prediction class. Keep forward branches and\\nJALR unpredicted, and carry the existing prediction metadata and EX mismatch\\nrecovery unchanged. Removing duplicated target arithmetic and an unnecessary\\npost-adder selection should improve Fmax and LUT pressure without adding\\npredictor state, aliasing, warm-up misses, or architectural risk.\\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
