{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260710-003-r1s2\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-003-r5s2\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-003-r7s2\\\") | [.id,.title,.implementation_notes,.hypothesis] | @json' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"[\"hyp-20260710-003-r1s2\",\"Early static backward-branch prediction\",\"\",{\"motivation\":\"The bench core resolves conditional branches and jumps in EX, then flushes\\nyounger work and redirects the fetch PC. CoreMark contains many tight loops,\\nso taken backward branches repeatedly pay this avoidable redirect penalty.\\nThe fixture is already close to its LUT budget, making a table-based BTB/BHT\\na riskier tradeoff than a small decode-only predictor.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Add an IF-stage static control-flow predictor that predicts valid backward\\nconditional branches taken and predicts direct JAL instructions to their\\nimmediately computed targets; leave forward branches and JALR unpredicted.\\nCarry the predicted next PC through ID/EX and make EX redirect only when the\\nresolved next PC differs from the prediction, recovering to the actual\\ntarget or fall-through PC on a miss. This should remove most EX redirect\\nbubbles from CoreMark loop branches with little area and timing overhead.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":4,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Compute aligned B/J immediates from the fetched instruction and select a predicted target for backward conditional branches and direct JALs before the EX redirect path.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Extend the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles with prediction-valid/target metadata needed to compare the prediction against the resolved next PC.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch the IF-stage prediction metadata alongside the decoded instruction so EX can validate or recover from the prediction.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Compare the resolved branch/jump next PC with the carried prediction and issue redirects only on mispredictions, preserving trap and RVFI pc_next semantics.\"}]}]\n[\"hyp-20260710-003-r5s2\",\"Add a tiny exact-tag return target cache\",\"\",{\"motivation\":\"The existing static predictor removes most backward-loop and direct-JAL\\nredirects, but indirect JALR returns still resolve in EX and pay a flush.\\nThe prior BHT regressed from aliasing and the four-entry RAS regressed from\\nits IF-stage multiway mux. A very small exact-tag structure can target only\\nrepeated return sites while keeping the fetch lookup narrow.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Add a two-entry direct-mapped return-target cache indexed by one PC bit and\\ntagged with the full JALR PC. In IF, recognize only return-form JALR\\ninstructions (rd=x0 and rs1=x1 or x5); on an exact valid-tag hit, predict\\nthe cached target, otherwise retain the current sequential prediction.\\nUpdate the selected entry only when that return resolves in EX, carrying the\\nexisting prediction metadata so the normal mismatch redirect recovers from\\ncold entries and collisions. This should remove recurring JALR return\\nbubbles with less timing and state cost than a stack or general BTB, while\\nexact tags make an alias a harmless miss rather than a wrong-path fetch.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":3,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Add the two-entry exact-tag return-target lookup on the existing IF prediction path, selecting a cached target only for recognized return-form JALR instructions and falling back to the current static prediction otherwise.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Expose a precise resolved-return update event containing the JALR PC and aligned resolved target, without changing redirect, trap, or RVFI behavior.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire the EX return-target update event into IF and preserve prediction metadata, bus-stall handling, and the single-channel RVFI contract.\"}]}]\n[\"hyp-20260710-003-r7s2\",\"Selective gshare forward-branch predictor\",\"\",{\"motivation\":\"The current static predictor is effective for CoreMark's backward loops and\\ndirect JALs, but it leaves every forward conditional branch not-taken. The\\nearlier PC-only 16-entry BHT regressed because it aliased branch sites and\\nused a harmful weak-taken startup bias, while larger tagged predictors hurt\\nthe IF timing path. A predictor that targets only the remaining forward\\nbranches can add useful direction information without disturbing the proven\\nloop prediction policy.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Add a small 32-entry, 2-bit gshare direction table for forward conditional\\nbranches. Index the table with a low PC slice XORed with a short global\\nconditional-branch history, initialize counters weakly not-taken, and update\\nthe counter from the precise EX branch outcome. Use the table only when the\\nbranch immediate is forward; retain the existing static backward-taken and\\ndirect-JAL predictions for all other control flow. Carry the existing\\nprediction metadata and redirect on a resolved next-PC mismatch, so cold\\nentries and history aliasing recover precisely without changing RVFI or\\narchitectural behavior. The XOR history should separate recurring CoreMark\\nbranch contexts better than the failed PC-only BHT while adding only a small\\ncounter array and narrow update state.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":3,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Add the small gshare history/counter state, use it only to choose taken predictions for forward conditional branches, preserve the existing backward-branch and direct-JAL static cases, and update state from resolved branches.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Expose a precise conditional-branch update event containing the resolved branch PC, direction, and validity while leaving redirect, trap, and RVFI next-PC behavior unchanged.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire the EX branch-resolution update event into the IF predictor without changing the external bus or single-channel RVFI contract.\"}]}]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The history confirms that stateful IF predictors, return structures, and extra target-path logic all hurt Fmax; the only durable win is the existing decode-only BTFNT/direct-JAL policy. I’m selecting a narrow extension of that policy: predict only architecturally certain conditional branches whose two source register fields are identical, adding no table, tags, history, or update path."}}
