{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r11s2.yaml; git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r11s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r11s2\ntitle: \"Static operand-identity branch prediction\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The proven backward-taken/direct-JAL predictor improves CoreMark, while\n  every stateful predictor tested so far has added enough IF timing cost to\n  lose fitness. Some conditional branches have an architecturally certain\n  direction when rs1 and rs2 name the same register, so this is a predictor\n  opportunity that needs no table, tags, history, or training state.\nhypothesis: |\n  Extend the existing IF static predictor to recognize conditional branches\n  with identical rs1 and rs2 fields. Predict BEQ, BGE, and BGEU as taken when\n  the operands are the same; leave the complementary always-not-taken cases\n  on the existing sequential path. Preserve backward-taken and direct-JAL\n  prediction, carry the current prediction metadata, and retain EX as the\n  authoritative mismatch recovery point. The added five-bit identity check\n  should be much cheaper than a dynamic lookup while eliminating redirects for\n  compiler-emitted unconditional or known-direction branch idioms.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 1\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a stateless exact-direction branch check for identical source-register fields, combine only its taken cases with the existing backward-branch/direct-JAL predictor, and preserve current target, redirect, stall, and prediction metadata behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
