{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'predictor|branch|BHT|gshare|RAS|return|taken|prediction' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Zero-bubble load-use forwarding\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current five-stage pipeline unconditionally stalls one cycle for every\\nload-use dependency, even though the Tang Nano bench presents combinational\\nzero-wait read data. CoreMark has frequent load-dependent address, compare,\\nand arithmetic instructions, so this bubble directly reduces iterations per\\ncycle. The existing P&R report also shows the EX/MEM-to-EX forwarding path as\\nthe dominant timing path, making a dedicated load-data bypass a focused\\nhigh-value datapath optimization.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current five-stage pipeline unconditionally stalls one cycle for every\\nload-use dependency, even though the Tang Nano bench presents combinational\\nzero-wait read data. CoreMark has frequent load-dependent address, compare,\\nand arithmetic instructions, so this bubble directly reduces iterations per\\ncycle. The existing P&R report also shows the EX/MEM-to-EX forwarding path as\\nthe dominant timing path, making a dedicated load-data bypass a focused\\nhigh-value datapath optimization.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a dedicated EX/MEM load-data bypass from the memory stage's extracted\\nbyte/half/word value into the EX operand mux, and remove the unconditional\\nload-use bubble. When dmemReady is low, hold the dependent instruction and\\nsuppress redirects or side effects until the load completes; when it is high,\\nforward the load value directly and retire the dependent instruction without\\na bubble. This should preserve arbitrary bus-stall correctness while\\nimproving CoreMark IPC on the zero-wait FPGA path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the unconditional load-use bubble with replay-safe holding on an outstanding dmem stall, and provide control to block redirects while the dependent instruction waits.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a highest-priority EX/MEM load-result forwarding selection, with normal ALU and MEM/WB forwarding retained as fallbacks.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the already sign/zero-extended load value as a combinational forwarding source while retaining the existing RVFI extraction and stall behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the load-data bypass and ensure a stalled dependent instruction cannot generate a redirect or architectural side effect before its operand is valid.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the load-result bypass and dmem-stall qualification through the pipeline without changing the top-level IO or RVFI contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the unconditional load-use bubble with replay-safe holding on an outstanding dmem stall, and provide control to block redirects while the dependent instruction waits.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a highest-priority EX/MEM load-result forwarding selection, with normal ALU and MEM/WB forwarding retained as fallbacks.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the already sign/zero-extended load value as a combinational forwarding source while retaining the existing RVFI extraction and stall behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the load-data bypass and ensure a stalled dependent instruction cannot generate a redirect or architectural side effect before its operand is valid.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\