{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -c 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260710-003-r7s2\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-003-r6s2\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-003-r1s2\\\")' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-003-r1s2\",\"title\":\"Early static backward-branch prediction\",\"category\":\"predictor\",\"motivation\":\"The bench core resolves conditional branches and jumps in EX, then flushes\\nyounger work and redirects the fetch PC. CoreMark contains many tight loops,\\nso taken backward branches repeatedly pay this avoidable redirect penalty.\\nThe fixture is already close to its LUT budget, making a table-based BTB/BHT\\na riskier tradeoff than a small decode-only predictor.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The bench core resolves conditional branches and jumps in EX, then flushes\\nyounger work and redirects the fetch PC. CoreMark contains many tight loops,\\nso taken backward branches repeatedly pay this avoidable redirect penalty.\\nThe fixture is already close to its LUT budget, making a table-based BTB/BHT\\na riskier tradeoff than a small decode-only predictor.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Add an IF-stage static control-flow predictor that predicts valid backward\\nconditional branches taken and predicts direct JAL instructions to their\\nimmediately computed targets; leave forward branches and JALR unpredicted.\\nCarry the predicted next PC through ID/EX and make EX redirect only when the\\nresolved next PC differs from the prediction, recovering to the actual\\ntarget or fall-through PC on a miss. This should remove most EX redirect\\nbubbles from CoreMark loop branches with little area and timing overhead.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":4,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Compute aligned B/J immediates from the fetched instruction and select a predicted target for backward conditional branches and direct JALs before the EX redirect path.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Extend the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles with prediction-valid/target metadata needed to compare the prediction against the resolved next PC.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch the IF-stage prediction metadata alongside the decoded instruction so EX can validate or recover from the prediction.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Compare the resolved branch/jump next PC with the carried prediction and issue redirects only on mispredictions, preserving trap and RVFI pc_next semantics.\"}]},\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":4,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Compute aligned B/J immediates from the fetched instruction and select a predicted target for backward conditional branches and direct JALs before the EX redirect path.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Extend the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles with prediction-valid/target metadata needed to compare the prediction against the resolved next PC.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch the IF-stage prediction metadata alongside the decoded instruction so EX can validate or recover from the prediction.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Compare the resolved branch/jump next PC with the carried prediction and issue redirects only on mispredictions, preserving trap and RVFI pc_next semantics.\"}],\"outcome\":\"improvement\",\"fitness\":310.56,\"delta_pct\":9.81,\"vs_baseline\":9.81,\"fmax_mhz\":132.29,\"ipc_coremark\":0.000002,\"cycles\":4259699,\"iterations\":10,\"lut4\":10554,\"ff\":1897,\"seeds\":[128.47,132.29,133.98],\"formal_passed\":true,\"cosim_passed\":true,\"error\":null,\"implementation_notes\":\"\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-07-10T20:04:27.584939Z\",\"slot\":2,\"round_id\":1,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r1s2 (improvement, +9.81%): A small IF-stage predictor for backward conditional branches and direct JALs, with prediction metadata carried through ID/EX and EX redirects only on next-PC mismatch, removes most CoreMark loop redirect bubbles without the area cost of a BTB/BHT.\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-003-r6s2\",\"title\":\"Shadow-link return predictor\",\"category\":\"predictor\",\"motivation\":\"The existing static predictor already covers backward CoreMark loops and\\ndirect JALs, leaving canonical JALR returns as the main recurring control\\nflow penalty. Prior BHT, loop-table, RAS, and tagged return-cache attempts\\neither aliased or placed expensive lookup and muxing on the IF critical\\npath. A predictor based directly on the architectural link registers can\\ntarget the same return pattern with substantially less state and timing\\noverhead.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The existing static predictor already covers backward CoreMark loops and\\ndirect JALs, leaving canonical JALR returns as the main recurring control\\nflow penalty. Prior BHT, loop-table, RAS, and tagged return-cache attempts\\neither aliased or placed expensive lookup and muxing on the IF critical\\npath. A predictor based directly on the architectural link registers can\\ntarget the same return pattern with substantially less state and timing\\noverhead.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Add reset-valid shadow registers for x1 and x5, updated at writeback from\\nthe ordinary architectural write stream. In IF, when the fetched\\ninstruction is the canonical return-form JALR (rd=x0, funct3=0, rs1=x1 or\\nx5), use the corresponding shadow link value plus the decoded immediate as\\nthe predicted target; otherwise retain the current backward-branch and\\ndirect-JAL predictor. Carry the existing prediction metadata unchanged so\\nEX still resolves every return and redirects only on a mismatch. This\\nremoves repeated return bubbles without a tag compare, BHT aliasing, RAS\\nstack mux, or multi-entry target-table lookup; stale or nonstandard link\\nvalues remain harmless because the existing precise redirect recovery\\nremains authoritative.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":3,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Add two valid shadow link registers and a narrow canonical-return JALR prediction path that uses x1/x5 plus the decoded immediate, while preserving existing static predictions and redirect fallback.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Connect the writeback architectural write-enable, destination, and data to IF so the shadow link registers track committed x1/x5 values without changing the external IO or RVFI contract.\"}]},\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":3,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Add two valid shadow link registers and a narrow canonical-return JALR prediction path that uses x1/x5 plus the decoded immediate, while preserving existing static predictions and redirect fallback.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Connect the writeback architectural write-enable, destination, and data to IF so the shadow link registers track committed x1/x5 values without changing the external IO or RVFI contract.\"}],\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"fitness\":375.45,\"delta_pct\":-5.28,\"vs_baseline\":32.75,\"fmax_mhz\":161.92,\"ipc_coremark\":0.000002,\"cycles\":4312687,\"iterations\":10,\"lut4\":10577,\"ff\":2144,\"seeds\":[161.79,161.92,173.64],\"formal_passed\":true,\"cosim_passed\":true,\"error\":null,\"implementation_notes\":\"\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-07-10T21:57:51.602940Z\",\"slot\":2,\"round_id\":6,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r6s2 (regression, -5.28%): A writeback-fed x1/x5 shadow predictor can lose CoreMark throughput when return decode, valid compares, and a 32-bit link-plus-immediate adder enter the IF next-PC cone, so return-bubble savings must be weighed against fetch timing and stale-link mispredict redirects.\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-003-r7s2\",\"title\":\"Selective gshare forward-branch predictor\",\"category\":\"predictor\",\"motivation\":\"The current static predictor is effective for CoreMark's backward loops and\\ndirect JALs, but it leaves every forward conditional branch not-taken. The\\nearlier PC-only 16-entry BHT regressed because it aliased branch sites and\\nused a harmful weak-taken startup bias, while larger tagged predictors hurt\\nthe IF timing path. A predictor that targets only the remaining forward\\nbranches can add useful direction information without disturbing the proven\\nloop prediction policy.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The current static predictor is effective for CoreMark's backward loops and\\ndirect JALs, but it leaves every forward conditional branch not-taken. The\\nearlier PC-only 16-entry BHT regressed because it aliased branch sites and\\nused a harmful weak-taken startup bias, while larger tagged predictors hurt\\nthe IF timing path. A predictor that targets only the remaining forward\\nbranches can add useful direction information without disturbing the proven\\nloop prediction policy.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Add a small 32-entry, 2-bit gshare direction table for forward conditional\\nbranches. Index the table with a low PC slice XORed with a short global\\nconditional-branch history, initialize counters weakly not-taken, and update\\nthe counter from the precise EX branch outcome. Use the table only when the\\nbranch immediate is forward; retain the existing static backward-taken and\\ndirect-JAL predictions for all other control flow. Carry the existing\\nprediction metadata and redirect on a resolved next-PC mismatch, so cold\\nentries and history aliasing recover precisely without changing RVFI or\\narchitectural behavior. The XOR history should separate recurring CoreMark\\nbranch contexts better than the failed PC-only BHT while adding only a small\\ncounter array and narrow update state.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":3,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Add the small gshare history/counter state, use it only to choose taken predictions for forward conditional branches, preserve the existing backward-branch and direct-JAL static cases, and update state from resolved branches.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Expose a precise conditional-branch update event containing the resolved branch PC, direction, and validity while leaving redirect, trap, and RVFI next-PC behavior unchanged.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire the EX branch-resolution update event into the IF predictor without changing the external bus or single-channel RVFI contract.\"}]},\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":3,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Add the small gshare history/counter state, use it only to choose taken predictions for forward conditional branches, preserve the existing backward-branch and direct-JAL static cases, and update state from resolved branches.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Expose a precise conditional-branch update event containing the resolved branch PC, direction, and validity while leaving redirect, trap, and RVFI next-PC behavior unchanged.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Wire the EX branch-resolution update event into the IF predictor without changing the external bus or single-channel RVFI contract.\"}],\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"fitness\":403.25,\"delta_pct\":1.74,\"vs_baseline\":42.58,\"fmax_mhz\":174.67,\"ipc_coremark\":0.000002,\"cycles\":4331511,\"iterations\":10,\"lut4\":10400,\"ff\":2145,\"seeds\":[184.77,164.07,174.67],\"formal_passed\":true,\"cosim_passed\":true,\"error\":null,\"implementation_notes\":\"\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-07-10T22:18:02.863966Z\",\"slot\":2,\"round_id\":7,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r7s2 (regression, +1.74%): Even a weakly-not-taken, forward-only 32-entry gshare can regress CoreMark when the combinational `forward_bht[prediction_index][1]` lookup and global-history update add IF-path/state cost that the benchmark's relatively few useful forward-taken predictions do not repay.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
