capture in one timing\n  interval.  The earlier broad memory retiming attempt failed placement\n  because it carried wide request and retirement payloads through added\n  control.  A narrower boundary can target the likely memory critical path\n  without replicating the whole backend or adding a completion queue.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a registered, compact memory-response stage between the existing\n  EX/MEM request and MEM/WB retirement paths.  Capture only the accepted raw\n  dmem read word plus byte offset, width/sign metadata, operation kind, and\n  the minimum destination/valid token; perform load extraction and\n  sign-extension after that register while carrying the existing retirement\n  sideband in age order.  Stores and loads must remain one operation per\n  cycle when io_dmemReady is high, while a dmem stall holds the request and\n  response token atomically.  This should isolate FPGA memory-output timing\n  from the load-formatting cone and improve Fmax with one extra load latency,\n  while preserving precise load-use forwarding, store ordering, RVFI memory\n  fields, rvfi_order, and all external buses.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Define a narrow registered memory-response payload containing raw read data, lane/width/sign metadata, operation validity, and the retirement token needed to align loads and stores.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Split memory request acceptance from response formatting, registering the compact response only on dmem-ready and preserving byte masks, load semantics, store effects, and deterministic RVFI payloads.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Adjust dmem-stall, load-use, and forwarding timing for the extra response boundary without allowing duplicate requests or retirement.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the compact response and delayed load-forwarding result into the existing single-issue pipeline while retaining the unchanged top-level IO and RVFI contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
