:20.23-20.37): 28\\\\nSBY  2:58:03 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:10  Assert failed in rvfi_testbench: rvfi_reg_check.sv:44.6-44.59 (_witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_reg_check_sv_44_62)\\\\nSBY  2:58:03 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:10  Writing trace to VCD file: engine_0/trace.vcd\\\\nSBY  2:58:03 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:10  Writing trace to Verilog testbench: engine_0/trace_tb.v\\\\nSBY  2:58:03 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:10  Writing trace to constraints file: engine_0/trace.smtc\\\\nSBY  2:58:03 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:10  Writing trace to Yosys witness file: engine_0/trace.yw\\\\nSBY  2:58:03 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:10  Status: failed\\\\nSBY  2:58:03 [reg_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=1)\\\\nSBY  2:58:03 [reg_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: FAIL\\\\nSBY  2:58:03 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:11 (11)\\\\nSBY  2:58:03 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:08 (8)\\\\nSBY  2:58:03 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned FAIL\\\\nSBY  2:58:03 [reg_ch0] summary: counterexample trace: reg_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\\\nSBY  2:58:03 [reg_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_reg_check_sv_44_62 at rvfi_reg_check.sv:44.6-44.59 step 20\\\\nSBY  2:58:03 [reg_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\\\n\\\\nFull run log: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/kimi-k2_6-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260514-001-r7s0/formal/last_run-63200.log\\\\nPer-check logs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/kimi-k2_6-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260514-001-r7s0/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-63200/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 0, \\\"round_id\\\": 7, \\\"scribe_skipped\\\": \\\"TimeoutError: scribe timed out after 240s\\\"}\\n{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260514-002-r7s1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Replace combinational divider with iterative multi-cycle unit\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current ALU infers a full 32-bit combinational divider from the\\\\nSystemVerilog `/` and `%` operators. Flattened synthesis shows the EX\\\\nstage alone consumes over 6000 cells (52 % of the entire core) and is\\\\ndominated by arithmetic primitives. Division is essentially unused in\\\\nCoreMark, yet the combinational divider consumes massive area and\\\\nrouting resources that congest the fabric around the critical ALU adder\\\\npath, limiting Fmax. A prior attempt at this change failed because the\\\\ndivider state machine lacked a proper IDLE/RUNNING/DONE FSM with a\\\\n'started' bit, causing deadlock. With a correct FSM implementation,\\\\nremoving the combinational divider should relieve routing congestion\\\\nand raise Fmax with negligible IPC impact.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current ALU infers a full 32-bit combinational divider from the\\\\nSystemVerilog `/` and `%` operators. Flattened synthesis shows the EX\\\\nstage alone consumes over 6000 cells (52 % of the entire core) and is\\\\ndominated by arithmetic primitives. Division is essentially unused in\\\\nCoreMark, yet the combinational divider consumes massive area and\\\\nrouting resources that congest the fabric around the critical ALU adder\\\\npath, limiting Fmax. A prior attempt at this change failed because the\\\\ndivider state machine lacked a proper IDLE/RUNNING/DONE FSM with a\\\\n'started' bit, causing deadlock. With a correct FSM implementation,\\\\nremoving the combinational divider should relieve routing congestion\\\\nand raise Fmax with negligible IPC impact.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Extract DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU out of the combinational ALU into a new\\\\n`divider.sv` module that performs restoring division in 33 cycles.\\\\nThe divider MUST use a proper 3-state FSM (IDLE, RUNNING, DONE) with\\\\na registered 'started' bit:\\\\n  - IDLE:  waiting for start pulse. busy=0, done=0.\\\\n  - RUNNING: counting down 32 bits. busy=1, done=0.\\\\n  - DONE: result valid for one cycle. busy=0, done=1. Next clock\\\\n    returns to IDLE automatically.\\\\nIn `ex_stage`, detect divide ops and assert `div_start` for exactly\\\\none cycle when the divider is in IDLE. The hazard unit stalls IF,\\\\nID, and EX/MEM while `div_busy` (= RUNNING) is high. Because `busy`\\\\nis LOW in the DONE state, the EX/MEM register naturally captures the\\\\ndivider result on the done cycle and the next instruction can enter\\\\nEX on the following cycle. The main ALU keeps all I-type ops and the\\\\nmultiplier path. This structural change shrinks the EX stage\\\\nsignificantly, frees routing capacity on the critical path, and\\\\nshould improve median Fmax without hurting CoreMark IPC.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 6, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Remove DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU cases and all combinational divide/rem\\\\nlogic. Keep the multiplier paths and the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\\\\nbranch unchanged.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/divider.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"New iterative restoring divider with IDLE/RUNNING/DONE FSM.\\\\nInputs: clock, reset, start, dividend[31:0], divisor[31:0],\\\\nop[3:0] selecting DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU. Outputs: result[31:0],\\\\nbusy, done. 33-cycle latency. busy is high only in RUNNING.\\\\ndone is high for one cycle in DONE. Returns to IDLE on next\\\\nclock edge. Handles all RV32M corner cases (divide by zero,\\\\nINT_MIN/-1).\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Detect divide ops from in.ctrl.alu_op. Route operands to the\\\\ndivider and assert div_start when the divider is idle.\\\\nCapture divider result into ex_mem_w.alu_result when div_done\\\\nis high. Stall EX/MEM via hazard_unit during div_busy.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add div_busy input. Extend stall_if, stall_id, and stall_ex_mem\\\\nto freeze the entire pipeline while div_busy is high. Do not\\\\nassert flush_id during div_busy; hold the pipeline state.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Instantiate divider module. Wire div_busy into hazard_unit.\\\\nConnect divider inputs from id_ex_w operands. No top-level IO\\\\nchanges.\\\\n\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 6, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Remove DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU cases and all combinational divide/rem\\\\nlogic. Keep the multiplier paths and the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\\\\nbranch unchanged.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/divider.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"New iterative restoring divider with IDLE/RUNNING/DONE FSM.\\\\nInputs: clock, reset, start, dividend[31:0], divisor[31:0],\\\\nop[3:0] selecting DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU. Outputs: result[31:0],\\\\nbusy, done. 33-cycle latency. busy is high only in RUNNING.\\\\ndone is high for one cycle in DONE. Returns to IDLE on next\\\\nclock edge. Handles all RV32M corner cases (divide by zero,\\\\nINT_MIN/-1).\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Detect divide ops from in.ctrl.alu_op. Route operands to the\\\\ndivider and assert div_start when the divider is idle.\\\\nCapture divider result into ex_mem_w.alu_result when div_done\\\\nis high. Stall EX/MEM via hazard_unit during div_busy.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add div_busy input. Extend stall_if, stall_id, and stall_ex_mem\\\\nto freeze the entire pipeline while div_busy is high. Do not\\\\nassert flush_id during div_busy; hold the pipeline state.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Instantiate divider module. Wire div_busy into hazard_unit.\\\\nConnect divider inputs from id_ex_w operands. No top-level IO\\\\nchanges.\\\\n\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 347.76, \\\"delta_pct\\\": 0.0, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 22.96, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 146.18, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4203461, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 10254, \\\"ff\\\": 1940, \\\"seeds\\\": [146.18, 132.82, 146.26], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-05-14T06:07:59.336648Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 1, \\\"round_id\\\": 7, \\\"scribe_skipped\\\": \\\"PermissionError: scribe touched off-limits paths and was rolled back: ['cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/core.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'cores/bench/test/test_alu.py', 'cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py', 'cores/bench/rtl/divider.sv', 'cores/bench/test/test_divider.py']\\\"}\\n{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260514-003-r7s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/kimi-k2_6-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260514-003-r7s2.yaml\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"broken\\\", \\\"formal_passed\\\": false, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": false, \\\"error\\\": \\\"schema_error: 'category' is a required property\\\\n\\\\nFailed validating 'required' in schema:\\\\n    {'$schema': 'http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#',\\\\n     'type': 'object',\\\\n     'required': ['id',\\\\n                  'title',\\\\n                  'category',\\\\n                  'motivation',\\\\n                  'hypothesis',\\\\n                  'expected_impact',\\\\n                  'changes'],\\\\n     'properties': {'id': {'type': 'string',\\\\n                           'pattern': '^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$'},\\\\n                    'title': {'type': 'string', 'minLength': 5},\\\\n                    'category': {'type': 'string',\\\\n                                 'enum': ['micro_opt',\\\\n                                          'structural',\\\\n                                          'extension',\\\\n                                          'predictor',\\\\n                                          'memory']},\\\\n                    'motivation': {'type': 'string', 'minLength': 20},\\\\n                    'hypothesis': {'type': 'string', 'minLength': 20},\\\\n                    'expected_impact': {'type': 'object',\\\\n                                        'required': ['fitness_delta_pct',\\\\n                                                     'confidence'],\\\\n                                        'properties': {'fitness_delta_pct': {'type': 'integer'},\\\\n                                                       'confidence': {'type': 'string',\\\\n                                                                      'enum': ['low',\\\\n                                                                               'medium',\\\\n                                                                               'high']}}},\\\\n                    'changes': {'type': 'array',\\\\n                                'minItems': 1,\\\\n                                'items': {'type': 'object',\\\\n                                          'required': ['file',\\\\n                                                       'description'],\\\\n                                          'properties': {'file': {'type': 'string',\\\\n                                                                  'description': 'Must '\\\\n                                                                                 'be '\\\\n                                                                                 'under '\\\\n                                                                                 'rtl/ '\\\\n                                                                                 '(any '\\\\n                                                                                 'extension) '\\\\n                                                                                 'or '\\\\n                                                                                 'be '\\\\n                                                                                 'a '\\\\n                                                                                 'test/test_*.py '\\\\n                                                                                 'cocotb '\\\\n                                                                                 'suite. '\\\\n                                                                                 'Anything '\\\\n                                                                                 'else '\\\\n                                                                                 'is '\\\\n                                                                                 'rejected '\\\\n                                                                                 'by '\\\\n                                                                                 'the '\\\\n                                                                                 'runtime '\\\\n                                                                                 'sandbox '\\\\n                                                                                 'check.',\\\\n                                                                  'pattern': '^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.py)$'},\\\\n                                                         'description': {'type': 'string'}}}}}}\\\\n\\\\nOn instance:\\\\n    {'id': 'hyp-20260514-003-r7s2',\\\\n     'title': 'Fix gshare by speculatively updating GHR in IF with '\\\\n              'mispredict restore',\\\\n     'motivation': 'The prior 32-entry BHT added +7.3% fitness, but a '\\\\n                   'follow-up gshare variant\\\\\\\\n'\\\\n                   'regressed -6.7% because its GHR was updated '\\\\n                   'non-speculatively in EX. By the\\\\\\\\n'\\\\n                   'time a branch resolved, the next branch had already '\\\\n                   'been fetched with stale\\\\\\\\n'\\\\n                   'history, increasing destructive aliasing. CoreMark '\\\\n                   'contains short basic blocks\\\\\\\\n'\\\\n                   'with back-to-back branches where history staleness is '\\\\n                   'fatal.\\\\\\\\n',\\\\n     'hypothesis': 'Replace the non-speculative EX-stage GHR update with a '\\\\n                   'speculative IF-stage\\\\\\\\n'\\\\n                   'update plus EX-stage restore on mispredict. A 5-bit '\\\\n                   'GHR register in IF is\\\\\\\\n'\\\\n                   'shifted left with predict_taken whenever a conditional '\\\\n                   'branch is fetched.\\\\\\\\n'\\\\n                   'The pre-update GHR value is snapshotted into a new '\\\\n                   '5-bit field in the IF/ID\\\\\\\\n'\\\\n                   'and ID/EX bundles. In EX, when a conditional branch '\\\\n                   'mispredicts (redirect),\\\\\\\\n'\\\\n                   'the GHR is restored to {snapshot[3:0], actual_taken}; '\\\\n                   'on correct prediction\\\\\\\\n'\\\\n                   'the speculative update is already exact and needs no '\\\\n                   'action. The BHT read\\\\\\\\n'\\\\n                   'index remains pc[6:2] ^ ghr and the update index '\\\\n                   'remains pc[6:2] ^ snapshot.\\\\\\\\n'\\\\n                   'This gives the 32-entry BHT history-aware indexing '\\\\n                   'without any Fmax penalty\\\\\\\\n'\\\\n                   'from a larger array, and fixes the staleness that '\\\\n                   'broke the first gshare.\\\\\\\\n',\\\\n     'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 4, 'confidence': 'medium'},\\\\n     'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/core_pkg.sv',\\\\n                  'description': 'Add a 5-bit ghr_snapshot field to '\\\\n                                 'if_id_t and id_ex_t pipeline bundles.'},\\\\n                 {'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv',\\\\n                  'description': 'Add a 5-bit ghr register initialised to '\\\\n                                 '0. Compute BHT read index as pc[6:2] ^ '\\\\n                                 'ghr. Drive the current ghr value into '\\\\n                                 'out.ghr_snapshot. On non-stalled, '\\\\n                                 'non-flushed cycles where the fetched '\\\\n                                 'instruction is a conditional branch, '\\\\n                                 'speculatively update ghr <= {ghr[3:0], '\\\\n                                 'predict_taken}. Add a new input port '\\\\n                                 'ghr_restore[4:0] and ghr_restore_en; '\\\\n                                 'when restore_en is asserted on redirect '\\\\n                                 'from EX, reload ghr with ghr_restore.\\\\\\\\n'},\\\\n                 {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv',\\\\n                  'description': 'Capture in.ghr_snapshot into the ID/EX '\\\\n                                 'register so it reaches EX.'},\\\\n                 {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv',\\\\n                  'description': 'Compute BHT update index as in.pc[6:2] ^ '\\\\n                                 'in.ghr_snapshot so the counter update '\\\\n                                 'writes the exact entry that was read '\\\\n                                 'during fetch. Add output ports '\\\\n                                 'ghr_restore[4:0] and ghr_restore_en. '\\\\n                                 'Drive ghr_restore = '\\\\n                                 '{in.ghr_snapshot[3:0], branch_taken} and '\\\\n                                 'assert ghr_restore_en whenever redirect '\\\\n                                 'is asserted for a conditional branch '\\\\n                                 '(in.ctrl.is_branch). JAL/JALR redirects '\\\\n                                 'must not assert restore_en.\\\\\\\\n'},\\\\n                 {'file': 'rtl/core.sv',\\\\n                  'description': 'Wire the new ghr_restore/ghr_restore_en '\\\\n                                 'signals from ex_stage back to '\\\\n                                 'if_stage.'}]}\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 2, \\\"round_id\\\": 7, \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The prior 32-entry BHT added +7.3% fitness, but a follow-up gshare variant\\\\nregressed -6.7% because its GHR was updated non-speculatively in EX. By the\\\\ntime a branch resolved, the next branch had already been fetched with stale\\\\nhistory, increasing destructive aliasing. CoreMark contains short basic blocks\\\\nwith back-to-back branches where history staleness is fatal.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Replace the non-speculative EX-stage GHR update with a speculative IF-stage\\\\nupdate plus EX-stage restore on mispredict. A 5-bit GHR register in IF is\\\\nshifted left with predict_taken whenever a conditional branch is fetched.\\\\nThe pre-update GHR value is snapshotted into a new 5-bit field in the IF/ID\\\\nand ID/EX bundles. In EX, when a conditional branch mispredicts (redirect),\\\\nthe GHR is restored to {snapshot[3:0], actual_taken}; on correct prediction\\\\nthe speculative update is already exact and needs no action. The BHT read\\\\nindex remains pc[6:2] ^ ghr and the update index remains pc[6:2] ^ snapshot.\\\\nThis gives the 32-entry BHT history-aware indexing without any Fmax penalty\\\\nfrom a larger array, and fixes the staleness that broke the first gshare.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a 5-bit ghr_snapshot field to if_id_t and id_ex_t pipeline bundles.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a 5-bit ghr register initialised to 0. Compute BHT read index as pc[6:2] ^ ghr. Drive the current ghr value into out.ghr_snapshot. On non-stalled, non-flushed cycles where the fetched instruction is a conditional branch, speculatively update ghr <= {ghr[3:0], predict_taken}. Add a new input port ghr_restore[4:0] and ghr_restore_en; when restore_en is asserted on redirect from EX, reload ghr with ghr_restore.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Capture in.ghr_snapshot into the ID/EX register so it reaches EX.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Compute BHT update index as in.pc[6:2] ^ in.ghr_snapshot so the counter update writes the exact entry that was read during fetch. Add output ports ghr_restore[4:0] and ghr_restore_en. Drive ghr_restore = {in.ghr_snapshot[3:0], branch_taken} and assert ghr_restore_en whenever redirect is asserted for a conditional branch (in.ctrl.is_branch). JAL/JALR redirects must not assert restore_en.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire the new ghr_restore/ghr_restore_en signals from ex_stage back to if_stage.\\\"}]}}\\n{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260514-003-r9s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Fix gshare by speculatively updating GHR in IF with mispredict restore\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The 32-entry bimodal BHT already yielded +7.3% fitness, but a follow-up\\\\ngshare variant regressed -6.7% because its GHR was updated non-speculatively\\\\nin EX. By the time a branch resolved, the next branch had already been\\\\nfetched with stale history, increasing destructive aliasing. CoreMark\\\\ncontains short basic blocks with back-to-back branches where history\\\\nstaleness is fatal. A speculative IF-stage update with EX-stage restore\\\\nfixes the staleness while keeping the table small and the read path fast.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The 32-entry bimodal BHT already yielded +7.3% fitness, but a follow-up\\\\ngshare variant regressed -6.7% because its GHR was updated non-speculatively\\\\nin EX. By the time a branch resolved, the next branch had already been\\\\nfetched with stale history, increasing destructive aliasing. CoreMark\\\\ncontains short basic blocks with back-to-back branches where history\\\\nstaleness is fatal. A speculative IF-stage update with EX-stage restore\\\\nfixes the staleness while keeping the table small and the read path fast.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a 5-bit Global History Register (GHR) to the IF stage and XOR it into\\\\nthe existing 32-entry BHT index (gshare). The GHR is updated speculatively\\\\nwhenever a conditional branch is fetched: ghr <= {ghr[3:0], predict_taken}.\\\\nThe pre-update GHR value is snapshotted into a new 5-bit field in the\\\\nIF/ID and ID/EX bundles. In EX, when a conditional branch mispredicts\\\\n(redirect is asserted), the GHR is restored to {snapshot[3:0], actual_taken}\\\\nvia a new feedback port to IF. On correct prediction no restore is needed.\\\\nThe BHT write index uses pc[6:2] ^ snapshot so the counter update hits the\\\\nsame entry that was read during fetch. This gives history-aware prediction\\\\nwithout enlarging the array and with negligible combinational delay (a\\\\n5-bit XOR on an existing mux path).\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a 5-bit ghr_snapshot field to if_id_t and id_ex_t pipeline bundles\\\\nso the GHR value present at fetch time reaches EX for update-index\\\\ncalculation and mispredict restore.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a 5-bit ghr register initialised to 0. Replace the BHT read index\\\\npc[6:2] with pc[6:2] ^ ghr. Drive the current ghr value into\\\\nout.ghr_snapshot. On non-stalled, non-flushed, non-redirected cycles\\\\nwhere the fetched instruction is a conditional branch, speculatively\\\\nupdate ghr <= {ghr[3:0], bht_pred}. Add new input ports\\\\nghr_restore[4:0] and ghr_restore_en; when restore_en is asserted\\\\n(from EX on a conditional-branch mispredict), reload ghr with\\\\nghr_restore, taking precedence over the speculative update.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Capture in.ghr_snapshot into the ID/EX register so the snapshot\\\\nreaches the EX stage for BHT update-index computation and GHR restore.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Compute BHT update index as in.pc[6:2] ^ in.ghr_snapshot so the\\\\nsaturating-counter update writes the exact entry that was read during\\\\nfetch. Add output ports ghr_restore[4:0] and ghr_restore_en. Drive\\\\nghr_restore = {in.ghr_snapshot[3:0], branch_taken} and assert\\\\nghr_restore_en whenever redirect is asserted for a conditional branch\\\\n(in.ctrl.is_branch). JAL/JALR redirects must not assert ghr_restore_en.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Instantiate new wires ghr_restore[4:0] and ghr_restore_en and route\\\\nthem from ex_stage outputs back to if_stage inputs. No top-level IO\\\\nor RVFI changes are required.\\\\n\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a 5-bit ghr_snapshot field to if_id_t and id_ex_t pipeline bundles\\\\nso the GHR value present at fetch time reaches EX for update-index\\\\ncalculation and mispredict restore.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a 5-bit ghr register initialised to 0. Replace the BHT read index\\\\npc[6:2] with pc[6:2] ^ ghr. Drive the current ghr value into\\\\nout.ghr_snapshot. On non-stalled, non-flushed, non-redirected cycles\\\\nwhere the fetched instruction is a conditional branch, speculatively\\\\nupdate ghr <= {ghr[3:0], bht_pred}. Add new input ports\\\\nghr_restore[4:0] and ghr_restore_en; when restore_en is asserted\\\\n(from EX on a conditional-branch mispredict), reload ghr with\\\\nghr_restore, taking precedence over the speculative update.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Capture in.ghr_snapshot into the ID/EX register so the snapshot\\\\nreaches the EX stage for BHT update-index computation and GHR restore.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Compute BHT update index as in.pc[6:2] ^ in.ghr_snapshot so the\\\\nsaturating-counter update writes the exact entry that was read during\\\\nfetch. Add output ports ghr_restore[4:0] and ghr_restore_en. Drive\\\\nghr_restore = {in.ghr_snapshot[3:0], branch_taken} and assert\\\\nghr_restore_en whenever redirect is asserted for a conditional branch\\\\n(in.ctrl.is_branch). JAL/JALR redirects must not assert ghr_restore_en.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Instantiate new wires ghr_restore[4:0] and ghr_restore_en and route\\\\nthem from ex_stage outputs back to if_stage inputs. No top-level IO\\\\nor RVFI changes are required.\\\\n\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 347.76, \\\"delta_pct\\\": 0.0, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 22.96, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 146.18, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4203461, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 10254, \\\"ff\\\": 1940, \\\"seeds\\\": [146.18, 132.82, 146.26], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-05-14T06:55:45.098358Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 2, \\\"round_id\\\": 9, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-003-r9s2 (regression, +0.00%): Speculative IF-stage GHR update with mispredict restore fixes the history-staleness bug but still yields zero net gain over the bimodal 32-entry BHT; CoreMark's branch working set is small enough that 2-bit saturating counters capture all exploitable locality, leaving global history with no accuracy upside.\\\"}\\n\",\"metadata\":{\"output\":\"...\\n\\nnally by comparing in.instr[19:15] and in.instr[24:20] against reg_q.rd and ex_mem_rd with the same write-enable / x0 guards used by forward_unit. Register the resulting 2-bit values into the ID/EX payload.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Remove the fwd_rs1_sel and fwd_rs2_sel input ports. Use in.fwd_rs1_sel and in.fwd_rs2_sel directly in the rs1/rs2 forwarding muxes instead of the former forward_unit-driven selects.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire ex_mem_w.rd and ex_mem_w.ctrl.reg_write into the id_stage instance for precomputation.  Remove the forward_unit instantiation and its wires.  Connect id_ex_w.fwd_rs1_sel and id_ex_w.fwd_rs2_sel directly to ex_stage.\\\\n\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add fwd_rs1_sel [1:0] and fwd_rs2_sel [1:0] fields to the id_ex_t struct.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/id_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add inputs ex_mem_rd [4:0] and ex_mem_reg_write. Compute next_fwd_rs1/next_fwd_rs2 combinationally by comparing in.instr[19:15] and in.instr[24:20] against reg_q.rd and ex_mem_rd with the same write-enable / x0 guards used by forward_unit. Register the resulting 2-bit values into the ID/EX payload.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Remove the fwd_rs1_sel and fwd_rs2_sel input ports. Use in.fwd_rs1_sel and in.fwd_rs2_sel directly in the rs1/rs2 forwarding muxes instead of the former forward_unit-driven selects.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Wire ex_mem_w.rd and ex_mem_w.ctrl.reg_write into the id_stage instance 