ker_inst__assert_rvfi_reg_check_sv_44_62 at rvfi_reg_check.sv:44.6-44.59 step 20\\\\nSBY  2:58:03 [reg_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\\\n\\\\nFull run log: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/kimi-k2_6-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260514-001-r7s0/formal/last_run-63200.log\\\\nPer-check logs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/kimi-k2_6-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260514-001-r7s0/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-63200/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 0, \\\"round_id\\\": 7, \\\"scribe_skipped\\\": \\\"TimeoutError: scribe timed out after 240s\\\"}\\n{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260514-002-r7s1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Replace combinational divider with iterative multi-cycle unit\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current ALU infers a full 32-bit combinational divider from the\\\\nSystemVerilog `/` and `%` operators. Flattened synthesis shows the EX\\\\nstage alone consumes over 6000 cells (52 % of the entire core) and is\\\\ndominated by arithmetic primitives. Division is essentially unused in\\\\nCoreMark, yet the combinational divider consumes massive area and\\\\nrouting resources that congest the fabric around the critical ALU adder\\\\npath, limiting Fmax. A prior attempt at this change failed because the\\\\ndivider state machine lacked a proper IDLE/RUNNING/DONE FSM with a\\\\n'started' bit, causing deadlock. With a correct FSM implementation,\\\\nremoving the combinational divider should relieve routing congestion\\\\nand raise Fmax with negligible IPC impact.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current ALU infers a full 32-bit combinational divider from the\\\\nSystemVerilog `/` and `%` operators. Flattened synthesis shows the EX\\\\nstage alone consumes over 6000 cells (52 % of the entire core) and is\\\\ndominated by arithmetic primitives. Division is essentially unused in\\\\nCoreMark, yet the combinational divider consumes massive area and\\\\nrouting resources that congest the fabric around the critical ALU adder\\\\npath, limiting Fmax. A prior attempt at this change failed because the\\\\ndivider state machine lacked a proper IDLE/RUNNING/DONE FSM with a\\\\n'started' bit, causing deadlock. With a correct FSM implementation,\\\\nremoving the combinational divider should relieve routing congestion\\\\nand raise Fmax with negligible IPC impact.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Extract DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU out of the combinational ALU into a new\\\\n`divider.sv` module that performs restoring division in 33 cycles.\\\\nThe divider MUST use a proper 3-state FSM (IDLE, RUNNING, DONE) with\\\\na registered 'started' bit:\\\\n  - IDLE:  waiting for start pulse. busy=0, done=0.\\\\n  - RUNNING: counting down 32 bits. busy=1, done=0.\\\\n  - DONE: result valid for one cycle. busy=0, done=1. Next clock\\\\n    returns to IDLE automatically.\\\\nIn `ex_stage`, detect divide ops and assert `div_start` for exactly\\\\none cycle when the divider is in IDLE. The hazard unit stalls IF,\\\\nID, and EX/MEM while `div_busy` (= RUNNING) is high. Because `busy`\\\\nis LOW in the DONE state, the EX/MEM register naturally captures the\\\\ndivider result on the done cycle and the next instruction can enter\\\\nEX on the following cycle. The main ALU keeps all I-type ops and the\\\\nmultiplier path. This structural change shrinks the EX stage\\\\nsignificantly, frees routing capacity on the critical path, and\\\\nshould improve median Fmax without hurting CoreMark IPC.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 6, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Remove DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU cases and all combinational divide/rem\\\\nlogic. Keep the multiplier paths and the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\\\\nbranch unchanged.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/divider.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"New iterative restoring divider with IDLE/RUNNING/DONE FSM.\\\\nInputs: clock, reset, start, dividend[31:0], divisor[31:0],\\\\nop[3:0] selecting DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU. Outputs: result[31:0],\\\\nbusy, done. 33-cycle latency. busy is high only in RUNNING.\\\\ndone is high for one cycle in DONE. Returns to IDLE on next\\\\nclock edge. Handles all RV32M corner cases (divide by zero,\\\\nINT_MIN/-1).\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Detect divide ops from in.ctrl.alu_op. Route operands to the\\\\ndivider and assert div_start when the divider is idle.\\\\nCapture divider result into ex_mem_w.alu_result when div_done\\\\nis high. Stall EX/MEM via hazard_unit during div_busy.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add div_busy input. Extend stall_if, stall_id, and stall_ex_mem\\\\nto freeze the entire pipeline while div_busy is high. Do not\\\\nassert flush_id during div_busy; hold the pipeline state.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Instantiate divider module. Wire div_busy into hazard_unit.\\\\nConnect divider inputs from id_ex_w operands. No top-level IO\\\\nchanges.\\\\n\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 6, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Remove DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU cases and all combinational divide/rem\\\\nlogic. Keep the multiplier paths and the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\\\\nbranch unchanged.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/divider.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"New iterative restoring divider with IDLE/RUNNING/DONE FSM.\\\\nInputs: clock, reset, start, dividend[31:0], divisor[31:0],\\\\nop[3:0] selecting DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU. Outputs: result[31:0],\\\\nbusy, done. 33-cycle latency. busy is high only in RUNNING.\\\\ndone is high for one cycle in DONE. Returns to IDLE on next\\\\nclock edge. Handles all RV32M corner cases (divide by zero,\\\\nINT_MIN/-1).\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Detect divide ops from in.ctrl.alu_op. Route operands to the\\\\ndivider and assert div_start when the divider is idle.\\\\nCapture divider result into ex_mem_w.alu_result when div_done\\\\nis high. Stall EX/MEM via hazard_unit during div_busy.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add div_busy input. Extend stall_if, stall_id, and stall_ex_mem\\\\nto freeze the entire pipeline while div_busy is high. Do not\\\\nassert flush_id during div_busy; hold the pipeline state.\\\\n\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Instantiate divider module. Wire div_busy into hazard_unit.\\\\nConnect divider inputs from id_ex_w operands. No top-level IO\\\\nchanges.\\\\n\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 347.76, \\\"delta_pct\\\": 0.0, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 22.96, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 146.18, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4203461, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 10254, \\\"ff\\\": 1940, \\\"seeds\\\": [146.18, 132.82, 146.26], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-05-14T06:07:59.336648Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 1, \\\"round_id\\\": 7, \\\"scribe_skipped\\\": \\\"PermissionError: scribe touched off-limits paths and was rolled back: ['cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/core.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'cores/bench/test/test_alu.py', 'cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py', 'cores/bench/rtl/divider.sv', 'cores/bench/test/test_divider.py']\\\"}\\n{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260514-003-r7s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/kimi-k2_6-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260514-003-r7s2.yaml\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"broken\\\", \\\"formal_passed\\\": false, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": false, \\\"error\\\": \\\"sche