jalr region\",\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"Disassemble hot jalr region\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778836380177,\"end\":1778836380181}},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"fc_088c612b537be815016a06e39c0db0819b979a1e32c38ed9ee\"}},\"id\":\"prt_e2ae919f3001jV3bBt1oCSd5ZK\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d51ad624ffe3QWHb1QQRha61G\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2ae78fca001IHMzySFBP7EDN4\"}}\nbench/gpt-5_4_xhigh/rep2/agent.log:1100:{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778836380345,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d51ad624ffe3QWHb1QQRha61G\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"bash\",\"callID\":\"call_eyaauPsyqZ2CPD5Y2CrfCBo3\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"riscv64-unknown-elf-objdump -d \\\"bench/programs/coremark.elf\\\" | rg -c \\\"\\\\b(beq|bne|blt|bge|bltu|bgeu)\\\\b\\\"\",\"timeout\":120000,\"workdir\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep2\",\"description\":\"Count CoreMark branch instructions\"},\"output\":\"184\\n\",\"metadata\":{\"output\":\"184\\n\",\"exit\":0,\"description\":\"Count CoreMark branch instructions\",\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"Count CoreMark branch instructions\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778836380337,\"end\":1778836380344}},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"fc_088c612b537be815016a06e39c0de0819baf7a8cfafa2fa480\"}},\"id\":\"prt_e2ae91a120016D8XldOR27sy0g\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d51ad624ffe3QWHb1QQRha61G\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2ae78fca001IHMzySFBP7EDN4\"}}\nbench/gpt-5_4_xhigh/rep2/agent.log:1331:{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778826406384,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d5b168d2ffe54h4Tbiec6gEOe\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"apply_patch\",\"callID\":\"call_UbXDcDdY57JnatSwDqO6zu4A\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"patchText\":\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r9s1.yaml\\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r9s1\\n+title: \\\"Resolve canonical RET in ID\\\"\\n+category: structural\\n+motivation: |\\n+  The current best `bench` core already removed the cheapest unconditional\\n+  control bubble by redirecting direct `JAL` in ID, but common `ret`\\n+  instructions still wait until EX. Full ID-stage BRANCH/JALR resolution\\n+  already proved too timing-expensive on Tang Nano 20K, so the next\\n+  structural step should target only the hottest JALR subcase that needs no\\n+  compare logic and usually no bypassing.\\n+hypothesis: |\\n+  Extend the existing ID redirect path to cover canonical aligned returns,\\n+  e.g. `jalr x0, x1, 0` and `jalr x0, x5, 0`, when the return-address\\n+  register is already architecturally available from the regfile/WB path. If\\n+  an older in-flight instruction still owns that source register, simply fall\\n+  back to the current EX-stage JALR path instead of adding the full ID-stage\\n+  bypass/interlock machinery that regressed earlier. This reuses the existing\\n+  `id_redirect` plumbing, carries an \\\"already redirected in ID\\\" bit through\\n+  the pipeline so EX suppresses the duplicate redirect, and should cut\\n+  another hot function-return bubble in CoreMark with much lower timing risk\\n+  than general early JALR/BRANCH resolution.\\n+expected_impact:\\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\\n+  confidence: medium\\n+changes:\\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Generalize the existing `jal_early_redirect` pipeline bit into an ID-resolved jump marker that can cover both direct `JAL` and narrow early-return `JALR` cases.\\\"\\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Detect canonical aligned return-form `JALR`s, use the existing regfile read data to form an early redirect target, and only assert the ID redirect when no older in-flight writer can still change `rs1`.\\\"\\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Plumb simple in-flight `rd`-match blocker signals from older pipeline stages into decode so early-return `JALR` only fires when the architectural source value is already available.\\\"\\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Treat ID-resolved return `JALR`s like the current early `JAL` path: keep normal `pc+4` writeback/RVFI behavior, but suppress the duplicate EX redirect and retain EX-side fallback behavior for non-early cases.\\\"\\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Reuse the existing ID redirect PC update and replay invalidation path for the broader ID-resolved jump class, updating any narrow `JAL` assumptions in the frontend comments or control naming.\\\"\\n*** End Patch\"},\"output\":\"Success. Updated the following files:\\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r9s1.yaml\",\"metadata\":{\"diff\":\"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r9s1.yaml\\n===================================================================\\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r9s1.yaml\\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep2/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r9s1.yaml\\n@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@\\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r9s1\\n+title: \\\"Resolve canonical RET in ID\\\"\\n+category: structural\\n+motivation: |\\n+  The current best `bench` core already removed the cheapest unconditional\\n+  control bubble by redirecting direct `JAL` in ID, but common `ret`\\n+  instructions still wait until EX. Full ID-stage BRANCH/JALR resolution\\n+  already proved too timing-expensive on Tang Nano 20K, so the next\\n+  structural step should target only the hottest JALR subcase that needs no\\n+  compare logic and usually no bypassing.\\n+hypothesis: |\\n+  Extend the existing ID redirect path to cover canonical aligned returns,\\n+  e.g. `jalr x0, x1, 0` and `jalr x0, x5, 0`, when the return-address\\n+  register is already architecturally available from the regfile/WB path. If\\n+  an older in-flight instruction still owns that source register, simply fall\\n+  back to the current EX-stage JALR path instead of adding the full ID-stage\\n+  bypass/interlock machinery that regressed earlier. This reuses the existing\\n+  `id_redirect` plumbing, carries an \\\"already redirected in ID\\\" bit through\\n+  the pipeline so EX suppresses the duplicate redirect, and should cut\\n+  another hot function-return bubble in CoreMark with much lower timing risk\\n+  than general early JALR/BRANCH resolution.\\n+expected_impact:\\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\\n+  confidence: medium\\n+changes:\\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Generalize the existing `jal_early_redirect` pipeline bit into an ID-resolved jump marker that can cover both direct `JAL` and narrow early-return `JALR` cases.\\\"\\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Detect canonical aligned return-form `JALR`s, use the existing regfile read data to form an early redirect target, and only assert the ID redirect when no older in-flight writer can still change `rs1`.\\\"\\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Plumb simple in-flight `rd`-match blocker signals from older pipeline stages into decode so early-return `JALR` only fires when the architectural source value is already available.\\\"\\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Treat ID-resolved return `JALR`s like the current early `JAL` path: keep normal `pc+4` writeback/RVFI behavior, but suppress the duplicate EX redirect and retain EX-side fallback behavior for non-early cases.\\\"\\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Reuse the existing ID redirect PC update and replay invalidation path for the broader ID-resolved jump class, updating any narrow `JAL` assumptions in the frontend comments or control naming.\\\"\\n\\n\",\"files\":[{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep2/core