{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r3s2.yaml && git diff -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r3s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r3s2\ntitle: \"Add a compact return-address stack predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The successful static predictor removes most backward-loop and direct-JAL\n  redirects, but JALR returns remain unpredicted and still pay the EX resolve\n  penalty on every function return. CoreMark contains frequent call/return\n  traffic, while the prior 16-entry BHT showed that a general PC-indexed table\n  can hurt both accuracy through aliasing and Fmax through added IF logic.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a small, low-associativity return-address stack (RAS) in IF for JALR\n  instructions whose source is x1 or x5 and whose destination is x0. Predict\n  the top stack entry as the next PC, while retaining the existing static\n  backward-branch and direct-JAL predictions for other control flow. Update\n  the RAS from resolved EX calls and returns, pushing pc+4 for link-register\n  JAL/JALR calls and popping on returns; use the existing prediction metadata\n  and next-PC comparison so a cold or imperfect RAS recovers through the\n  current redirect path. A 4-entry stack should cover CoreMark's shallow call\n  depth with substantially less tag-compare and aliasing cost than a BHT/BTB.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a compact return-address stack, recognize return-form JALR opcodes, and select the stack top as their predicted target while preserving the existing static branch/JAL predictor.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire resolved call/return classification and link addresses from EX into IF so RAS updates occur on the architectural control-flow event rather than arbitrary fetch aliases.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Expose precise JAL/JALR call and return update signals, including the resolved link address, without changing redirect, trap, or RVFI behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
