{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r6s2.yaml && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r6s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r6s2\ntitle: \"Shadow-link return predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The existing static predictor already covers backward CoreMark loops and\n  direct JALs, leaving canonical JALR returns as the main recurring control\n  flow penalty. Prior BHT, loop-table, RAS, and tagged return-cache attempts\n  either aliased or placed expensive lookup and muxing on the IF critical\n  path. A predictor based directly on the architectural link registers can\n  target the same return pattern with substantially less state and timing\n  overhead.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add reset-valid shadow registers for x1 and x5, updated at writeback from\n  the ordinary architectural write stream. In IF, when the fetched\n  instruction is the canonical return-form JALR (rd=x0, funct3=0, rs1=x1 or\n  x5), use the corresponding shadow link value plus the decoded immediate as\n  the predicted target; otherwise retain the current backward-branch and\n  direct-JAL predictor. Carry the existing prediction metadata unchanged so\n  EX still resolves every return and redirects only on a mismatch. This\n  removes repeated return bubbles without a tag compare, BHT aliasing, RAS\n  stack mux, or multi-entry target-table lookup; stale or nonstandard link\n  values remain harmless because the existing precise redirect recovery\n  remains authoritative.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add two valid shadow link registers and a narrow canonical-return JALR prediction path that uses x1/x5 plus the decoded immediate, while preserving existing static predictions and redirect fallback.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect the writeback architectural write-enable, destination, and data to IF so the shadow link registers track committed x1/x5 values without changing the external IO or RVFI contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
