{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r7s2.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r7s2.yaml && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r7s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r7s2\ntitle: \"Selective gshare forward-branch predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current static predictor is effective for CoreMark's backward loops and\n  direct JALs, but it leaves every forward conditional branch not-taken. The\n  earlier PC-only 16-entry BHT regressed because it aliased branch sites and\n  used a harmful weak-taken startup bias, while larger tagged predictors hurt\n  the IF timing path. A predictor that targets only the remaining forward\n  branches can add useful direction information without disturbing the proven\n  loop prediction policy.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a small 32-entry, 2-bit gshare direction table for forward conditional\n  branches. Index the table with a low PC slice XORed with a short global\n  conditional-branch history, initialize counters weakly not-taken, and update\n  the counter from the precise EX branch outcome. Use the table only when the\n  branch immediate is forward; retain the existing static backward-taken and\n  direct-JAL predictions for all other control flow. Carry the existing\n  prediction metadata and redirect on a resolved next-PC mismatch, so cold\n  entries and history aliasing recover precisely without changing RVFI or\n  architectural behavior. The XOR history should separate recurring CoreMark\n  branch contexts better than the failed PC-only BHT while adding only a small\n  counter array and narrow update state.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add the small gshare history/counter state, use it only to choose taken predictions for forward conditional branches, preserve the existing backward-branch and direct-JAL static cases, and update state from resolved branches.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Expose a precise conditional-branch update event containing the resolved branch PC, direction, and validity while leaving redirect, trap, and RVFI next-PC behavior unchanged.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the EX branch-resolution update event into the IF predictor without changing the external bus or single-channel RVFI contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
