{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.category==\\\"predictor\\\") | [.id,.title,.outcome,(.fitness//\\\"n/a\\\"),(.delta_pct//\\\"n/a\\\"),(.fmax_mhz//\\\"n/a\\\"),(.cycles//\\\"n/a\\\")] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl && rg -n 'category.:.predictor|\\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20260710-003-r1s2\tEarly static backward-branch prediction\timprovement\t310.56\t9.81\t132.29\t4259699\nhyp-20260710-003-r2s2\tAdd a tiny dynamic branch history predictor\tregression\t281.94\t-9.22\t118.96\t4219411\nhyp-20260710-003-r3s2\tAdd a compact return-address stack predictor\tregression\t266.64\t-14.14\t113.21\t4245805\nhyp-20260710-003-r4s2\tAdd a tagged loop-exit predictor\tregression\t244.72\t-22.88\t104.48\t4269318\nhyp-20260710-003-r5s2\tAdd a tiny exact-tag return target cache\tregression\t249.03\t-21.52\t105.82\t4249209\nhyp-20260710-003-r6s2\tShadow-link return predictor\tregression\t375.45\t-5.28\t161.92\t4312687\nhyp-20260710-003-r7s2\tSelective gshare forward-branch predictor\tregression\t403.25\t1.74\t174.67\t4331511\nhyp-20260710-003-r8s2\tNarrow zero-offset return predictor\tregression\t391.01\t-18.69\t168.63\t4312687\n4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Early static backward-branch prediction\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The bench core resolves conditional branches and jumps in EX, then flushes\\nyounger work and redirects the fetch PC. CoreMark contains many tight loops,\\nso taken backward branches repeatedly pay this avoidable redirect penalty.\\nThe fixture is already close to its LUT budget, making a table-based BTB/BHT\\na riskier tradeoff than a small decode-only predictor.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The bench core resolves conditional branches and jumps in EX, then flushes\\nyounger work and redirects the fetch PC. CoreMark contains many tight loops,\\nso taken backward branches repeatedly pay this avoidable redirect penalty.\\nThe fixture is already close to its LUT budget, making a table-based BTB/BHT\\na riskier tradeoff than a small decode-only predictor.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add an IF-stage static control-flow predictor that predicts valid backward\\nconditional branches taken and predicts direct JAL instructions to their\\nimmediately computed targets; leave forward branches and JALR unpredicted.\\nCarry the predicted next PC through ID/EX and make EX redirect only when the\\nresolved next PC differs from the prediction, recovering to the actual\\ntarget or fall-through PC on a miss. This should remove most EX redirect\\nbubbles from CoreMark loop branches with little area and timing overhead.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute aligned B/J immediates from the fetched instruction and select a predicted target for backward conditional branches and direct JALs before the EX redirect path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles with prediction-valid/target metadata needed to compare the prediction against the resolved next PC.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the IF-stage prediction metadata alongside the decoded instruction so EX can validate or recover from the prediction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare the resolved branch/jump next PC with the carried prediction and issue redirects only on mispredictions, preserving trap and RVFI pc_next semantics.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute aligned B/J immediates from the fetched instruction and select a predicted target for backward conditional branches and direct JALs before the EX redirect path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles with prediction-valid/target metadata needed to compare the prediction against the resolved next PC.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch the IF-stage prediction metadata alongside the decoded instruction so EX can validate or recover from the prediction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare the resolved branch/jump next PC with the carried prediction and issue redirects only on mispredictions, preserving trap and RVFI pc_next semantics.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 310.56, \"delta_pct\": 9.81, \"vs_baseline\": 9.81, \"fmax_mhz\": 132.29, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4259699, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10554, \"ff\": 1897, \"seeds\": [128.47, 132.29, 133.98], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T20:04:27.584939Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r1s2 (improvement, +9.81%): A small IF-stage predictor for backward conditional branches and direct JALs, with prediction metadata carried through ID/EX and EX redirects only on next-PC mismatch, removes most CoreMark loop redirect bubbles without the area cost of a BTB/BHT.\"}\n7:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r2s2\", \"title\": \"Add a tiny dynamic branch history predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current static predictor removes most taken backward-loop redirects, but\\nit still predicts every forward conditional branch as not taken and cannot\\nlearn recurring loop-exit or irregular branch behavior. CoreMark contains\\nrepeated control-flow patterns where a few bits of per-PC history can improve\\nprediction without the LUT and timing cost of a BTB.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current static predictor removes most taken backward-loop redirects, but\\nit still predicts every forward conditional branch as not taken and cannot\\nlearn recurring loop-exit or irregular branch behavior. CoreMark contains\\nrepeated control-flow patterns where a few bits of per-PC history can improve\\nprediction without the LUT and timing cost of a BTB.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a small PC-indexed 2-bit saturating branch history table in the IF stage.\\nUse the existing IF-stage B/J immediate target calculation, but consult the\\ntable for every valid conditional branch, with reset counters biased weakly\\ntaken so the existing backward-loop behavior is preserved. Update the\\ncounter at EX resolution for every conditional branch, carrying the existing\\nprediction metadata through the pipeline and redirecting only on a\\nnext-PC mismatch. This should retain the static predictor's loop benefit,\\nreduce forward-branch and repeated loop-exit mispredictions, and add only a\\nfew small registers plus a narrow update path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small PC-indexed 2-bit saturating BHT, use it to choose conditional-branch taken predictions while retaining direct target generation, and update the selected counter from resolved EX branch outcomes.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the EX branch-resolution PC, taken outcome, and update-valid signal into IF so the dynamic predictor learns every resolved conditional branch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose a precise conditional-branch predictor update event and outcome at EX resolution without changing redirect or RVFI retirement behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small PC-indexed 2-bit saturating BHT, use it to choose conditional-branch taken predictions while retaining direct target generation, and update the selected counter from resolved EX branch outcomes.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the EX branch-resolution PC, taken outcome, and update-valid signal into IF so the dynamic predictor learns every resolved conditional branch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose a precise conditional-branch predictor update event and outcome at EX resolution without changing redirect or RVFI retirement behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 281.94, \"delta_pct\": -9.22, \"vs_baseline\": -0.31, \"fmax_mhz\": 118.96, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4219411, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10302, \"ff\": 1935, \"seeds\": [121.02, 118.96, 103.07], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T20:29:45.722231Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 2, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r2s2 (regression, -9.22%): A 16-entry BHT indexed only by `pc[5:2]` aliases CoreMark conditional branches, and weak-taken reset can turn the tuned static forward-not-taken behavior into costly early mispredictions, so tiny dynamic predictors need an aliasing-aware initialization and benchmark profile check.\"}\n10:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r3s2\", \"title\": \"Add a compact return-address stack predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The successful static predictor removes most backward-loop and direct-JAL\\nredirects, but JALR returns remain unpredicted and still pay the EX resolve\\npenalty on every function return. CoreMark contains frequent call/return\\ntraffic, while the prior 16-entry BHT showed that a general PC-indexed table\\ncan hurt both accuracy through aliasing and Fmax through added IF logic.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The successful static predictor removes most backward-loop and direct-JAL\\nredirects, but JALR returns remain unpredicted and still pay the EX resolve\\npenalty on every function return. CoreMark contains frequent call/return\\ntraffic, while the prior 16-entry BHT showed that a general PC-indexed table\\ncan hurt both accuracy through aliasing and Fmax through added IF logic.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a small, low-associativity return-address stack (RAS) in IF for JALR\\ninstructions whose source is x1 or x5 and whose destination is x0. Predict\\nthe top stack entry as the next PC, while retaining the existing static\\nbackward-branch and direct-JAL predictions for other control flow. Update\\nthe RAS from resolved EX calls and returns, pushing pc+4 for link-register\\nJAL/JALR calls and popping on returns; use the existing prediction metadata\\nand next-PC comparison so a cold or imperfect RAS recovers through the\\ncurrent redirect path. A 4-entry stack should cover CoreMark's shallow call\\ndepth with substantially less tag-compare and aliasing cost than a BHT/BTB.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a compact return-address stack, recognize return-form JALR opcodes, and select the stack top as their predicted target while preserving the existing static branch/JAL predictor.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire resolved call/return classification and link addresses from EX into IF so RAS updates occur on the architectural control-flow event rather than arbitrary fetch aliases.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose precise JAL/JALR call and return update signals, including the resolved link address, without changing redirect, trap, or RVFI behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a compact return-address stack, recognize return-form JALR opcodes, and select the stack top as their predicted target while preserving the existing static branch/JAL predictor.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire resolved call/return classification and link addresses from EX into IF so RAS updates occur on the architectural control-flow event rather than arbitrary fetch aliases.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose precise JAL/JALR call and return update signals, including the resolved link address, without changing redirect, trap, or RVFI behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 266.64, \"delta_pct\": -14.14, \"vs_baseline\": -5.72, \"fmax_mhz\": 113.21, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4245805, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10460, \"ff\": 2032, \"seeds\": [116.74, 110.53, 113.21], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T20:58:03.456890Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 3, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r3s2 (regression, -14.14%): Even a four-entry RAS can regress CoreMark when its combinational 4-way `ras_top` mux and return-form decode sit directly on the IF next-PC path, so return-prediction savings must be weighed against fetch timing before adding predictor state.\"}\n13:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r4s2\", \"title\": \"Add a tagged loop-exit predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The successful static predictor already removes most taken backward-branch\\nredirects, but it predicts the final iteration of every loop as taken and\\npays an EX redirect when the loop exits. A general 16-entry BHT regressed\\nbecause of aliasing and weak-taken startup behavior, while a RAS regressed\\nFmax by adding a wide IF-stage mux. CoreMark's repeated counted loops make a\\nspecialized, low-aliasing loop predictor a better targeted opportunity.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The successful static predictor already removes most taken backward-branch\\nredirects, but it predicts the final iteration of every loop as taken and\\npays an EX redirect when the loop exits. A general 16-entry BHT regressed\\nbecause of aliasing and weak-taken startup behavior, while a RAS regressed\\nFmax by adding a wide IF-stage mux. CoreMark's repeated counted loops make a\\nspecialized, low-aliasing loop predictor a better targeted opportunity.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a very small tagged loop predictor for backward conditional branches.\\nKeep the current static backward-taken prediction on a cold or tag-mismatch\\nlookup, then learn a branch's repeated taken sequence and expected exit so a\\nmatching loop PC can predict not-taken on its final iteration. Use exact PC\\ntags and a compact remaining-iterations/confidence state rather than a\\nbroadly aliased BHT, and update entries only from resolved EX branches.\\nCarry the existing prediction metadata and retain the current redirect-on-\\nmismatch recovery, so wrong or changing trip counts remain architecturally\\nharmless while common CoreMark loop exits avoid an extra flush.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny exact-tag loop predictor that overrides the existing backward-taken heuristic only for learned loop exits, with a static-prediction fallback and a narrow lookup path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the resolved backward conditional-branch PC and taken/not-taken outcome as a precise loop-predictor update event without changing redirect or RVFI behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the EX loop-branch update event into IF and preserve prediction metadata, bus-stall handling, and the existing single-channel RVFI contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny exact-tag loop predictor that overrides the existing backward-taken heuristic only for learned loop exits, with a static-prediction fallback and a narrow lookup path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the resolved backward conditional-branch PC and taken/not-taken outcome as a precise loop-predictor update event without changing redirect or RVFI behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the EX loop-branch update event into IF and preserve prediction metadata, bus-stall handling, and the existing single-channel RVFI contract.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 244.72, \"delta_pct\": -22.88, \"vs_baseline\": -13.47, \"fmax_mhz\": 104.48, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4269318, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 13301, \"ff\": 3141, \"seeds\": [104.48, 100.13, 104.93], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T21:20:20.478409Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 4, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r4s2 (regression, -22.88%): A tagged loop predictor that adds IF-stage tag/state lookup to suppress only final-iteration backward-branch redirects can cost more fetch performance than the occasional exit flush it removes, even when exact tags avoid BHT aliasing.\"}\n16:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r5s2\", \"title\": \"Add a tiny exact-tag return target cache\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The existing static predictor removes most backward-loop and direct-JAL\\nredirects, but indirect JALR returns still resolve in EX and pay a flush.\\nThe prior BHT regressed from aliasing and the four-entry RAS regressed from\\nits IF-stage multiway mux. A very small exact-tag structure can target only\\nrepeated return sites while keeping the fetch lookup narrow.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The existing static predictor removes most backward-loop and direct-JAL\\nredirects, but indirect JALR returns still resolve in EX and pay a flush.\\nThe prior BHT regressed from aliasing and the four-entry RAS regressed from\\nits IF-stage multiway mux. A very small exact-tag structure can target only\\nrepeated return sites while keeping the fetch lookup narrow.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a two-entry direct-mapped return-target cache indexed by one PC bit and\\ntagged with the full JALR PC. In IF, recognize only return-form JALR\\ninstructions (rd=x0 and rs1=x1 or x5); on an exact valid-tag hit, predict\\nthe cached target, otherwise retain the current sequential prediction.\\nUpdate the selected entry only when that return resolves in EX, carrying the\\nexisting prediction metadata so the normal mismatch redirect recovers from\\ncold entries and collisions. This should remove recurring JALR return\\nbubbles with less timing and state cost than a stack or general BTB, while\\nexact tags make an alias a harmless miss rather than a wrong-path fetch.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the two-entry exact-tag return-target lookup on the existing IF prediction path, selecting a cached target only for recognized return-form JALR instructions and falling back to the current static prediction otherwise.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose a precise resolved-return update event containing the JALR PC and aligned resolved target, without changing redirect, trap, or RVFI behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the EX return-target update event into IF and preserve prediction metadata, bus-stall handling, and the single-channel RVFI contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the two-entry exact-tag return-target lookup on the existing IF prediction path, selecting a cached target only for recognized return-form JALR instructions and falling back to the current static prediction otherwise.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose a precise resolved-return update event containing the JALR PC and aligned resolved target, without changing redirect, trap, or RVFI behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the EX return-target update event into IF and preserve prediction metadata, bus-stall handling, and the single-channel RVFI contract.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 249.03, \"delta_pct\": -21.52, \"vs_baseline\": -11.95, \"fmax_mhz\": 105.82, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4249209, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10910, \"ff\": 1997, \"seeds\": [105.33, 105.82, 107.61], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T21:32:35.438089Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 5}\n19:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r6s2\", \"title\": \"Shadow-link return predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The existing static predictor already covers backward CoreMark loops and\\ndirect JALs, leaving canonical JALR returns as the main recurring control\\nflow penalty. Prior BHT, loop-table, RAS, and tagged return-cache attempts\\neither aliased or placed expensive lookup and muxing on the IF critical\\npath. A predictor based directly on the architectural link registers can\\ntarget the same return pattern with substantially less state and timing\\noverhead.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The existing static predictor already covers backward CoreMark loops and\\ndirect JALs, leaving canonical JALR returns as the main recurring control\\nflow penalty. Prior BHT, loop-table, RAS, and tagged return-cache attempts\\neither aliased or placed expensive lookup and muxing on the IF critical\\npath. A predictor based directly on the architectural link registers can\\ntarget the same return pattern with substantially less state and timing\\noverhead.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add reset-valid shadow registers for x1 and x5, updated at writeback from\\nthe ordinary architectural write stream. In IF, when the fetched\\ninstruction is the canonical return-form JALR (rd=x0, funct3=0, rs1=x1 or\\nx5), use the corresponding shadow link value plus the decoded immediate as\\nthe predicted target; otherwise retain the current backward-branch and\\ndirect-JAL predictor. Carry the existing prediction metadata unchanged so\\nEX still resolves every return and redirects only on a mismatch. This\\nremoves repeated return bubbles without a tag compare, BHT aliasing, RAS\\nstack mux, or multi-entry target-table lookup; stale or nonstandard link\\nvalues remain harmless because the existing precise redirect recovery\\nremains authoritative.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add two valid shadow link registers and a narrow canonical-return JALR prediction path that uses x1/x5 plus the decoded immediate, while preserving existing static predictions and redirect fallback.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect the writeback architectural write-enable, destination, and data to IF so the shadow link registers track committed x1/x5 values without changing the external IO or RVFI contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add two valid shadow link registers and a narrow canonical-return JALR prediction path that uses x1/x5 plus the decoded immediate, while preserving existing static predictions and redirect fallback.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect the writeback architectural write-enable, destination, and data to IF so the shadow link registers track committed x1/x5 values without changing the external IO or RVFI contract.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 375.45, \"delta_pct\": -5.28, \"vs_baseline\": 32.75, \"fmax_mhz\": 161.92, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4312687, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10577, \"ff\": 2144, \"seeds\": [161.79, 161.92, 173.64], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T21:57:51.602940Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r6s2 (regression, -5.28%): A writeback-fed x1/x5 shadow predictor can lose CoreMark throughput when return decode, valid compares, and a 32-bit link-plus-immediate adder enter the IF next-PC cone, so return-bubble savings must be weighed against fetch timing and stale-link mispredict redirects.\"}\n22:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r7s2\", \"title\": \"Selective gshare forward-branch predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current static predictor is effective for CoreMark's backward loops and\\ndirect JALs, but it leaves every forward conditional branch not-taken. The\\nearlier PC-only 16-entry BHT regressed because it aliased branch sites and\\nused a harmful weak-taken startup bias, while larger tagged predictors hurt\\nthe IF timing path. A predictor that targets only the remaining forward\\nbranches can add useful direction information without disturbing the proven\\nloop prediction policy.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current static predictor is effective for CoreMark's backward loops and\\ndirect JALs, but it leaves every forward conditional branch not-taken. The\\nearlier PC-only 16-entry BHT regressed because it aliased branch sites and\\nused a harmful weak-taken startup bias, while larger tagged predictors hurt\\nthe IF timing path. A predictor that targets only the remaining forward\\nbranches can add useful direction information without disturbing the proven\\nloop prediction policy.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a small 32-entry, 2-bit gshare direction table for forward conditional\\nbranches. Index the table with a low PC slice XORed with a short global\\nconditional-branch history, initialize counters weakly not-taken, and update\\nthe counter from the precise EX branch outcome. Use the table only when the\\nbranch immediate is forward; retain the existing static backward-taken and\\ndirect-JAL predictions for all other control flow. Carry the existing\\nprediction metadata and redirect on a resolved next-PC mismatch, so cold\\nentries and history aliasing recover precisely without changing RVFI or\\narchitectural behavior. The XOR history should separate recurring CoreMark\\nbranch contexts better than the failed PC-only BHT while adding only a small\\ncounter array and narrow update state.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the small gshare history/counter state, use it only to choose taken predictions for forward conditional branches, preserve the existing backward-branch and direct-JAL static cases, and update state from resolved branches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose a precise conditional-branch update event containing the resolved branch PC, direction, and validity while leaving redirect, trap, and RVFI next-PC behavior unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the EX branch-resolution update event into the IF predictor without changing the external bus or single-channel RVFI contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the small gshare history/counter state, use it only to choose taken predictions for forward conditional branches, preserve the existing backward-branch and direct-JAL static cases, and update state from resolved branches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose a precise conditional-branch update event containing the resolved branch PC, direction, and validity while leaving redirect, trap, and RVFI next-PC behavior unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the EX branch-resolution update event into the IF predictor without changing the external bus or single-channel RVFI contract.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 403.25, \"delta_pct\": 1.74, \"vs_baseline\": 42.58, \"fmax_mhz\": 174.67, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4331511, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10400, \"ff\": 2145, \"seeds\": [184.77, 164.07, 174.67], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T22:18:02.863966Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 7, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r7s2 (regression, +1.74%): Even a weakly-not-taken, forward-only 32-entry gshare can regress CoreMark when the combinational `forward_bht[prediction_index][1]` lookup and global-history update add IF-path/state cost that the benchmark's relatively few useful forward-taken predictions do not repay.\"}\n25:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r8s2\", \"title\": \"Narrow zero-offset return predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The proven static predictor already removes most backward-loop and direct-JAL\\nredirects. Broader return predictors have regressed because their IF logic\\nadded a return decode, validity compares, target arithmetic, or multiway\\nlookup to the fetch critical path. CoreMark's common ABI return form is the\\ncanonical zero-offset JALR through x1, so a narrower predictor can target the\\nrecurring penalty while avoiding the expensive general case.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The proven static predictor already removes most backward-loop and direct-JAL\\nredirects. Broader return predictors have regressed because their IF logic\\nadded a return decode, validity compares, target arithmetic, or multiway\\nlookup to the fetch critical path. CoreMark's common ABI return form is the\\ncanonical zero-offset JALR through x1, so a narrower predictor can target the\\nrecurring penalty while avoiding the expensive general case.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Track only the committed value of x1 in one valid shadow register and predict\\nonly `jalr x0, 0(x1)` in IF. The prediction target is the shadow value itself,\\nwith no link-plus-immediate adder, tag array, history table, or x5 selection\\non the fetch path. Update the shadow from the existing writeback stream and\\ncarry the existing prediction metadata so EX remains authoritative and\\nredirects on a cold, stale, or noncanonical prediction. This should recover\\nrepeated ABI return bubbles at substantially lower Fmax risk than the prior\\ngeneral x1/x5 shadow predictor.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a single valid x1 shadow target and predict only canonical zero-offset jalr x0,0(x1), preserving the existing static branch and direct-JAL predictions and precise redirect fallback.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Feed the committed writeback destination/data into IF so the x1 shadow tracks architectural state without changing the external buses or RVFI contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a single valid x1 shadow target and predict only canonical zero-offset jalr x0,0(x1), preserving the existing static branch and direct-JAL predictions and precise redirect fallback.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Feed the committed writeback destination/data into IF so the x1 shadow tracks architectural state without changing the external buses or RVFI contract.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 391.01, \"delta_pct\": -18.69, \"vs_baseline\": 38.25, \"fmax_mhz\": 168.63, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4312687, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10162, \"ff\": 2105, \"seeds\": [168.63, 175.56, 167.64], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T22:37:24.834917Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r8s2 (regression, -18.69%): Even a one-entry committed x1 shadow that recognizes only `jalr x0, 0(x1)` can regress CoreMark when IF adds canonical-return decode and validity gating to the next-PC cone, so narrowing target arithmetic does not remove the critical-path cost of return prediction.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
