:# rtl/ legitimately has multiple top modules. Drop this once phase 2 is in.\nMakefile:98:\t  verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+$(RTL_DIR) \\\nMakefile:121:\tbash formal/run_all.sh formal/checks.cfg\nMakefile:129:\tbash formal/run_all.sh formal/checks-deep.cfg\nformal/run_all.sh:10:# Usage: bash formal/run_all.sh [checks-cfg-path]\nformal/run_all.sh:20:# invoking `bash formal/run_all.sh` directly therefore get the\nformal/run_all.sh:25:  echo \"ERROR: formal/run_all.sh requires RTL_DIR and CORE_NAME env vars.\" >&2\nformal/run_all.sh:26:  echo \"  Example: RTL_DIR=cores/v1/rtl CORE_NAME=v1 bash formal/run_all.sh formal/checks.cfg\" >&2\nformal/run_all.sh:38:# because the agent invoked `bash formal/run_all.sh` 6+ times in quick\nformal/run_all.sh:67:        echo \"[run_all.sh] auto-detected nret=1 from $CORE_YAML; using wrapper_si.sv + checks_si.cfg\"\nformal/run_all.sh:96:# Bounds disk growth from long runs (an agent that invokes run_all.sh\nformal/run_all.sh:170:# cores; without -k make stops on first error and 95+ checks never run,\ntest/_helpers.py:3:Constants mirror rtl/core_pkg.sv. If a localparam there changes, change\ntest/_helpers.py:14:# ── ALU encodings (rtl/core_pkg.sv) ────────────────────────────────────────\ntest/_helpers.py:51:def run_cocotb(toplevel: str, sources: list[str], test_module: str) -> None:\ntest/_helpers.py:57:    sim = os.environ.get(\"SIM\", \"verilator\")\ntest/_helpers.py:59:    build_dir = SIM_BUILD / toplevel\ntest/_helpers.py:63:        hdl_toplevel=toplevel,\ntest/_helpers.py:69:        hdl_toplevel=toplevel,\nfpga/scripts/synth.tcl:42:synth_gowin -top core_bench -json $gen_dir/synth.json\ncores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv:1:// rtl/id_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv:66:  // are also wired to the hazard unit at top level for load-use detection.\ntest/cosim/reference.py:6:Trap policy (matches rtl/decoder.sv default-illegal + rtl/ex_stage.sv +\ntest/cosim/reference.py:7:rtl/mem_stage.sv misalign traps):\ntest/cosi