{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"The current core is single-retire (`nret: 1`), so the implementation only needs to preserve channel 0; there is no hidden channel-1 wiring to maintain. The existing memory stage is a single EX/MEM-to-MEM/WB path, and its stall logic currently freezes the whole backend on a non-ready memory operation. I’m checking the exact cosim and pipeline expectations now so the added response latency does not create duplicate stores or stale forwarding."}}
